{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_13","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '1,230p' B-17-Cross-Channel-Chaos-B-17-Bomber-gpt-6.1-sol-ultra-20261106-043517/vendor/engine/src/starter3d/60-flight.js\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_13","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '1,230p' B-17-Cross-Channel-Chaos-B-17-Bomber-gpt-6.1-sol-ultra-20261106-043517/vendor/engine/src/starter3d/60-flight.js\"","aggregated_output":"/* =====================================================================================\n * SLICE 6  FLIGHT  (Star Fox 64, Panzer Dragoon).\n * A stage on rails: out over the sea between rock islands, fighters coming at you in waves, rings to fly through, then\n * over the coast and the enemy's base (turrets on the plateau, masts to weave between, fighters taking off), and into a\n * bay where their flagship waits: there the rails end and you fly free round it, its four engines first, then its core.\n * J (or Space, a click) fires the twin lasers; hold it to charge: the reticle locks on what is ahead, let go and the\n * charged shot flies to it. K (or Q) barrel-rolls toward the stick: a roll turns shots aside. Shift boosts, X brakes\n * (the meter refills). The stick moves the ship about the screen (on rails) or turns it (free). Silver rings mend the\n * shield, a gold one more. Your wingman, KESTREL, calls on the radio and needs a hand once. Settings: Invert flight.\n * THE 3D: world.flyer (on rails along an E.Path, the ship moving in a window across it; then free within the bay's\n * bounds), f.seek (the charged shot's lock), barrel rolls (f.rolling), the 'behind' camera (behind the rail's point,\n * then the ship), a terrain (the sea, islands, the coast, the base's plateau, mountains round the bay), Dialog's radio.\n * FLIGHT.run(n): a scripted flight's hash (the proof); FLIGHT.bot(): flies the stage and beats the flagship\n * ===================================================================================== */\nconst FLIGHT = (() => {\n  const PI = Math.PI, U = 16;\n  const KEYS = Object.assign({}, W3.INPUT, { fire: ['KeyJ', 'Space', 'Mouse0', 'Pad0'], roll: ['KeyK', 'KeyQ', 'Pad4', 'Pad5'], boost: ['ShiftLeft', 'ShiftRight', 'KeyL', 'Pad1'], brake: ['KeyX', 'KeyH', 'Pad2'] });\n  for (const k of ['attack', 'dash', 'skill', 'jump', 'lock']) delete KEYS[k];\n  const TOUCH = ['brake', 'boost', 'roll', 'fire'], TOUCH_LABELS = { fire: 'FIRE', roll: 'ROLL', boost: 'BOOST', brake: 'BRAKE' };\n  const INVERT = { key: 'invertFlight', label: 'Invert flight', group: 'Game', value: false, help: 'Up on the stick dives, as a pilot\\'s stick does.' };\n\n  /* ---- THE WORLD: a terrain. The sea (height 0), rock islands by the rail, the coast (a diagonal line: x + y = 30,500),\n   * the base's plateau beyond it, mountains further in, and a bay carved out of them for the flagship ---- */\n  const BAY = [21000, 14500], ISLES = [[9000, 11400, 450, 300], [9000, 9560, 450, 260], [12100, 12950, 420, 340], [13150, 11700, 420, 300], [6200, 9100, 380, 220], [5200, 10900, 300, 160]];\n  const vn = (x, y) => { const xi = Math.floor(x), yi = Math.floor(y), fx = x - xi, fy = y - yi, sx = fx * fx * (3 - 2 * fx), sy = fy * fy * (3 - 2 * fy), a = E.hash2(xi, yi), b = E.hash2(xi + 1, yi), c = E.hash2(xi, yi + 1), d = E.hash2(xi + 1, yi + 1); return a + (b - a) * sx + (c - a) * sy + (a - b - c + d) * sx * sy; };\n  const fbm = (x, y) => vn(x, y) * .55 + vn(x * 2.1 + 5, y * 2.1 + 9) * .3 + vn(x * 4.3 + 1, y * 4.3 + 3) * .15, sstep = (a, b, v) => { const k = clamp((v - a) / (b - a), 0, 1); return k * k * (3 - 2 * k); };\n  function height(x, y) {\n    const inland = (x + y - 30500) / 1500; let h = 0;\n    if (inland > 0) h = Math.min(1, inland * 1.6) * 48 + sstep(2.5, 4, inland) * fbm(x / 1700, y / 1700) * 900;   // the plateau, then mountains\n    const db = Math.hypot(x - BAY[0], y - BAY[1]); if (db < 3000) h *= sstep(2200, 3000, db);   // the bay: sea inside the mountains\n    for (const [cx, cy, r, H] of ISLES) { const d2 = ((x - cx) ** 2 + (y - cy) ** 2) / (r * r); if (d2 < 1) h = Math.max(h, H * (1 - d2) ** .6 * (.75 + .5 * vn(x / 80, y / 80))); }\n    return h;\n  }\n  const inBase = (x, y) => { const k = x + y - 30500; return k > 600 && k < 3600 && Math.hypot(x - BAY[0], y - BAY[1]) > 3000; };\n  function color(x, y, z, nz, out) {\n    const n = E.hash2(x >> 5, y >> 5);\n    if (z < 1.5) { const w = vn(x / 260, y / 260); out[0] = 30 + w * 20 + n * 8; out[1] = 90 + w * 40 + n * 10; out[2] = 170 + w * 40; return out; }   // the sea\n    if (z < 9) { out[0] = 214 + n * 20; out[1] = 196 + n * 16; out[2] = 140; return out; }   // sand\n    if (inBase(x, y) && z < 70) { const g = ((x >> 7) + (y >> 7)) & 1 ? 128 : 118; out[0] = g + n * 10; out[1] = g + 2 + n * 10; out[2] = g + 8 + n * 10; return out; }   // the base: concrete\n    const w = vn(x / 400, y / 400); out[0] = 70 + w * 40 + n * 12; out[1] = 128 + w * 30 + n * 12; out[2] = 60 + w * 10; return out;   // grass\n  }\n\n  /* ---- THE RAIL: the path the stage rides (heights in it), and what is set along it, by distance ---- */\n  const RAIL = new E.Path([[3000, 9000, 170], [7000, 10000, 150], [9000, 10480, 140], [11000, 11000, 130], [14000, 13500, 150], [16500, 15800, 150], [18500, 15200, 190], [21000, 14500, 240]], { smooth: 'catmull' });\n  const RL = RAIL.length, SPEED = 380, WIN = [320, 180];   // the rail's pace, the window the ship moves in across it\n  const BOUNDS = [BAY[0] - 2600, BAY[1] - 2600, 70, BAY[0] + 2600, BAY[1] + 2600, 1100];\n  // the waves: at rail distance d, fighters [pattern, ox, oy, k]; rings; the turrets and masts of the base; radio calls\n  const WAVES = [\n    [900, 'v', 0, 30, 5], [2600, 'cross', -1, 10, 4], [4300, 'v', 80, -20, 5], [7600, 'chase', 0, 0, 1], [9200, 'behind', 0, 40, 5],\n    [11200, 'cross', 1, 40, 4], [13400, 'rise', 0, 0, 6], [15400, 'v', -60, 30, 5]];\n  const RINGS = [[3500, 0, 0, 's'], [3720, 60, 20, 's'], [3940, 120, 30, 's'], [4160, 60, 10, 's'], [5800, -100, -30, 'g'], [10200, 0, 50, 's'], [12600, -80, 0, 's'], [16400, 60, 40, 'g']];\n  const TURRETS = Array.from({ length: 10 }, (_, k) => [12900 + k * 420, k % 2 ? 1 : -1, 140 + (k * 37) % 110]);\n  const MASTS = Array.from({ length: 8 }, (_, k) => [13300 + k * 480, ((k * 53) % 9 - 4) * 30]);\n  const CALLS = [[150, 'KESTREL', 'Stay with me! Their base is past the islands.'], [800, 'KESTREL', 'Fighters, dead ahead!'], [3300, 'KESTREL', 'Rings! Fly through them to mend your shield.'],\n    [7500, 'KESTREL', 'I\\'ve got one on my tail! Get it off me!'], [9100, 'KESTREL', 'More behind us! Hold your fire till they pass.'], [12400, 'KESTREL', 'Turrets on the plateau. Roll to turn their shots aside!'],\n    [13300, 'KESTREL', 'Weave through those masts!'], [RL - 900, 'KESTREL', 'That\\'s their flagship in the bay. Hit the engines first!']];\n\n  let world, ship, rnd = Math.random, mode = 'play', t = 0, scripted = false, ended = 0, endT = 0, freed = false, boss = null;\n  let foes = [], shots = [], lasers = [], rings = [], turrets = [], masts = [], wave = 0, call = 0, score = 0, hits = 0, lock = null;\n  const S = { shield: 100, boost: 1, charge: 0, fireT: 0, hurtT: 0, held: false, wing: 100, wingT: 0, saved: null };\n  const camT = { x: 0, y: 0, z: 0, yaw: 0, pitch: 0, roll: 0 };   // the camera's target: the rail's point, drawn a little after the ship\n  const talk = new E.Dialog(game, { lines: 2, place: 'top', border: '#8ad0ff' });\n  const PILOT = new E.Humanoid({ hair: 'short', colors: { cloth: '#3a6ad8', pants: '#2a3a5a', hair: '#e8c060', skin: '#e8b890' } });\n  const radio = (name, line) => { if (!scripted) talk.say(line, { name, auto: 2.6, modal: false, alpha: .75, portrait: PILOT, portraitOpts: { zoom: 3, turn: .4 } }); };\n  const SONG = { bpm: 140, steps: 4, tracks: [\n    { wave: 'square', vol: .055, notes: 'A4 . C5 E5 . A5 . G5 | F5 . E5 C5 . D5 . E5 | A4 . C5 E5 . A5 . B5 | C6 . B5 G5 . E5 . . ' },\n    { wave: 'triangle', vol: .26, notes: 'A2 A2 E3 A2 A2 E3 A2 G2 | F2 F2 C3 F2 G2 G2 D3 G2 | A2 A2 E3 A2 A2 E3 A2 G2 | F2 F2 G2 G2 A2 A2 A2 A2' },\n    { wave: 'drums', vol: .07, notes: 'k . h . s . h k k . h . s . h h' }] };\n\n  BOOT.push(['The sea and the base', () => {\n    world = new W3(game, { terrain: { size: 32768, cell: 64, chunk: 32, height, color, far: 9000, physics: 0, detail: 1.1, rock: { colors: ['#8a8478', '#a09a8c', '#6e685e', '#b4ad9c'], band: 40, slope: [.4, .6] } },\n      sky: { top: '#3a78d8', horizon: '#d8ecff', ground: '#3a6aa8', sun: '#fff4d0', haze: .25 }, fog: { color: '#cfe4f8', near: 2600, far: 8800 },\n      ambient: ['#d8e4ff', '#5a7aa0', 2], sun: { color: '#fff4dc', intensity: 2.8, dir: [-.4, .5, -.7], area: 900 }, torchLights: 0, glowLights: 6, camera: { mode: 'behind', far: 12000 }, onDraw });\n    reset(1);\n  }]);\n\n  /** the stage from the start (seed: the fighters' choices) */\n  function reset(seed = 1) {\n    world.reset(); rnd = E.rng(seed); t = 0; ended = 0; endT = 0; freed = false; wave = 0; call = 0; score = 0; hits = 0; lock = null;\n    Object.assign(S, { shield: 100, boost: 1, charge: 0, fireT: 0, hurtT: 0, held: false, wing: 100, wingT: 0, saved: null });\n    ship = world.flyer({ rail: { path: RAIL, speed: SPEED, w: WIN[0], h: WIN[1], slide: 240 }, speed: SPEED, min: 230, max: 640, turn: 1.4, climb: 1.2, bank: .7, low: 18, invert: !!game.settings[INVERT.key] });\n    foes = []; shots = []; lasers = [];\n    rings = RINGS.map(([d, ox, oy, k]) => Object.assign(frameAt(d, ox, oy), { d, kind: k, got: false }));\n    turrets = TURRETS.map(([d, side, off]) => { const p = RAIL.at(d), x = p.x - Math.sin(p.angle) * side * off, y = p.y + Math.cos(p.angle) * side * off; return { x, y, z: height(x, y), hp: 3, cool: 1 + rnd(), yaw: 0, alive: true, type: 'turret', r: 18 }; });\n    masts = MASTS.map(([d, ox]) => { const q = frameAt(d, ox, 0); return { x: q.x, y: q.y, z: height(q.x, q.y), top: height(q.x, q.y) + 210 }; });\n    boss = { x: BAY[0] + 1200, y: BAY[1], z: 280, yaw: PI / 2, a: 0, alive: true, hp: 30, core: false, parts: [[60, -70, 0], [60, 70, 0], [-60, -90, -6], [-60, 90, -6]].map(o => ({ o, hp: 10, alive: true })), cool: 3, mcool: 6, t: 0, dying: 0 };\n    camT.x = ship.x; camT.y = ship.y; camT.z = ship.z;\n    world.camera.set('behind'); world.camera.follow(camT); Object.assign(world.camera.behind, { dist: 120, height: 26, ahead: 260, lag: 7, fov: 70, roll: .3 });\n  }\n  /** a point in the rail's frame: d along it, ox right of it, oy up */\n  function frameAt(d, ox, oy) { const p = RAIL.at(clamp(d, 0, RL)); return { x: p.x - Math.sin(p.angle) * ox, y: p.y + Math.cos(p.angle) * ox, z: p.z + oy, yaw: p.angle }; }\n\n  /* ---- the fighters: each rides the rail's frame by its pattern (d along it, ox, oy across it), or chases ---- */\n  function spawn([d0, kind, a, b, n]) {\n    for (let i = 0; i < n; i++) {\n      const f = { type: 'fighter', kind, hp: 2, alive: true, t: -i * .25, cool: 1.2 + rnd() * 1.4, r: 16, x: 0, y: 0, z: 0, yaw: 0, roll: 0 };\n      if (kind === 'v') Object.assign(f, { d: d0 + 1900 + Math.abs(i - (n - 1) / 2) * 90, ox: a + (i - (n - 1) / 2) * 70, oy: b + Math.abs(i - (n - 1) / 2) * 15, vd: -320 });\n      else if (kind === 'cross') Object.assign(f, { d: d0 + 760 + i * 60, ox: -a * 600, oy: b + i * 25, vd: -100, vx: a * 330 });\n      else if (kind === 'behind') Object.assign(f, { d: d0 - 300 - i * 60, ox: (i - 2) * 70, oy: b + 60, vd: 620 });\n      else if (kind === 'rise') Object.assign(f, { d: d0 + 900 + i * 120, ox: (i % 2 ? 1 : -1) * (60 + i * 25), oy: -200, vd: -150, vy: 140 });   // (up from the base's runways)\n      else if (kind === 'chase') Object.assign(f, { d: d0 + 240, ox: 150, oy: 30, vd: 0, hp: 3, chase: true });\n      foes.push(f);\n    }\n  }\n  function moveFoe(f, dt) {\n    f.t += dt; if (f.t < 0) { place(f); return; }\n    f.d += (SPEED + f.vd) * dt;\n    if (f.kind === 'v') { f.oy += Math.sin(f.t * 2) * 20 * dt; if (f.d < ship.d + 300) f.vd = -60; }   // (they come at you, then hang ahead)\n    if (f.kind === 'cross') f.ox += f.vx * dt;\n    if (f.kind === 'behind' && f.d > ship.d + 600) f.vd = 20;   // (past you, they turn to hold ahead)\n    if (f.kind === 'rise') { f.oy = Math.min(60, f.oy + f.vy * dt); }\n    if (f.chase) { const k = wingAt(); f.ox = k.ox + Math.sin(f.t * 1.7) * 30; f.oy = k.oy + Math.cos(f.t * 2.3) * 15; f.d = ship.d + 240; }   // (on KESTREL's tail, ahead of you)\n    place(f);\n    if (f.d < ship.d - 400 || Math.abs(f.ox) > 900 || f.t > 40) f.alive = false, f.gone = true;   // (behind you, or off the screen: gone)\n  }\n  /** KESTREL, your wingman: where it flies in the rail's frame (ahead of you, weaving, while a fighter chases it) */\n  function wingAt() { const chased = foes.some(f => f.chase && f.alive), w = t; return { chased, d: ship.d + (chased ? 300 : 60), ox: (chased ? 90 : 150) + Math.sin(w * (chased ? 1.7 : .7)) * 30, oy: 30 + Math.sin(w * 1.1) * 15 }; }\n  function place(f) { const q = frameAt(f.d, f.ox, f.oy); f.x = q.x; f.y = q.y; f.z = q.z; f.yaw = q.yaw + (f.vd < 0 ? PI : 0); f.roll = Math.sin(f.t * 3) * .4 + (f.vx || 0) / 700; }\n\n  /* ---- shots: theirs (aimed at you, turned aside by a roll), your lasers and the charged shot ---- */\n  function fireAt(o, sp = 520, spread = 0) {\n    const dx = ship.x - o.x, dy = ship.y - o.y, dz = ship.z - o.z, d = Math.hypot(dx, dy, dz) || 1, a = spread * (rnd() - .5);\n    const c = Math.cos(a), s = Math.sin(a), vx = (dx * c - dy * s) / d, vy = (dx * s + dy * c) / d;\n    shots.push({ x: o.x, y: o.y, z: o.z, vx: vx * sp, vy: vy * sp, vz: dz / d * sp, t: 0, back: false }); if (!scripted) A.sfx('laser', { vol: .25 });\n  }\n  const nose = (k = 1) => { const cp = Math.cos(ship.pitch); return [Math.cos(ship.yaw) * cp * k, Math.sin(ship.yaw) * cp * k, Math.sin(ship.pitch) * k]; };\n  function laser() {\n    const f = nose(), r = [-Math.sin(ship.yaw), Math.cos(ship.yaw)], v = 2400 + ship.speed;\n    for (const s of [-1, 1]) lasers.push({ x: ship.x + r[0] * s * 9 + f[0] * 10, y: ship.y + r[1] * s * 9 + f[1] * 10, z: ship.z, vx: f[0] * v, vy: f[1] * v, vz: f[2] * v, t: 0, dmg: 1 });\n    if (!scripted) A.sfx('shoot', { vol: .35 });\n  }\n  function charged() {\n    const f = nose(); lasers.push({ x: ship.x + f[0] * 14, y: ship.y + f[1] * 14, z: ship.z, vx: f[0] * 1300, vy: f[1] * 1300, vz: f[2] * 1300, t: 0, dmg: 6, big: true, target: lock });\n    if (!scripted) A.sfx('powerup');\n  }\n  const targets = () => { const L = foes.filter(f => f.alive && f.t >= 0).concat(turrets.filter(q => q.alive)); if (freed && boss.alive) { for (const p of boss.parts) if (p.alive) L.push(partAt(p)); if (boss.core) L.push(coreAt()); } return L; };\n  function partAt(p) { const c = Math.cos(boss.yaw), s = Math.sin(boss.yaw); return Object.assign(p, { type: 'part', x: boss.x + p.o[0] * c - p.o[1] * s, y: boss.y + p.o[0] * s + p.o[1] * c, z: boss.z + p.o[2], r: 34 }); }\n  const CORE = { type: 'core', o: [0, 0, 16], r: 40, hp: 1, alive: true };\n  function coreAt() { return Object.assign(partAt(CORE), { type: 'core', alive: boss.alive && boss.core, hp: boss.hp }); }\n  function hurtFoe(q, dmg, x, y, z) {\n    P.sparks(x, y, z, 5, null, { color: '#ffd080' }); if (!scripted) A.sfx('hit', { vol: .4 });\n    if (q.type === 'core') { boss.hp -= dmg; if (boss.hp <= 0) { boss.alive = false; boss.dying = 3; score += 5000; hits += 10; } return; }\n    q.hp -= dmg; if (q.hp > 0) return;\n    q.alive = false; score += q.type === 'part' ? 1000 : q.type === 'turret' ? 300 : 100; hits++;\n    P.fire(q.x, q.y, q.z, 10, { size: 9, speed: 80 }); P.bits(q.x, q.y, q.z, 8, ['#5a5a6a', '#8a8a9a', '#ff9a3a']); game.shake(q.type === 'part' ? 5 : 2); if (!scripted) A.sfx('explode', { vol: .5 });\n    if (q.chase) radio('KESTREL', 'Thanks! I owe you one.');\n    if (q.type === 'part' && boss.parts.every(p => !p.alive)) { boss.core = true; radio('KESTREL', 'The core\\'s open! Now!'); }\n  }\n  function moveShots(dt) {\n    const L = targets();\n    for (const l of lasers) {\n      if (l.target && l.target.alive !== false) { const dx = l.target.x - l.x, dy = l.target.y - l.y, dz = l.target.z - l.z, d = Math.hypot(dx, dy, dz) || 1, sp = Math.hypot(l.vx, l.vy, l.vz), k = Math.min(1, dt * 7);\n        l.vx += (dx / d * sp - l.vx) * k; l.vy += (dy / d * sp - l.vy) * k; l.vz += (dz / d * sp - l.vz) * k; }\n      const x0 = l.x, y0 = l.y, z0 = l.z; l.x += l.vx * dt; l.y += l.vy * dt; l.z += l.vz * dt; l.t += dt;\n      for (const q of L) if (q.alive !== false && segHit(x0, y0, z0, l.x, l.y, l.z, q.x, q.y, q.z, q.r + (l.big ? 10 : 2))) { hurtFoe(q, l.dmg, l.x, l.y, l.z); l.t = 9; if (l.big) for (const o of L) if (o !== q && o.alive !== false && Math.hypot(o.x - l.x, o.y - l.y, o.z - l.z) < 90) hurtFoe(o, 2, o.x, o.y, o.z); break; }\n      if (l.z < height(l.x, l.y)) { if (l.big) P.fire(l.x, l.y, l.z, 6); l.t = 9; }\n    }\n    lasers = lasers.filter(l => l.t < (l.big ? 3 : .9));\n    for (const s of shots) {\n      const x0 = s.x, y0 = s.y, z0 = s.z; s.x += s.vx * dt; s.y += s.vy * dt; s.z += s.vz * dt; s.t += dt;\n      if (s.back) { for (const q of L) if (q.alive !== false && segHit(x0, y0, z0, s.x, s.y, s.z, q.x, q.y, q.z, q.r)) { hurtFoe(q, 2, s.x, s.y, s.z); s.t = 9; break; } continue; }\n      if (segHit(x0, y0, z0, s.x, s.y, s.z, ship.x, ship.y, ship.z, ship.rolling > 0 ? 26 : 11)) {\n        if (ship.rolling > 0) { s.vx *= -1.3; s.vy *= -1.3; s.vz *= -1.3; s.back = true; P.sparks(s.x, s.y, s.z, 4, null, { color: '#a0e0ff' }); if (!scripted) A.sfx('blip', { vol: .5 }); }   // (a roll turns it aside)\n        else { hurt(8); s.t = 9; }\n      }\n    }\n    shots = shots.filter(s => s.t < 3.5);\n  }\n  function segHit(x0, y0, z0, x1, y1, z1, cx, cy, cz, r) {   // (a step's segment against a ball: fast shots never pass through)\n    const dx = x1 - x0, dy = y1 - y0, dz = z1 - z0, L2 = dx * dx + dy * dy + dz * dz || 1, k = clamp(((cx - x0) * dx + (cy - y0) * dy + (cz - z0) * dz) / L2, 0, 1);\n    return Math.hypot(x0 + dx * k - cx, y0 + dy * k - cy, z0 + dz * k - cz) < r;\n  }\n  function hurt(n) { if (S.hurtT > 0 || ended) return; S.shield -= n; S.hurtT = .5; game.shake(3); game.flash('#ff3a2a'); if (!scripted) A.sfx('hurt'); if (S.shield <= 0) { S.shield = 0; end(-1); } }\n  function end(k) { if (ended) return; ended = k; endT = 0; if (k < 0) { P.fire(ship.x, ship.y, ship.z, 16, { size: 10 }); } }\n\n  /* ---- the flagship: it circles the bay, fires spreads from its engines and homing mines; its core opens when they burn ---- */\n  function moveBoss(dt) {\n    const B = boss; B.t += dt;\n    if (!B.alive) { B.dying -= dt; B.z -= 40 * dt; if ((world.n & 7) === 0) P.fire(B.x + (rnd() - .5) * 120, B.y + (rnd() - .5) * 120, B.z, 4, { size: 12 }); if (B.dying <= 0 && !ended) end(1); return; }\n    B.a += dt * .11; B.x = BAY[0] + Math.cos(B.a) * 1200; B.y = BAY[1] + Math.sin(B.a) * 1200; B.z = 280 + Math.sin(B.t * .5) * 60; B.yaw = B.a + PI / 2;\n    if (!freed) return;\n    B.cool -= dt; B.mcool -= dt; const near = Math.hypot(ship.x - B.x, ship.y - B.y) < 2400;\n    if (B.cool <= 0 && near) { B.cool = B.core ? 1.6 : 2.4; const from = B.parts.filter(p => p.alive).map(partAt)[0] || coreAt(); for (let k = 0; k < 5; k++) fireAt(from, 560, .5 + k * .1); }\n    if (B.mcool <= 0 && near) { B.mcool = 7; for (const s of [-1, 1]) foes.push({ type: 'mine', alive: true, hp: 1, r: 14, x: B.x, y: B.y + s * 60, z: B.z, t: 0, home: true }); }\n  }\n  function moveMine(m, dt) {\n    m.t += dt; const dx = ship.x - m.x, dy = ship.y - m.y, dz = ship.z - m.z, d = Math.hypot(dx, dy, dz) || 1, sp = 300;\n    m.x += dx / d * sp * dt; m.y += dy / d * sp * dt; m.z += dz / d * sp * dt;\n    if (d < 20) { m.alive = false; if (ship.rolling > 0) { P.sparks(m.x, m.y, m.z, 6, null, { color: '#a0e0ff' }); } else { hurt(12); P.fire(m.x, m.y, m.z, 8); } }\n    if (m.t > 9) m.alive = false;\n  }\n\n  /* ---- one step: the controls, the ship, the stage's script, the shots, the camera's target ---- */\n  const ctl = { steer: [0, 0], boost: false, brake: false, roll: 0, fire: false, down: a => game.input.down(a), pressed: a => game.input.pressed(a) };\n  function controls() {\n    const I = game.input, m = I.move(); ctl.steer[0] = m[0]; ctl.steer[1] = m[1];\n    ctl.boost = I.down('boost'); ctl.brake = I.down('brake'); ctl.roll = I.pressed('roll') ? (Math.sign(m[0]) || 1) : 0; ctl.fire = I.down('fire'); ctl.tap = I.pressed('fire');\n    return ctl;\n  }\n  function step(dt, c) {\n    t += dt; world.step(dt);\n    if (ended) { endT += dt; if (ended < 0) ship.z -= 60 * dt; for (const l of lasers) l.t += dt; return; }\n    if (S.hurtT > 0) S.hurtT -= dt;\n    // the boost meter: boost or brake while it lasts, then it refills\n    const use = (c.boost || c.brake) && S.boost > 0; S.boost = clamp(S.boost + (use ? -.45 : .25) * dt, 0, 1);\n    ship.update(dt, { steer: c.steer, boost: use && c.boost, brake: use && c.brake, roll: c.roll });\n    if (c.roll && !scripted) A.sfx('whoosh', { vol: .5 });\n    if (ship.hitGround) { if ((world.n & 7) === 0) { P.sparks(ship.x, ship.y, ship.z - 6, 3); hurt(4); } }\n    // fire: a tap shoots; held, it charges (a lock on what is ahead), let go, the charged shot flies\n    S.fireT -= dt;\n    if (c.fire) { S.charge = Math.min(1, S.charge + dt * 1.4); if (S.charge > .35) lock = ship.seek(targets(), { cone: .3, range: 1800 }) || lock; if (lock && lock.alive === false) lock = null; }\n    if (c.tap && S.fireT <= 0) { laser(); S.fireT = .12; }\n    if (!c.fire && S.held) { if (S.charge >= 1) charged(); S.charge = 0; lock = null; }\n    S.held = c.fire;\n    // the stage's script: waves, radio calls, the end of the rails\n    while (wave < WAVES.length && ship.d >= WAVES[wave][0]) spawn(WAVES[wave++]);\n    while (call < CALLS.length && ship.d >= CALLS[call][0]) { radio(CALLS[call][1], CALLS[call][2]); call++; }\n    if (!freed && ship.d >= RL - 20) { freed = true; ship.o.rail = null; ship.o.bounds = BOUNDS; ship.pitch = 0; foes = []; shots = []; if (!scripted) A.music(BOSS_SONG); radio('KESTREL', 'All range mode! Take it down!'); }\n    // the fighters, turrets and masts\n    for (const f of foes) if (f.alive) {\n      if (f.type === 'mine') { moveMine(f, dt); continue; }\n      moveFoe(f, dt); if (!f.alive || f.t < 0) continue;\n      f.cool -= dt; if (f.cool <= 0 && !f.chase && f.d > ship.d + 150) { f.cool = 1.8 + rnd() * 1.6; fireAt(f, 480, .15); }\n      if (Math.hypot(f.x - ship.x, f.y - ship.y, f.z - ship.z) < 22) { hurt(10); hurtFoe(f, 9, f.x, f.y, f.z); }\n      if (f.chase) { S.wingT += dt; if (S.wingT > 9) { f.alive = false; S.wing -= 40; radio('KESTREL', 'I\\'m hit! I\\'ll make it.'); } }\n    }\n    foes = foes.filter(f => f.alive);\n    for (const q of turrets) if (q.alive) {\n      const dx = ship.x - q.x, dy = ship.y - q.y, d = Math.hypot(dx, dy); q.yaw = Math.atan2(dy, dx);\n      q.cool -= dt; if (q.cool <= 0 && d < 1500 && !freed) { q.cool = 2 + rnd() * 1.2; fireAt({ x: q.x, y: q.y, z: q.z + 26 }, 460, .1); }\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_14","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"ls B-17-Cross-Channel-Chaos-B-17-Bomber-gpt-6.1-sol-ultra-20261106-043517/vendor/engine/dist/handoff && cat B-17-Cross-Channel-Chaos-B-17-Bomber-gpt-6.1-sol-ultra-20261106-043517/vendor/engine/package.json && sed -n '1,220p' B-17-Cross-Channel-Chaos-B-17-Bomber-gpt-6.1-sol-ultra-20261106-043517/vendor/engine/dist/handoff/README.md\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_14","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"ls B-17-Cross-Channel-Chaos-B-17-Bomber-gpt-6.1-sol-ultra-20261106-043517/vendor/engine/dist/handoff && cat B-17-Cross-Channel-Chaos-B-17-Bomber-gpt-6.1-sol-ultra-20261106-043517/vendor/engine/package.json && sed -n '1,220p' B-17-Cross-Channel-Chaos-B-17-Bomber-gpt-6.1-sol-ultra-20261106-043517/vendor/engine/dist/handoff/README.md\"","aggregated_output":"AI_GUIDE.md\nAPI-INDEX.md\nAPI.md\nREADME.md\ndocs\ngame\nindex.html\nkits\nmodules\nmy-3d2dge-agent.js\nmy-3d2dge.js\npackage.json\nsrc\ntools\n{\n  \"name\": \"my-3d2dge\",\n  \"version\": \"0.89.1\",\n  \"description\": \"my-3D2dge (My \\\"3D\\\" 2D Game Engine): a general-purpose retro-modern 2D game engine built for AI models. Port, remaster, reimagine and remix 8-bit to 64-bit era games in every classic view, from one self-contained HTML file.\",\n  \"type\": \"module\",\n  \"license\": \"MIT\",\n  \"main\": \"engine/my-3d2dge.js\",\n  \"repository\": { \"type\": \"git\", \"url\": \"https://github.com/michaelcrosato/my-3d2dge.git\" },\n  \"homepage\": \"https://github.com/michaelcrosato/my-3d2dge\",\n  \"keywords\": [\"game-engine\", \"pixel-art\", \"retro\", \"2d\", \"isometric\", \"platformer\", \"procedural-animation\", \"llm\", \"ai\"],\n  \"files\": [\"engine/my-3d2dge.js\", \"engine/my-3d2dge-agent.js\", \"engine/my-3d2dge-3d.js\", \"API.md\", \"AI_GUIDE.md\", \"dist/\"],\n  \"scripts\": {\n    \"build\": \"node tools/build.mjs\",\n    \"check\": \"node tools/check.mjs\",\n    \"version:check\": \"node tools/version.mjs --check\",\n    \"doctrine:check\": \"node tools/doctrine-check.mjs\",\n    \"stamp\": \"node tools/stamp.mjs\",\n    \"test\": \"node tools/test-run.mjs --all\",\n    \"test:changed\": \"node tools/test-run.mjs --changed\",\n    \"test:which\": \"node tools/test-run.mjs --list\",\n    \"test:agent\": \"node tools/agent-test.mjs\",\n    \"test:contract\": \"node tools/contract-test.mjs\",\n    \"test:standard\": \"node tools/standard-test.mjs\",\n    \"test:phone\": \"node tools/phone-test.mjs\",\n    \"test:kits\": \"node tools/kits-test.mjs\",\n    \"test:modules\": \"node tools/modules-test.mjs\",\n    \"test:motion\": \"node tools/motion-test.mjs\",\n    \"test:players\": \"node tools/players-test.mjs\",\n    \"test:fight\": \"node tools/fight-test.mjs\",\n    \"test:traversal\": \"node tools/traversal-test.mjs\",\n    \"test:views\": \"node tools/views-test.mjs\",\n    \"bench\": \"node tools/agent-bench.mjs\",\n    \"test:labs\": \"node tools/labs-test.mjs\",\n    \"test:assets\": \"node tools/assets-test.mjs\",\n    \"assets:sheet\": \"node tools/asset-sheet.mjs\",\n    \"assets:fetch\": \"node tools/asset-fetch.mjs\",\n    \"assets:import\": \"node tools/asset-import.mjs\",\n    \"assets:set\": \"node tools/asset-set.mjs\",\n    \"assets:find\": \"node tools/asset-find.mjs\",\n    \"test:stress\": \"node tools/stress-test.mjs\",\n    \"test:kit3d\": \"node tools/kit3d-test.mjs\",\n    \"test:determinism\": \"node tools/determinism-test.mjs\",\n    \"test:replay\": \"node tools/replay-test.mjs\",\n    \"replay\": \"node tools/replay.mjs\",\n    \"test:cross-engine\": \"node tools/cross-engine-math.cjs\",\n    \"vendor:3d\": \"node tools/vendor-3d.mjs\",\n    \"test:mocap\": \"node tools/mocap-test.mjs && node tools/ed-clips-test.mjs\",\n    \"mocap:import\": \"node tools/anim-import.mjs\",\n    \"mocap:set\": \"node tools/anim-set.mjs\",\n    \"mocap:sheet\": \"node tools/anim-sheet.mjs\",\n    \"mocap:cmu\": \"node tools/cmu.mjs\",\n    \"test:smoke\": \"node tools/ed-smoke.mjs\",\n    \"test:character\": \"node tools/ed-character-test.mjs\",\n    \"character:check\": \"node tools/character-check.mjs\",\n    \"character:sheet\": \"node tools/ed-sheet.mjs\",\n    \"character:balance\": \"node tools/ed-balance.mjs\",\n    \"new:character\": \"node tools/new-character.mjs\",\n    \"test:codex\": \"npm run build && node tools/ed-codex-test.mjs\",\n    \"showcase:codex\": \"node tools/ed-codex-showcase.mjs\"\n  },\n  \"devDependencies\": {\n    \"acorn\": \"^8.15.0\",\n    \"gpt-tokenizer\": \"^4.0.0\",\n    \"playwright\": \"^1.56.0\",\n    \"terser\": \"^5.51.2\"\n  }\n}\n# my-3D2dge handoff package (v0.89.1)\n\nEverything a coding agent needs to build, run, test and check a game on the full my-3D2dge engine, in one folder of text\nfiles. You don't need the engine's repository, and you don't need to read the engine's source below its header.\n\n**The engine is yours to change.** This copy is yours to fix, extend or rewrite in any way you see fit: `my-3d2dge.js`\nis the engine, readable, with every module, and every page and test here loads it (`modules/` and `my-3d2dge-agent.js`\nare separate copies). If you hand the game back, a line on what you changed and why helps: it shows what the engine\nlacks.\n\n## Start here\n\n1. **Read `API.md`**, the API card: a complete game to start from, what x, y and z mean in each view, the rules, the\n   common mistakes and the API by area. It is the one page to read whole.\n2. **Start from a game, not an empty file.** The kit for your genre (`kits/`): the card's Genre playbook names one for\n   each genre, and `kits/README.md` says which file is which. `kits/<id>.js` is a complete game in that genre, readable\n   (its title, play and end, the modules it rests on, sound, touch controls), `kits/<id>.html` plays it, and\n   `node kits/test.mjs <id>` runs it headless. Or the template, `game/`: a small complete game (climbing, a guard with\n   sight, an HTML HUD, scenes) that `game/index.html` plays and `game/test.mjs` tests without a browser. Copy one into\n   `game/` and make it yours.\n3. **Search `API-INDEX.md`** when you need a name: every public name in the engine, one line each, with its signature,\n   units and defaults, and the height rules at the top. `grep -n \"ledge\\|landing\" API-INDEX.md`. Don't read it whole.\n4. **`AI_GUIDE.md`** has the recipes: genre by genre, the look to aim for, the frame order, heights, recorded sessions.\n5. **Don't build a pause menu, settings, key rebinding, full screen or a loading screen**: every game has them (`API.md`,\n   \"Standard features\"). Adjust them with `new E.Game({ menu: { items, settings, controls, quit } })`; heavy setup goes in\n   `game.start({ boot: { steps } })`.\n6. **Objects without drawing code:** read `docs/ASSETS.md` whole before you draw a barrel, a table or a tree.\n   `r.shape('barrel', x, y, 0, { facing })` draws one of the core library's in every view; `node tools/asset-find.mjs\n   \"market stall\"` searches it and the store (`src/assets/sets/`: about a thousand objects, materials and sprites,\n   each with where it came from), and `node tools/asset-sheet.mjs mine.js#stool` draws one you wrote, to look at\n   before you use it.\n7. **A game in real 3D** (first person, a light gun, a racer on banked roads, flight, a dungeon crawled in 3D, fixed\n   cameras): the 2D views have no perspective camera, but the engine has a 3D add-on, `World3D` (three.js r182 and\n   Rapier 0.19.3 under the 2D engine, which keeps the HUD, menus and sound). It is not in this folder: take\n   `engine/my-3d2dge-3d.js` (its header is its manual), `vendor/` and the 3D kit closest to your game\n   (`src/starter3d/`) from the repository, github.com/michaelcrosato/my-3d2dge, and see them play at\n   my-3d2dge.vercel.app/3d.\n\n## What is here\n\n| File | What it is |\n| --- | --- |\n| `my-3d2dge.js` | the full engine, readable (one file, no dependencies): the core, then every module |\n| `modules/` | each engine module on its own, when there are any (one general system; its header is its manual), to load after the agent edition |\n| `my-3d2dge-agent.js` | the agent edition: the essential engine, whose header is a shorter manual (a game written for it runs on the full engine) |\n| `API.md`, `API-INDEX.md`, `AI_GUIDE.md` | the card, the index, the guide |\n| `kits/` | the 2D genre kits, readable: each kit's game (`<id>.js`) and the page that plays it (`<id>.html`), the table of them (`README.md`) and their headless test (`test.mjs`) |\n| `game/` | the template game: `index.html`, `game.js`, `test.mjs` |\n| `tools/check.mjs` | plays a game in headless Chromium, switches its views, and reports errors, what is on screen, and `game.debug.snapshot()` |\n| `tools/filmstrip.mjs` | records frames into one picture, to judge motion (`--seed 1` makes it repeatable, `--compare` marks what changed) |\n| `tools/replay.mjs` | replays a recorded play session exactly (`E.session`, a bug seen on a phone) |\n| `docs/ASSETS.md` | the asset card: still objects and materials as data (`r.shape`, `map.solid`, `E.MATERIALS`), the core library, writing one |\n| `tools/asset-find.mjs`, `asset-sheet.mjs`, `asset-set.mjs` | search the core library and the store; draw an object in every view and lint it; cut the few entries a game uses into a set of its own (`asset-lib.mjs` is theirs) |\n| `src/assets/` | the asset store: sets of objects and materials converted from CC0 libraries (Kenney, KayKit, ambientCG), with their catalogs. A game loads one with its script and `E.addAssets(window.ASSETS['kenney-furniture'])`; the Asset Lab shows them all at my-3d2dge.vercel.app/asset-lab |\n| `package.json` | pins Playwright for the tools |\n\nNot here: the 3D engine (three.js and Rapier) and its kits, the playbook's 3D rows. They are on the site\n(my-3d2dge.vercel.app/3d) and in the repository (github.com/michaelcrosato/my-3d2dge); here a 3D game is built on the 2D\nengine's views (`kits/README.md`, 3D).\n\n## Run, test, check\n\n```sh\nnpm install                          # Playwright, for the tools (once)\nnpx playwright install chromium      # its browser (once)\nnode game/test.mjs                   # the game's headless test: no browser, a second\nnode tools/check.mjs game/index.html # play it in a browser: errors, screenshots, its snapshot\nnode kits/test.mjs arcade            # a kit, headless: it plays, and its proof gives the same hash twice\nnode tools/check.mjs kits/arcade.html#arcade/maze   # a kit in a browser, at a part (its deep link)\nnode tools/filmstrip.mjs game/index.html --steps \"wait:800 press:Enter wait:500 rec:16:2 down:KeyD wait:600\" --seed 1\n```\n\nOpen `game/index.html` in a browser to play (or serve the folder: `npx serve`). To hand a single file to a person, inline\nthe two scripts into the page, writing every `</script` inside them as `<\\/script` (the agent edition's header has one,\nand the page would end there).\n\n## Testing a game without a browser\n\n`new E.Game()` is headless in Node (or with `{ headless: true }`): no screen, sound or DOM, and `draw` is skipped unless\nthe game is made with `draw: true` (the template is): then each `advance` draws a frame on a stand-in, and a draw error\nlands in `game.errors`, as it would on a player's screen.\n\n- `game.advance(seconds)` runs exact fixed steps of 1/120 s at once: `advance(1)` is 120 updates.\n- `game.input.tap('jump')` presses an action for one step, `hold('right')` holds one down, `hold('right', false)` lets go.\n- `game.debug = { snapshot() { return {...} }, teleport(x, y, z) {...} }` is your game's handle: tests read it, and\n  `tools/check.mjs` and `tools/replay.mjs` print it.\n- `game.stop()`, `game.start()` and `game.dispose()` stop, resume and end a game.\n- `game.go('play')` fades for `game.fadeTime` (.22 s) before the new scene enters: advance past it, or set\n  `game.fadeTime = 0` in a test.\n- A scene change clears `game.after` and `game.every` timers (`{ keep: true }` outlives it); those made before the first\n  scene live into it. It ends a hit-stop; `game.timeScale` stays (restore a slow motion with a kept timer). A boot step's `game.go(name)` enters that scene when the boot ends.\n- Draw changes nothing, and nothing your update or input relies on (a click target, what is on screen) may be made only\n  in `draw`: `E.Menu`'s rows come from its update (`menu.rowAt(i)` is entry i's box, for a test's click), and the camera\n  (`game.cam`) says where the screen is in update.\n- `E.store` keeps values for the visit in Node, which has no `localStorage` (`E.store.clear()` between games in one test).\n- A script's `tap` and `hold` are no device: `input.label()` keeps showing the keys or buttons the player used last.\n\nThe same inputs give the same game on every machine and at every refresh rate: the clock is an exact fixed step.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_15","type":"agent_message","text":"The title is **B-17 Cross Channel Chaos**. Research confirms the source’s defining loop: four directional guns, fuel-versus-payload choices, a downward bombsight, and assisted recovery at home. I’m now building the native 3D view and shared aircraft simulation in parallel.\n"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_16","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '1,220p' B-17-Cross-Channel-Chaos-B-17-Bomber-gpt-6.1-sol-ultra-20261106-043517/vendor/engine/dist/handoff/API.md\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_16","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '1,220p' B-17-Cross-Channel-Chaos-B-17-Bomber-gpt-6.1-sol-ultra-20261106-043517/vendor/engine/dist/handoff/API.md\"","aggregated_output":"# my-3D2dge API card (v0.89.1)\n\nmy-3D2dge (\"My 3D 2D Game Engine\") is a general-purpose retro-modern 2D game engine built for AI models. Use it to port, remaster, reimagine and remix games from the 8-bit to 64-bit eras (NES, SNES, Genesis, N64, PS1), or to make spiritual successors to them. Everything is drawn by code: no image or sound files. Characters are 3D skeletons drawn as pixel art, and the camera can be any classic 2D view.\n\n**Start from a kit:** each genre has one, a complete small game written to be copied (the Genre playbook below names it). In a single file it sits between `GAME START` and `GAME END`: the starter's shell (the game, its title menu, the proof), the slice and the start; a genre kit holds one slice, `dist/my-3d2dge.html` every one and the ANIMATION LAB (how each animation is driven). In the handoff package each kit's game is `kits/<id>.js`, readable. **To make a game, change the slice into yours, with its own title, play and game-over scenes, and delete the starter's menu and the slices you do not use. The engine is yours to change too:** fix, extend or rewrite any of it as you see fit.\n\n**Looking a name up:** grep `API-INDEX.md` (every public name, one line; members are filed under instance names: `rig.`, `talk.`, `mover.`, `flow.`, `map.`), not the engine's source. It, the guide (`AI_GUIDE.md`) and the tools are in the handoff package (my-3d2dge.vercel.app/handoff/) and the repository.\n\n## Quick start (a complete game)\n```js\n(() => {\nconst E = My3D2dge, { px, clamp } = E;            // always start like this\nconst game = new E.Game({ canvas: 'screen', res: 'snes', view: 'threequarter' });\nconst map = new E.TileMap({\n  rows: ['##########', '#@...s...#', '#..##....#', '#........#', '##########'],\n  legend: { '#': 1, '@': 'hero', 's': 'slime' },  // number = wall type, string = spawn tag\n  types: { 1: { h: 30, top: '#57506a', side: '#3d3750' } },\n  floorTex: (x, y) => E.tex.flagstone(x, y, { stones: ['#4b4559', '#554f64'].map(E.hex), mortar: E.hex('#221e2b'), hi: E.hex('#6f6782'), lo: E.hex('#322d3e'), speck: E.hex('#2a2634') })\n});\ngame.cam.bounds = v => map.bounds(v);\nconst s = map.find('hero'), hero = new E.Body({ x: s.x, y: s.y, r: 5 });\nconst rig = new E.Humanoid({ hat: 'pointed' });\ngame.start({\n  update(dt) {\n    const m = game.input.move(), d = game.view.screenDirToGround(m[0], m[1]);\n    hero.vx = d[0] * 80; hero.vy = d[1] * 80; hero.update(dt, map);\n    if (Math.hypot(d[0], d[1]) > .1) hero.facing = Math.atan2(d[1], d[0]);\n    rig.update(dt, { x: hero.x, y: hero.y, z: hero.z, vx: hero.vx, vy: hero.vy, facing: hero.facing || 0 });\n    game.focus(hero.x, hero.y, 10);                // the camera looks here: call every update\n  },\n  draw(r) {\n    map.drawFloor(r); r.shadow(hero.x, hero.y, 5); map.queueWalls(r);\n    r.actor(hero.x, hero.y, hero.z, (g, ox, oy) => rig.draw(g, ox, oy, r.view));\n    r.text('HELLO', 4, 4, '#ffffff');              // HUD text in screen pixels\n  }\n});\n})();\n```\n\n## Look target (read this before drawing anything)\nAim above SNES, level with the best PS1 / N64 2D games (Symphony of the Night, Metal Slug, Legend of Mana, Klonoa). Games that skip these steps look like Atari games. **Every game should use all of them:**\n1. **Resolution** `res: 'ps1'` (320x240) or `'snes'`, with `expand: true` so it fills any screen (anchor the HUD to `r.W` / `r.H`), and characters 40-60 px tall: `new E.Humanoid({ size: 1.3 })` (HD style is the default: shaded volumetric limbs, outfits, hair).\n2. **Dress the character**: an `outfit`, `hair`, a `hat`, `armor`, a `cape`, `sleeves` (Characters), and a real palette in `colors` (never leave the defaults on everyone).\n3. **Backdrop behind every side-view level**: `const bg = new E.Backdrop('castle-night')` then `bg.draw(r)` first in `draw` (a ground view's floor runs on to the screen's edges: `map.outside`). Presets: `day dusk night castle-night city-night desert forest ocean cave space`, or your own `{ sky, sun | moon, stars, starsY: .7, layers: [{ kind: 'mountains' | 'hills' | 'forest' | 'city' | 'castle' | 'clouds' | 'sea' | 'fog' | 'stalactites', color, y, height, parallax, fill }] }` (`starsY` = how far down the stars reach; a layer but clouds, fog and stalactites fills the screen below its skyline unless `fill: false`).\n4. **Textured tiles**: PlatformMap styles `stone` (with `moss`), `brick`, `wood`, `metal`, `ground` (with `flower`), `block`, `pipe`, `bonus`; TileMap floors from `E.tex.*`, TileMap walls with `face: 'brick' | 'stone' | 'rock' | 'plank' | 'timber' | 'plaster' | 'hedge'` and tops with `roof: 'tiles' | 'slab' | 'leaves' | 'grass'` (a village = timber and plaster houses with tile roofs, hedges, rock cliffs).\n5. **Props in every room** (3-8 per screen): `r.prop(name, x, y, z, { size, color, light: true })` with `torch candle candelabra chandelier brazier window banner pillar statue crate barrel chest pot sign fence lamp door tree pine bush flowers grass rock crystal bones skull vines cobweb lantern streetlamp awning hydrant trashcan firedrum sandbags cactus palm mushroom`. Flames animate, glow and can light the scene. `chest` / `door` take `{ open: true }`, `pillar` takes `{ broken: true }`, `window` is a gothic rose window with lead cames (`colors: [...]` for the glass, `size: 2-3` for a cathedral); hang `vines`, `cobweb`, `lantern` with `{ anchor: 'top' }`. With heroes at size 1.2+, give the scene `propSize: 1.4` (or set `E.style.propSize`) so props match them.\n6. **Effects on every hit**: `particles.explosion(x, y, z, size)`, `smoke`, `fire`, `glints`, `sparks`, `game.flash(color, s)`, `game.freeze`, `game.shake`.\n7. **Color**: `E.tones(hex)` gives `{ deep, sh, base, lt, hi }` hue-shifted shades and `E.ramp(hex, n)` a palette ramp. Shade everything you draw yourself with them (shadow side `sh`, lit edge `lt`, a `hi` sparkle).\n8. **Typography**: the default font is a 5x7 proportional font with lower case. Titles: `E.font.title(g, 'NAME', x, y, { scale: 3, colors: [...], align: 'center' })`. HUD text: `{ shadow: '#000', outline: false }` or `gradient: [top, bottom]`. `font: 'tiny'` is the old 3x5 font.\n9. **Light every scene**: `game.lights.enabled = true; game.lights.ambient = .5` in a scene's `enter`, then each draw a few lights where light comes from (`r.prop('lamp', x, y, 0, { light: true })`, `game.lights.add(x, y, z, 60, .9, { color })`): dusk, torchlight and glows give depth. It looks the same in every browser and check; `game.enableGPU({ map })` adds shadows in ground views, and falls back to it.\n10. **Faces in dialog**: `talk.say(lines, { name: 'MIRA', portrait: miraRig })` puts a live close-up of that Humanoid (blinking, hair, hat) beside every line. `rig.drawPortrait(g, x, y, 40)` draws one anywhere (HUD, RPG party windows).\n\n## Coordinates: what x, y, z mean in each view\nWorld units: one tile = 16. **z is always up.** Game logic never stores screen pixels.\n\n| View | Looks like | Ground plane | Use for levels | Move with |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| `'iso'` (yaw 45, pitch 30) | Diablo, Landstalker | x/y ground, z up | `E.TileMap` | `E.Body` |\n| `'threequarter'` (pitch 55) | Zelda LttP, Stardew | x right, y down the screen | `E.TileMap` | `E.Body` |\n| `'topdown'` (pitch 80) | GTA 1, Hotline Miami | x right, y down | `E.TileMap` | `E.Body` |\n| `'brawler'` (pitch 25) | Final Fight, 2.5D | x right, y into the screen | `E.TileMap` or `E.PlatformMap` | `E.Body` or `E.Platformer` |\n| `'side'` (pitch 0) | Mario, Mega Man | **x right, z up, y = 0 (depth)** | `E.PlatformMap` | `E.Platformer` |\n| `'overhead'` (pitch 90, scale 1) | 1942, Galaga, Pac-Man | x = screen x px, y = screen y px | none, or a TileMap | your own x/y, or `E.Body` |\n\n- A unit is `r.ppu` pixels: at zoom 1 iso 1.41, overhead 1, the others 1.5 (a tile about 24). A sprite's pixel is a screen pixel (`{ world: true }`: it grows with the view, as rigs and maps do).\n- In `'side'` the screen shows x (right) and z (up). **y is depth and is normally 0.** Focus the camera with `game.focus(hero.x, 0, hero.z + 24)`.\n- In ground views, the screen direction the player pushes becomes a world direction through `game.view.screenDirToGround(mx, my)`.\n- `r.actor(x, y, z, (g, ox, oy) => ...)` calls your function with `(ox, oy)` = the buffer pixel where world point (x, y, z) lands. Draw the character around that point.\n\n## Rules\n1. Keep game logic in world units, and use `dt` everywhere. `update(dt)` runs in exact fixed steps: every 1/120 s of real time is one step of `dt = 1/120 * game.timeScale`, the same at any refresh rate (`game.alpha` = the part of a step left over).\n2. Draw only with `E.px.*`, `E.font`, `E.ui`, sprites, props and the `r.*` helpers. Never use `ctx.arc`, `ctx.stroke`, `ctx.fillText` or canvas gradients on the game buffer (they blur pixels). For translucency and glow use `px.blend(g, alpha, 'add' | 'multiply' | 'screen' | 'normal', () => {...})`, `px.polyDither`, `px.ddisc`, `r.glowDisc` and `r.shadow`: they use stepped alpha and blend modes like PS1 / SNES hardware (or dithering with `E.style.trans = 'dither'` for an NES / Genesis look).\n3. Anything that can overlap anything else goes through `r.actor`, `r.sprite` or `r.queue` (depth sorted). Backgrounds (`r.sky`, `map.drawFloor`, `level.draw`) come first in `draw`.\n4. Read input only in `update`. Use `pressed(a)` for one-shot actions (menus, jumps, shots), `down(a)` for held actions, and `buffered(a)` + `consume(a)` for forgiving combat input.\n5. Animate characters from continuous values (velocity, timers, easing): the rigs, not frame lists.\n6. Colors are `'#rrggbb'` (or `'#rgb'`) strings.\n7. Put the whole game in one IIFE `(() => { ... })();` between the markers, and start it with `game.start(...)`.\n\n## Common mistakes (check these first)\n- Nothing on screen: the camera looks at the wrong place. Use `game.follow(hero)` once (in the scene's `enter`), or call `game.focus(...)` every update. In side view the hero has y = 0.\n- Walls or level missing: you forgot `map.drawFloor(r)` + `map.queueWalls(r)` (TileMap) or `level.draw(r)` (PlatformMap).\n- Using a TileMap for a side-scroller. Side-scrollers use `E.PlatformMap` + `E.Platformer`.\n- HUD drawn in world coordinates. Use `r.text(...)` or `r.overlay(g => ...)` with screen pixels (`r.W`, `r.H`).\n- An old key layout: platformers want `input: 'PLATFORMER'` (Space jumps), shooters `input: 'SHMUP'` (Space fires).\n- Errors show in a red box on screen and in the console. Fix the first one first.\n- Colours are `'#rrggbb'`, `rgb()`, `hsl()` or a basic name ('orange'); any other draws magenta.\n- `mouseGround()` is `[x, y]`; `settings.reset(group)` resets a group ('Sound'; none: all), not a key; `particles.explosion()` adds a hit-stop and a shake (`{ freeze: false, shake: 0 }`); `E.font.text` outlines unless `outline: false`.\n- A frame past 50 ms gives up its time (no catch-up): a test in a slow browser waits on the game's state, not the clock.\n\n## Game\n`new E.Game({ canvas: 'screen', view, views, res, expand, input, bg })`\n- `res`: `'nes'` 256x240, `'snes'` 256x224, `'genesis'` 320x224, `'gb'` 160x144, `'gba'` 240x160, `'ps1'` / `'n64'` 320x240, `'wide'` 400x225, or `[w, h]`. Fixed pixels: whole-number scaling on a desktop screen, the largest fit on a phone (Settings, Pixel scaling). Leave it out for an adaptive size.\n- `expand: true`: full screen at any shape, no bars. `res` becomes the least the screen shows and `r.W` x `r.H` grows to fill the window (a 16:9 monitor shows about 427x240 of `'ps1'`, a phone held upright about 320x690). Anchor the HUD to `r.W` and `r.H`, and give the level something to show in the extra space (more of it, a backdrop, a HUD deck under it on a tall screen). `expand: { maxW, maxH }` caps the growth. A scene may set it too.\n- Adaptive size: `minW` / `minH` set the scale (the screen shows at least that many pixels), `maxW` / `maxH` cap the view (the rest is letterboxed). `portrait: { maxH: 1000 }` overrides them while the screen is taller than wide, so a phone held upright (9:16) is filled instead of showing a band across its middle. `game.screen.portrait` says which way it is.\n- `input`: `'DEFAULT'` (top-down action), `'PLATFORMER'`, `'SHMUP'`, `'THIRDPERSON'`, or your own `{ action: ['KeyQ', 'Pad0'] }`.\n- `views`: the views your game supports; `game.nextView()` cycles them (bind it to a key).\n- Start: `game.start({ update(dt), draw(r) })`, or with scenes (below).\n- Methods: `follow(obj, { z: 16, lead: 20 })` (camera tracks it automatically), `focus(x, y, z)` (or aim it yourself every update), `setView(id)`, `nextView()`, `freeze(s)` (hit-stop: `update` waits; `game.hitstop` is the time left), `shake(n)`, `after(s, fn)`, `every(s, fn)` (timers in game time, return `{ cancel() }`), `hook('input' | 'step' | 'enter', fn)` (your own each step, paused too for input; returns its removal), `mouseGround()`, `go(scene, data)`, `enableGPU({ map })`.\n- Fields: `W`, `H` (screen pixels), `time`, `real`, `timeScale` (0.25 = slow motion), `paused`, `input`, `audio`, `particles`, `lights`, `view`, `errors`, `cam`. `game.fail('my power', err)` reports an error in your code (logged, in `errors`, on the error panel) and plays on.\n- Camera zoom and turn: `game.setZoom(1.5)` (.5 .. 3; everything drawn by the engine re-rasterizes crisply, the HUD stays), `game.rotateView(45)` (ground views only), `game.resetCamera()` (to the scene's zoom), `game.zoom`, `game.yaw`, `game.note('ZOOM 2x')` (a short notice at the top of the screen; `game.shownNote` is the one showing). Custom painters can read `r.view.zoom` (undefined at 1x) to scale their own art.\n- The player's zoom: a scene's `camera: { zoom: [.75, 2], start: 1, tall: 1.5 }` lets the player zoom within `zoom` from `start` (wheel, `-` `=`, pinch, Settings; `false`: none; `AI_GUIDE.md`, Camera).\n- Tests and tools: `new E.Game({ headless: true })` (the default in Node: no screen, sound or DOM; `draw` is skipped, or with `draw: true` run on a stand-in, its errors in `game.errors`) or `{ loop: false }` runs only by `game.advance(seconds, { draw })` (exact fixed steps at once); `input.tap(action)` presses for one step, `input.hold(action, on)`; `game.debug = { snapshot() {...} }` is your game's handle (`tools/check.mjs` prints it); `game.stop()`, `start()`, `dispose()`.\n- Sessions: `?record=1`, then the pause menu's Save session; `node tools/replay.mjs session.json` replays it exactly, headless (`AI_GUIDE.md`, Sessions).\n- Camera: `cam.offset = [dx, dy]` sits the focus that many screen pixels from the centre (above a phone's touch buttons: `[0, -60]`); `cam.bounds = v => map.bounds(v)` keeps it inside the level (in side views a level shorter than the screen sits on the bottom edge; `cam.align = 'center'` to change); `cam.room = [160, 128]` moves screen by screen (Zelda, Metroid) and `cam.moving` is true while it slides; `cam.smooth` = lag in seconds (0: locked to the target); `cam.window = [48, 24]` a dead zone the focus moves in before the camera follows; `cam.snapY = true` follows a followed body's height only when it lands (side-scrollers); `cam.frame([p1, p2], { margin, zoom: [.5, 1] })` keeps them all in view, zooming out as they part (`frame(null)` stops); `cam.free = { keys, edge: 10, drag, speed: 300, bounds: [x0, y0, x1, y1] }` a free camera (strategy, sims): keys, a stick, the screen's edge or a drag pan it, a zoom goes toward the pointer or the pinch.\n\n## Scenes (title, play, game over)\n```js\ngame.start({ scene: 'title', scenes: {\n  title: { update(dt) { if (game.input.pressed('start')) game.go('play', { level: 1 }); },\n           draw(r) { r.sky(['#101848', '#402a70']); r.text('PRESS START', r.W / 2, 100, '#fff', { align: 'center', scale: 2 }); } },\n  play: { pausable: true, view: 'side', input: 'PLATFORMER', res: 'snes', views: ['side', 'brawler'], touch: ['jump', 'attack'],\n          enter(data) { /* build the level */ }, exit() {}, update(dt) {}, draw(r) {} }\n} });\n```\n`game.go(name, data)` switches after a short dithered fade (`game.fadeTime`: a test advances past it; `{ fade: 0 }` cuts; `{ fade: 'wipe' | 'iris' | 'mosaic' | 'swirl' | 'dissolve' | 'white', seconds: .4, at: hero }` a transition, a plain fade under reduce motion); timers (but `after(s, fn, { keep: true })`) and particles are cleared, a hit-stop ends (`timeScale` stays). `pausable: true`: Escape / P / Start pauses it, with the pause menu (below). `view`, `views`, `input`, `res`, `expand`, `touch`, `camera`, `propSize` are options applied on entry (a method so named warns). A scene is one object every visit: reset its state in `enter`. `back()` takes a phone's back gesture first (true if it went back: a sub-menu closed).\n\n## Motion and timing: tweens, scripts, paths, weather\n- Tweens (Phaser's): `game.tween(door, { y: 40 }, .5, { ease: 'outBack', delay, repeat, yoyo, onDone, keep })` eases numbers on game time: paused with the game, slowed by `timeScale`, ended by a scene change unless `keep`. Returns `{ done, cancel() }`. `E.ease` has Penner's set: `linear`, `inSine` `outSine` `inOutSine`, `inQuad` `outQuad` `inOutQuad`, the same for `Cubic`, `Back`, `Elastic`, `Bounce`.\n- Scripts (Unity's coroutines) for cutscenes, boss patterns, wave timelines, tutorials:\n```js full-script\ngame.script(function* () {\n  yield 1;                                   // seconds of game time\n  yield E.until(() => door.open);            // a condition\n  yield game.tween(boss, { y: 80 }, 1.5);    // a tween (or another script, or a generator) finishing\n  for (let w = 0; w < 3; w++) { spawnWave(w); yield E.any([8, () => enemies.length === 0]); }\n});\n```\n  `E.all([...])` waits for all; a bare `yield` waits one step. It runs at once to its first `yield`, the same at any refresh rate; `{ keep: true }` outlives the scene; `.cancel()`, `.done`, `.value`.\n- Paths: `const p = new E.Path([[x, y, z], ...], { closed, smooth: 'catmull' })`: `p.length`, `p.at(d)` (`{ x, y, z, angle }` by distance along: moving platforms, dives, rails), `p.nearest(x, y)` (a racer's progress), `p.draw(r)` to see it.\n- Weather: `game.weather = { kind: 'rain' | 'snow' | 'ash' | 'leaves' | 'sand', amount: .8, wind: .3, lightning: .2 }` (null: clear) falls through the world in every view, settles or splashes, flashes and thunders; cosmetic only (its own random stream), and it ends with the scene: set it in `enter`.\n- Wrap-around (Asteroids): `x = E.wrap(x, 0, W)`, `E.wrapDiff(a, b, W)` (the short way across the seam), and `wrap: [W, H]` on `r.sprite` or `r.actor` draws a copy across each edge.\n\n## Standard features (every game has them: don't build your own)\nWith no code: a **pause menu** on pausable scenes (Resume, Settings, Controls, Full screen, Quit to title; keys, mouse, gamepad and touch), **settings** saved per game (`game.settings`: volume, music, effects, mute, reduce motion, shake and flashes, pixel scaling, a screen filter, the frame rate and its readout), **controls** the player rebinds (conflicts said first; dead zone, invert aim and move, button symbols, vibration; touch button side, size, opacity), **full screen** (a phone's first tap, a top-right button, the menu; turning it off is remembered), a **menu button** at the top right (on a touch screen it stays in play: it is the touch START), a **way out** of every menu screen, the **back gesture** stepping back in the game (`game.back()`) before it leaves the page, **pausing** when the page is hidden or the controller unplugs, and a page set up for phones (safe areas, no scrolling, zooming or pull to refresh on the canvas).\n- Adjust: `new E.Game({ menu: { items: [['Restart', fn]], settings: [{ key: 'hints', label: 'Hints', value: true }, { key: 'difficulty', options: ['Easy', 'Normal', 'Hard'], value: 'Normal' }], controls: { attack: 'Sword', skill: false }, quit: 'title' } })`, then read `game.settings.hints`. Leave parts out: `menu: false` (your own pause), `fullscreen: 'button' | false`, `corner: false`, `backGesture: false`, `autoPause: false`, `touch: 'never'` (a phone is told a controller or keyboard is needed). `game.cornerArea()`: where the corner's buttons cover the screen (or null): keep a HUD clear of it.\n- Save slots (`game.saves`): three slots and an autosave, each with its place, level and time played. `game.saves.write = () => ({ data, place, level })` and `read = save => {...}`; then `save(slot)` (0, 1, 2 or `'auto'`), `load(slot)`, `copy(a, b)`, `erase(slot)`, `autosave()`, `list()`, `latest()` (a title's Continue). `menu: { saves: true }` (or `{ slots, version, migrate(data, from) }`) puts Save (while `saves.canSave`: a save point) and Load in the pause menu, and `saves.show('save' | 'load')` opens the screen from your own menu. Blocked storage keeps them for the visit.\n- Prompts: `game.input.label('jump')` is that action's key or button on the player's device, after rebinding ('Space', 'A', '✕'). PlayStation symbols by default: `settings: [{ key: 'glyphs', value: 'playstation' }]` (a standard key without a label sets its default). A canvas title's OPTIONS: `game.menu('settings')`. From code: `game.settings.set(key, v)`, `game.fullscreen.toggle()` (from a key, click or tap), `game.pause(reason)`, `game.resume()`. `live: true` (or `game.menu(name, { pause: false })`): menus over a world that keeps stepping (online play).\n- **Boot**: heavy setup in steps behind a boot screen, and a report for any error before play: `game.start({ scenes, scene, boot: { title, steps: [['Building the city', () => { map = build(); }]] } })` (`AI_GUIDE.md`, Boot).\n\n## Input: `game.input`\n- Actions in every preset: `up down left right` (WASD, arrows, d-pad), `start` (Enter, Start), `pause` (Escape, P, Start), `confirm` (Enter, Space, J, Z, pad A), `cancel` (Escape, Backspace, X, K, pad B).\n- DEFAULT adds `attack` (J, X, click), `dash` (Space, Shift, K), `skill` (L, E, right click), `jump` (Z). PLATFORMER: `jump` (Space, Z, K, pad A), `attack` (X, J, click), `dash` (Shift, C, L), `skill`. SHMUP: `fire` (Space, Z, J, click), `bomb` (X, K). THIRDPERSON: `sprint` (Shift), `jump` (Space), `crouch` (C, Ctrl), `interact` (E, F), `attack` (J), `block` (K), `dodge` (L), `use` (Q), `map` (M, Tab).\n- `down(a)`, `pressed(a)`, `released(a)`, `repeat(a, delay, rate)` (menus), `buffered(a, win)` + `consume(a)`, `consumeAll()`, `anyPressed()`, `move()` (screen direction `[x, y]`, length up to 1), `use(preset)`, `touchButtons(['jump', 'attack'])`, `touchSet('confirm', 'TALK', near)` (a context button: relabel it, or hide it while it has nothing to do).\n- Moves: `input.motion('236', 'attack', { facing })` is true on the step a quarter circle forward and punch ends (numpad notation, mirrored when `facing` is -1: `'623'`, `'41236'`); `input.sequence(['up', 'up', 'down', 'down+right', 'attack'], { window: .5 })` any run of inputs (a cheat code); `input.history` the last second of them (`{ t, dir, pressed }`, for an input display).\n- Players (two to four on one machine): `game.players` is `[game.input, ...]`, each an input with this API, its `player` number, `name` (`'P2'`), `color` (`E.PLAYER_COLORS`) and device. `game.allowJoin({ max: 2, onJoin: (input, n) => {} })` lets them in: Start on a free gamepad, or 2 on the keyboard (player 2 takes its right half: arrows, `.` `/` `,` and the numpad; player 1 keeps WASD with F G H; a preset's `halves: { left: { pass: ['KeyR'] }, right: {...} }` its own); `game.addPlayer({ pad: 0 })` or `({ keys: 'right' })`, `game.removePlayer(p)`. Prompts, the pause (P2 PAUSED), a lost controller and the Controls screen are per player. One screen: `cam.frame(heroes)`. Split: `game.splitScreen(2, { follow: [h1, h2], layout: 'auto' })` (`'columns'`, `'rows'`, `'grid'`; up to 4) draws the scene once per viewport (`r.viewport` is `{ i, x, y, w, h }`), then `scene.hud(r)` once over the whole screen; `game.viewports[i].follow(t)` or `.focus(x, y)`.\n- `clear()` releases held inputs, pending presses, virtual sticks and touch buttons; focus loss does this automatically. `suppress(a)` blocks an action for the current tick; `suppressCode('Mouse0')` lets a HUD widget consume that mouse button while other devices bound to the action still work.\n- Controller settings: `deadzone` (default `.18`, radial and rescaled), `invertAimY`, `lastDevice` (the index has the rest). The left stick and the touch stick, pushed past halfway, press `up` / `down` / `left` / `right` as the d-pad does (menus, dialog choices, ladders); bind `PadAxisUp/Down/Left/Right` to your own menu actions for the same; the right stick is `PadRAxisUp/Down/Left/Right`, the wheel `WheelUp`/`WheelDown`; `value(a)`: 0 to 1 (a trigger's travel, a stick's push). Options while Create is held is no press (the AI Hub's chord).\n- Touch settings: `touchEnabled`, `stickSide` (`'left'` or `'right'`), `stickRadius` (CSS pixels), `touchFilter(event)` (return false to reserve a canvas tap for UI). `touchArea()`: where the touch buttons cover the screen (`{ x0, y0, x1, y1 }`, or null): keep a prompt clear of it. `clicked()`: where a click or tap on the canvas landed (`[x, y]` in screen pixels) the step after it, else null; `pointer()`: the mouse in screen pixels; `drag()`: how far the stick's finger moved this step (`[dx, dy]`, or null), to steer one to one; `steer = 'drag'`: a finger anywhere steers, no stick drawn (`stickOn`: a finger is on it). `zones = [{ x0, y0, x1, y1, act }]` (fractions of the canvas): a finger in one holds its act until it lifts (a pinball's halves). Gestures (a mouse or one finger, screen pixels): `box()` → `{ x0, y0, x1, y1, done }` (a left drag; on touch a long press, then a drag), `longPress()`, `doubleTap()`, `pan()` → `[dx, dy]` (a finger's drag on open ground, a middle or right drag), `zoomPoint()`; `feed('down' | 'move' | 'up', x, y, { touch, button, id })` plays a pointer in a test. `bindButtons(root)` wires `[data-act]` elements.\n\n## Drawing: `r` in `draw(r)`\n- Background: `r.sky(['#top', '#mid', '#bottom'])`, `r.starfield({ count, speed, dir: 'down' | 'left' })`.\n- Depth sorted: `r.actor(x, y, z, (g, ox, oy) => rig.draw(g, ox, oy, r.view), { flash: '#ffffff', flashMix: .75, alpha, xray, outline, ghost, emissive, every, key })` (the flash tints over the sprite so shading shows: `flashMix` .5 by default, 1 solid; `every: 2, key: npc` redraws a background character every other frame; actors up to about 250 px tall), `r.sprite(x, y, z, sprite, { flip, anchor: 'bottom' | 'center', glow, flash })`, `r.queue(x, y, z, g => {...}, { bias })` (sorted by that one point: a long wall by `r.queueSpan(a, b, z, h, fn)`), `r.actorNow(...)` (as `r.actor`, drawn at once over what is drawn so far), `r.box(g, x0, y0, z0, x1, y1, z1, top, side)` (inside a queue function). `{ pick: unit }` on any of them (and `r.shape`), then `r.pick(sx, sy)` → what the last frame drew under a screen point, front to back.\n- Floor marks: `r.shadow(x, y, radius, alpha, color, surfaceZ)`, `r.decal(g => r.groundArc(...))`, `r.groundDisc`, `r.groundRing`, `r.groundPts(x, y, rad, n, z)`.\n- On top, unlit, screen pixels: `r.text(str, x, y, color, { align, scale, outline })`, `r.textAt(x, y, z, str, color)`, `r.overlay(g => {...})`.\n- `r.w(x, y, z)` = buffer pixel of a world point. `r.W`, `r.H`, `r.ix`, `r.iy` (pass to dither functions), `r.view`, `r.visible(x, y, z)`.\n- X-ray: `r.actor(..., { xray: true })` shows the actor's hidden part, a translucent tint with a 1-px outline (a checker in `E.style.trans = 'dither'`), wherever a wall, a prop or shape at least chest high (22; `hides: true | false` says otherwise) or anything queued with `{ hides: true }` is drawn in front of it; not by one rising less than 8 above its feet (the roof it stands on, a cut-down wall). `xray: { color, outline (false: none), actors: true }`: with `actors` other bodies in front hide it too (a hero stays findable in a crowd). Afterimages: `ghost: { color, life, alpha, owner }`; `owner` (the actor's `{x, y, z}`) keeps a trail left nearer the camera sorted behind the live body.\n- Glowing things you draw yourself: `r.queue(x, y, z, fn, { emissive: true })` is drawn again after lighting so darkness never dims it (flames, lasers, magic, neon). It still hides behind whatever stands in front of it: walls and `r.actor` bodies do this on their own, and any other queued draw can join them with `{ solid: true }`. (Canvas lighting builds a depth-ordered mask for this; `game.r.glowMask = false` skips it on slow machines.)\n\n## Pixels, sprites, text, UI\n- `px.rect(g, x, y, w, h, c)`, `dot`, `line(g, x0, y0, x1, y1, c, width)`, `disc(g, x, y, r, c)`, `ell`, `poly(g, pts, c)`, `polyDither(g, pts, c, 0..1, r.ix, r.iy)`, `ddisc`, `sprite(g, spr, x, y, flip)` (or `{ flip, rot, scale }`), `glow(g, 0..1)` (GPU glow for what follows).\n- Sprites from strings (for coins, bullets, ships, icons, NES-style enemies): `const COIN = E.sprite(['.yy.', 'yYYy', '.yy.'], { y: '#f0b020', Y: '#fff0a0' }, scale)`. `.` and space are transparent. Frames: `const walk = E.anim([f1, f2, f3], 8, { pingpong })` (or one sheet: `E.anim(sheet, 8, { frames: 4 })`), drawn with `r.sprite(x, y, z, walk, { t })`. `r.sprite(..., { rot: angle, scale })` turns and scales in whole pixels (cached in 16 steps a turn; `steps: 32`); `E.recolor(spr, { '#3a8a4a': '#8a3a4a' })` swaps a palette.\n- Font (5x7 proportional with lower case: ASCII, the face buttons, arrows, ★ ♥ ♪ ✓ … ° € £, the accented Latin letters; any other is `?`; `font: 'tiny'` for 3x5): `E.font.text(g, str, x, y, color, { outline, shadow, gradient, scale, align, wrap, font })`, `E.font.title(g, str, x, y, { scale, colors, outline, depth, depthColor, align })`, `E.font.width(str, opts)`, `E.font.lineHeight(opts)`, `E.font.wrap(str, maxW, opts)`. Glyphs: ASCII plus `♥ ★ ← → ↑ ↓ • × ♪ ▸ ©`.\n- UI (inside `r.overlay(g => ...)`): `E.ui.box(g, x, y, w, h, { bg, border, gradient, alpha })` (a gradient window like Final Fantasy; `bg` can be `[top, bottom]`, `gradient: false` for flat, `alpha: .6` for a see-through HUD panel), `E.ui.bar(g, x, y, w, h, 0..1, color)`, `E.ui.hearts(g, x, y, hp, max)` (half hearts allowed), `rig.drawPortrait(g, x, y, size, { zoom: 3, turn: .6, bg, frame, cape: false, weapon: false, tint: '#808080' })` (character close-up; it stays upright while the rig kneels or lies down; `tint` greys out a KO'd hero).\n- Dialog: `const talk = new E.Dialog(game)`; `talk.say(['Line one.', 'Page two.'], { name: 'ELDER', portrait: elderRig, onDone, choices: ['YES', 'NO'], onChoice(i) })` (choices show on the last page: the keys, or a tap or click on one, pick); in update `if (talk.update(dt)) return;` (true while a modal box is open: play waits); in draw `talk.draw(r)`. `portrait` takes a Humanoid (live close-up; `portraitSize: 40`, `portraitOpts: { zoom, turn }`) or a function `(g, x, y, size) => {...}`. Radio chatter during play: `talk.say('Enemy fighters ahead!', { name, portrait, auto: 2.5, modal: false })` turns its pages and closes by itself while the game keeps running. Per line: `place: 'top' | 'middle' | 'bottom'`, `y` (pixels) and `alpha` (see-through box). `new E.Dialog(game, { speed, lines, color, nameColor, voice, width, bg, border, vars })` (`voice`: a sound, or `(ch, i, talk) => {}` per letter); `talk.close()`, `talk.open`. Markup in the text: `{c=#ffd36a}gold{/c}` a color, `{w=.5}` a pause, `{s=12}slowly{/s}` letters a second, `{shake}..{/shake}`, `{wave}..{/wave}`, `{$name}` a value from `say(text, { vars })` or `talk.vars`.\n- Menu: `const menu = new E.Menu(game, ['START', { label: 'LOAD', disabled: true }], { x: 'center', y: 100, title, onPick(i, item), onCancel, scale: 2, rows: 6 })` (rows: it scrolls); `menu.update(dt)`; `menu.draw(r)`. Keys, d-pad and sticks move it; a click or tap on an entry picks it (so a phone can leave a title), and the mouse over one moves the cursor. A tap on a dialog box turns its page as confirm does.\n- HTML screens and HUD: `const ui = new E.Shell(game, { theme: { scale: 2 } (a TV; or `tv: true`), settings, screens: { pause, help, dev: { rows: ['glyphs'] } } })`; `ui.show('title' | 'results' | 'map' | ..., spec)`; each step `ui.hud({ objective, status, bars, prompt, minimap })` (`minimap: { map, fog, camera: true, markers, onClick(x, y) }`); `ui.toast(title, text)`.\n\n## Sound: `game.audio` (chip synth, no files, starts after the first key press)\n- `sfx(name, { vol, pitch, pan, loop })` → `{ stop(), set({ pan, vol }) }` (a loop sounds on: an engine, rain). Presets: `jump jump2 land step coin pickup key powerup oneup heal hit hurt stomp bump swing whoosh punch kick shoot laser charge explode boom door secret warp die select confirm cancel pause text blip`.\n- Custom: `sfx({ wave: 'square' | 'pulse' | 'pulse12' | 'triangle' | 'saw' | 'sine' | 'noise', freq: 440 or 'A4', to: 880, dur: .2, vol: .3, arp: [0, 4, 7], step: .05, vib: [8, .03] })`, or `audio.define('zap', voice)`; `audio.instrument('pluck', (ctx, bus, time, freq, dur, vol) => ...)` is a `wave` too.\n- Music: `music('title' | 'adventure' | 'dungeon' | 'boss' | 'victory')` (built in; any other name warns and plays nothing), or your own `{ bpm: 120, steps: 4, tracks: [{ wave: 'square', vol: .15, notes: 'C5 - E5 - G5 . . . | ...' }, { wave: 'triangle', notes: '...' }, { wave: 'drums', notes: 'k . h . s . h .' }] }`. Tokens: a note (`C4`, `F#3`, `Bb2`), `-` holds, `.` rests, `|` is ignored; drums `k s h o c t`. `music(null)` stops. `mute()`, `setVolume(0..1)` (or set `audio.musicVolume`, `sfxVolume`, then `audio.applyVolume()`), `duck(on)` (quieter music under your own pause or map screen). Your own Web Audio connects to `audio.bus('sfx' | 'music' | 'voice')`, under the volume and mute.\n- The music clock (the full engine): a song's place is game time, headless too, and the sound follows it. `music(song, { sync: true })` pauses with the game (else it plays on); `audio.pos` → `{ t, step, beat, bar, at, loop, bpm, layers, playing }`; `at(step, fn)`, `onBeat(fn)` (on the update step); `tempo(bpm)`; `layer(name or index, vol, fade)` (a track's `name`, `on: false` starts it silent: the chase's drums in by layers); `music(song, { fade: 1 })` crossfades; `sting(song, { at: 'bar' })` over the music; `sfx(voice, { step })` on a step of the music. `settings.audioOffset` (ms, Settings, Sound: Calibrate) sets `audio.offset`; `audio.calibrate()` → `{ tap(), result, done, stop() }`.\n\n## Levels\n**TileMap** (top-down, isometric, brawler): walls stand on the ground plane.\n- `new E.TileMap({ rows, legend, types, floorTex, block: ['water', 'lava'], ao: 5, outside })` (`ao` = width of the contact shadow along wall bases, 0 = none; `outside`: the ground past the map, a color, or `false` for none). `types[id] = { h, top, side, line, course, cut: true, cutH, face, roof, beam }` (`cut` lowers walls that block the camera, those `map.isFront(cx, cy, view)` says; a map may replace it; `face`: `'brick'` (default) `'stone' 'rock' 'plank' 'timber' 'plaster' 'hedge' 'none'`; `roof`: `'speckle'` (default) `'plain' 'tiles' 'slab' 'leaves' 'grass'`; `beam` = timber color). `floorTex(x, y, floorTag, view)` returns `[r, g, b]` (or `[r, g, b, glow]`); ready-made: `E.tex.flagstone`, `grass`, `dirt`, `water`, `planks`, `checker`, `plain`. A map of more than 128 x 128 cells bakes its floor in squares as the camera comes to them and lets the far ones go (`chunks: true | false` to choose; `map.floorBytes()` what it holds), so a 256 x 256 world map costs what the screen shows.\n- Legend values: a number = wall type, a string = spawn tag, `{ tile, floor, spawn, block }` for both. `block: true` (or the map's `block` list of floor tags) makes deep water, lava or pits stop walkers (jumping bodies pass over); `walkable(cx, cy)`, `block(cx, cy, on)` (a bridge appears). FlowField paths go around blocked cells and follow `block` and `set` at their next `update`.\n- `find(tag)` / `findAll(tag)` give `{ x, y, z, cx, cy }`. Also `cell(cx, cy)`, `set(cx, cy, id)` (open doors), `toCell(x, y)`, `center(cx, cy)`, `heightAt(x, y)`, `floorAt(x, y)`, `groundAt(x, y, r, z)`, `collide(body)`, `los(x0, y0, x1, y1)` (ground only), `bounds(view)` (`{ x0, y0, x1, y1 }`, buffer pixels), `drawFloor(r)`, `queueWalls(r)`.\n\n**Heights** (collision, standing, sight, reach and navigation share one rule): a body's `z` is its feet; a cell's top is `map.height(cx, cy)` (0 = floor); a body stands on the highest top within `z + 2`. Eyes at `z + E.HEIGHTS.eye` (30) see a target at `z + E.HEIGHTS.chest` (22); a body's own `eye` / `chest` override them (crouching). Same level: `|dz| <= 8`. On a TileMap (`dir` = an angle or `[dx, dy]`): `ray(a, b, { eye, target })` → `{ clear, t, x, y, z }`, `sight(a, b)`, `standable(x, y, z, r)`, `ledge(from, dir)` → `{ x, y, z, rise, facing, edge }` (climb), `landing(from, dir)` → `{ x, y, z, d }` (a jump across a gap), `drop(from, dir)` → `{ x, y, z, fall }`, `arcClear(a, b, apex, r)`, `pick(sx, sy)` → `{ cx, cy, z, face }` (the cell under a screen point: `input.clicked()`, any view and turn). Helpers: `E.sameLevel(a, b)`, `E.targets(from, list, { range, arc, dz, sight: map })` → `[{ target, d, dz, angle }]` nearest first, `E.inArc(..., dz)`. `new E.FlowField(map, { climb, drop, jump })` paths over roofs, between levels and across gaps.\n\n**PlatformMap** (side-scrollers; 2.5D in tilted views): tiles on the x/z plane, top row first.\n- `new E.PlatformMap({ rows, legend, types })`. `types[id] = { kind, style, side, top, line, mat }` (`mat`: any material for a solid tile's face). Example: `rows: ['      ?    ', '   ===     ', '@  g   ^^  ', '###########']`, `legend: { '#': 1, '=': 2, '?': 3, '^': 4, '@': 'hero', 'g': 'walker' }`, `types: { 1: { style: 'ground', side: '#8a5a32' }, 2: { kind: 'oneway' }, 3: { style: 'bonus', side: '#e8a830' }, 4: { kind: 'hazard' } }`. Kinds: `'solid'` (default), `'oneway'` (jump up through), `'ladder'`, `'slope'` (`dir: 1` rises to the right, `-1` to the left; `from` / `to` heights 0..1 for gentle slopes), `'hazard'` (spikes, lava), `'deco'`, `'back'` (background wall). Styles: `'stone'` (`moss`) `'brick' 'wood' 'metal' 'ground'` (`flower`) `'block' 'pipe' 'bonus' 'plank' 'spikes' 'ladder' 'liquid' 'plain'`.\n- Spawns: `find(tag)` gives `{ x, z }` with z = the bottom of that cell (feet). Standing on the ground means z = the top of the floor tiles (`level.groundBelow(x, z)`, which returns `null` over a pit), not z = 0. `cell(cx, cz)` / `set(cx, cz, id)` count cz from the bottom row. `slopeZ(cx, cz, x)`, `touching(body, 'hazard')`, `cellsTouching(body, kind)`, `groundBelow(x, z)`, `solidAt(x, z)`, `move(body, dt, solids)`, `bounds(view)`, `draw(r)` (call first, after `r.sky`), `width`, `height`.\n\n## Movement and physics\n**Platformer** (side-scroller character): `const hero = new E.Platformer({ x, z, w: 8, h: 22, run: 95, jump: 285, gravity: 800, airJumps: 0, wallJump: false, dash: 0 })`.\n- Each update: `hero.update(dt, level, game.input, movingPlatforms)`. For enemies pass `{ x: -1..1, jump, jumpPressed, up, down, dash }` instead of the input.\n- Read: `onGround`, `jumped`, `landed`, `facing` (1 or -1), `air`, `climbing`, `hitWall`, `hitCeiling`, `bumped` (`{ cx, cz, id }` of a block hit from below). Methods: `knock(dir)`, `rigState(extra)` (feed it to `rig.update`).\n- Built in: coyote time, jump buffering, variable jump height (let go early for a short hop), slopes and small steps (sticks to the ground going down), ladders (up / down), drop through one-way tiles (down + jump), optional double jump, wall jump and dash.\n- Further moves, each on request: `crouch` (down: half as tall, it crawls), `ledge` (catches a ledge falling past it; up climbs), `wallCling`, `momentum` (slopes, a roll, a charged dash); tile kinds `'water'` (it swims), `'rope'` (up grabs it), `'bars'` (it hangs and travels), grip `friction` (ice .15), `carry` (a conveyor), `bounce` (a spring), `crumble` and `respawn` (`level.update(dt)` each step); `hero.swingFrom(x, z)` (a grapple: a pendulum, jump lets go); draw `level.drawWater(r)` after the actors. State: `crouching`, `hanging`, `clinging`, `swimming`, `onRope`, `onBars`, `swinging`, `rolling`; `rigState()` poses them.\n- Moving platforms: `{ x, z, w, h, vx, vz }` boxes you move yourself and pass as `solids`; riders are carried.\n\n**Body** (top-down / isometric / brawler): `new E.Body({ x, y, r: 5, friction: 0, bounce: 0, gravity: 700 })`. Set `vx`, `vy`, then `body.update(dt, map)`. Also `push(ix, iy, iz)` (knockback), `jump(v)`, and `onGround`, `z`, `groundZ`, `hitWall`, `landed`, `bounced` (hit the ground and bounced: dust, a thud). Walls lower than your feet are walkable, so bodies can jump onto blocks.\n\n**Mover** (third person): `const mover = new E.Mover({ x, y })`; `mover.update(dt, map, game.input)` (input `'THIRDPERSON'`) or an AI's `{ move: [dx, dy], sprint, crouch, jumpPressed }`: it sprints, sneaks, climbs, vaults, leaps gaps, hops down and rolls; `climbAny: true` climbs any wall (jump at it; up the screen is up the wall; jump leaps up, crouch lets go; `mover.wall`, `map.wall(from, dir)`), `glide: true` glides (jump again in the air; `lift`: an updraft), `staminaMax: 100` (climbing, gliding and sprinting spend `mover.stamina`); `rig.update(dt, mover.rigState())`; `mover.play('takedown', { other })`, your own `E.ACTIONS`. Stealth: `E.sees(guard, hero, { map })` → `{ seen, exposure }`, `E.hears`, `new E.Suspicion()` (`update(dt, seen, hero)` → `'calm' | 'notice' | 'search' | 'alert'`), `r.sightCone(guard, { map })`, `r.marker(x, y, z, { label })`.\n\n**Attack** (melee timing for swords, punches, kicks): `const slash = new E.Attack('slash')` (a move from `E.MOVES`, optionally with overrides: `new E.Attack('thrust', { reach: 10 })`) or a spec `{ a0, a1, z0, z1, reach, wind, active, recover }`. `if (input.buffered('attack') && slash.start()) input.consume('attack')`; `slash.update(dt)` (returns the phase that just began); `slash.hits(enemies, e => E.inArc(hero, facing, e, 22, 1.4), e => {...})` hits each target once per swing during `'active'` (moves wait until `hitAt: .35` of the swing, so hit-stop freezes the strike, not the wind-up); `rig.update(dt, { ..., attack: slash.state })`. Also `busy`, `active`, `cancel()`. **Combo**: `const combo = new E.Combo(['jab', 'cross', 'hook', 'uppercut'], { window: .3 })` (names, specs or Attacks); `combo.press()` starts or chains the next hit; `update`, `hits`, `state`, `step` work the same. **Knockback**: `E.knockback(attacker, target, 160, up)` pushes a Body (or anything with vx / vy) away.\n\n**Bullets**: `const shots = new E.Bullets(game, { plane: 'ground' | 'side' })`; `shots.fire({ x, y, z, vx, vy, vz, r: 2, team: 'player', color, life, dmg, pierce, sprite })`; `shots.burst(base, E.pattern.spread(angle, n, arc, speed))`; `shots.update(dt, map)`; `shots.hit(targets, (b, t) => {...}, 'player')`; `shots.draw(r)`; `shots.clear(team)`. Patterns: `E.pattern.dir(angle, speed)`, `aim(a, b, speed)`, `aimSide(a, b, speed)`, `spread(angle, n, arc, speed)`, `ring(n, speed, offset)`. In side view the second number of a pattern velocity is vz.\n\n**Helpers**: `E.dist(a, b)`, `E.angleTo(a, b)`, `E.arc(a, b, gravity, { apex | time | speed })` → `{ vx, vy, vz, t }` (a throw that lands at b: a lob, a grenade), `E.overlap(a, b)` (circles x, y, r), `E.overlapBox(a, b)` (side boxes x center, z feet, w, h), `E.inArc(a, facing, b, range, halfAngle, dz)` (melee cone; `dz` limits the height difference), `E.rand(a, b)`, `E.randInt(a, b)`, `E.pick(list)`, `E.chance(p)`, `E.prune(list, fn)`, `E.store.get(key, fallback)` / `set(key, value)` (save data; slots: `game.saves`), `new E.SpatialHash(32)` (`build(list)`, `near(x, y, r, fn)`), `new E.FlowField(map)` (`update(tx, ty)` or `update([[x, y], ...])`: the nearest; `dir(x, y, tx, ty)` walks around walls and `map.solid` shapes), math `clamp lerp approach ease.* angDiff approachAng smoothDamp rng(seed) noise2 hex shade mix`; `E.version` (the release) and `E.versionLabel()` ('v0.7.0 · a1b2c3d 2026-10-07': show it on a title or a debug screen).\n\n## Characters\n**Humanoid** (knights, heroes, soldiers, zombies): `new E.Humanoid({ size: 1.3, build: 'chibi' (default) | 'heroic' (tall) | 'bulky' (brawlers, bosses) | 'skeleton' (tint with colors.bone), weapon: 'sword' (the default) | 'gun' | 'staff' | null (fists) | a game's own (`E.Humanoid.weapon(id, { length, rest, draw(w) })`; `.hat(id, draw)`, `.pose(id, (J, w) => ...)`; `draw: { under, over }`; state `tilt`, `roll`), outfit: 'shirt' | 'tunic' | 'robe' | 'coat', hair: 'short' | 'spiky' | 'long' | 'ponytail' | 'bald', hat: 'cap' | 'pointed' | 'helmet' | 'band' | 'crown' (or { style, color }), sleeves: 'short' | 'long' | 'none', armor, hood (in colors.hair), cape: { len: 6, width: 5, seg: 2.5 }, eyeGlow, hunch, lean, style: 'hd' (default) | 'classic' (stick figures for huge crowds), colors: { skin, hair, cloth, coat, pants, boot, belt, trim, glove, cape, capeIn, metal, plate, hilt, eye, iris } })` (`metal` colors the weapon, `plate` the armor, defaulting to `metal`).\n- `rig.update(dt, { x, y, z, vx, vy, facing, dash, hurt, air, point, aim, attack })`. `facing` is an angle (side view: 0 = right, `Math.PI` = left). `air: true` tucks the legs for jumps; `point: true` holds a gun forward; `aim` tilts it (radians, + = up: `aim: .8` shoots diagonally up, `Math.PI / 2` straight up).\n- **Moves** (`E.MOVES`, use them instead of hand-made specs; every one has anticipation, a committed strike with lunge / step / lean / twist, follow-through and a clean return to the stance, on every build and in every view):\n  - blades and clubs: `slash backslash overhead rising thrust spin plunge twohand`;\n  - fists: `jab` (left hand) `cross hook uppercut haymaker elbow`;\n  - kicks: `kick roundhouse sweep flyingkick knee axekick`;\n  - other: `cast` (both hands) `throw bash claw`.\n  Give each character its own set (a knight: `overhead`, `thrust`, `spin`; a mage: `cast`; a monk: `jab`, `cross`, `roundhouse`; a boss: `haymaker`, `sweep`). `E.move('uppercut', .5)` is the attack state of any move at any moment (previews, cutscenes).\n- `attack: { spec, phase: 'wind' | 'active' | 'recover', u: 0..1 }`, spec `{ a0, a1, z0, z1, reach, r0, r1, hand, rel, blade, spin, kick, plane, lunge, hop, crouch, lean, twist, hold }`. Angles are relative to facing (+ = right hand side). `rel: true`: heights relative to the shoulder and reach scaled by arm length (kick heights as a share of hip height). `r0`/`r1`: reach that extends (thrusts, jabs). `hand: 'L' | 'both'`. In side views horizontal swings turn into the screen plane (a Castlevania chop) by themselves; `plane: 'side' | 'ground'` (or the rig option `swingPlane`) chooses. `lunge` steps into the strike (body motion in local units, clamped to -4..5; to move the character itself, add speed to your body), `hop` lifts the body, `crouch` dips in the wind-up, `hold` is how long the end pose holds (share of recover). You time the phases.\n- In steep ground views (threequarter) rigs and Blobs are drawn from a lower, sprite-like angle so faces show, like SNES RPG sprites (`charView: false` turns it off for one rig, `E.style.charPitch = false` for all).\n- Faces (eyes with catch-lights, brows, mouth), a cheated 3/4 turn toward the camera in side views (`cheat: .5`, 0 turns it off) and hair layers are automatic. `face: { eyes: 'big' (anime / Mana style), bangs: 0..1 }`.\n- Poses: `rig.update(dt, { ..., pose: 'cheer' | 'cast' | 'guard' | 'kneel' | 'crouch' | 'wave' | 'hips' | 'down' })` (they blend in and out), `'block'` (weapon upright across the body), `'die'` (a stagger, then the body topples), `expr: 'smile' | 'shout' | 'angry' | 'wince'` (faces and portraits), `run: 0..1` (run in place), or `down: 0..1` to lie a defeated body flat. `stance: 'guard'` keeps fists up while walking (brawlers; the free hand guards the chin during punches), `stance: 'ready'` holds the weapon forward. `climb: true` with `vz` climbs a ladder hand over hand (`Platformer.rigState()` passes both). Traversal: `crouch` (a sneaking gait), `sprint` (a lean), `hang` with `hangZ` (hands on an edge that high above the feet), `flip: 0..1` (a roll), `land: k` (a heavy landing); `mover.rigState()` sets them. Every wind-up starts from the rig's current pose, so chained hits and hand changes never snap. Idle rigs breathe and shift their weight by themselves.\n- `rig.draw(g, ox, oy, view)` inside `r.actor`, `rig.drawSmear(r)` (a glowing trail along the real blade, fist or foot path, in every view), `rig.debug(r)` (skeleton), `rig.kick(v)` (squash and stretch), `rig.hand()` and `rig.tip()` (world points to spawn bullets from), `rig.worldOffset(p)` (where a point in the rig's own frame, such as a joint in `rig.J`, sits from its feet: to draw or spawn at any joint), `rig.lastView` (the view it last drew with), `rig.solvePose()` (sets `rig.J` from its state each step: wrap it on one rig to move joints).\n**Blob** (slimes, rabbites, bats, imps, round monsters): `new E.Blob({ R: 6, colors: { dk, base, lt, spec, eye, pupil }, ears: 'rabbit' | 'cat', horns: true, wings: true, feet: true, tail: true, mouth: true | 'fangs', face: 'front' })`, `update(dt, { squash: -0.4..0.4, look: [dx, dy], squint, walk: 0..1, flap: 0..1 (wing speed; 0 folds them), hang: true (roost upside down) })`, `kick(v)`, `draw(g, ox, oy, view)`. Mix the parts for a bestiary: `wings` + `mouth: 'fangs'` is a bat, `ears: 'rabbit'` + `feet` a Mana rabbite, `horns` + `tail` an imp.\n\n## Effects and lighting\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
