{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_21","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '1184,1235p' B-17-Cross-Channel-Chaos-B-17-Bomber-gpt-6.1-sol-ultra-20261106-043517/vendor/engine/dist/handoff/API-INDEX.md && sed -n '9415,9510p' B-17-Cross-Channel-Chaos-B-17-Bomber-gpt-6.1-sol-ultra-20261106-043517/vendor/engine/engine/my-3d2dge.js && sed -n '9680,9785p' B-17-Cross-Channel-Chaos-B-17-Bomber-gpt-6.1-sol-ultra-20261106-043517/vendor/engine/engine/my-3d2dge.js && sed -n '3087,3140p' B-17-Cross-Channel-Chaos-B-17-Bomber-gpt-6.1-sol-ultra-20261106-043517/vendor/engine/engine/my-3d2dge.js\"","aggregated_output":"## 21d. Shell\n\n- `new E.Shell(game, o = {}) → shell`: new E.Shell(game, { theme, screens: { name: spec }, settings: { items, onChange(settings, key) }, store: 'shell-settings', meters: .125, standard: true }): an HTML interface over the game (see the section's header)\n- `new E.Shell({ theme })`: CSS variables (ink, paper, accent, muted, danger, line, font: a family, titleFont), and scale: the whole interface that many times (a number, or a function of the window) for a TV across a room; tv: true picks one by the window's width (14 px text at 875 px, up to 30 at 1,875)\n- `new E.Shell({ screens })`: specs ui.show(name) starts from (the pause screen follows game.paused; screens: { pause: false } leaves it out)\n- `new E.Shell({ settings })`: settings.items: the game's own settings, { key, label, type: 'toggle' | 'slider' | 'select', min, max, step, options, value } (kept in game.settings, beside the standard ones)\n- `new E.Shell({ store, meters })`: store: where an older version saved them; meters: meters per world unit for distances\n- `new E.Shell({ standard })`: false leaves out the standard menu (the pause screen's Settings, Controls, Full screen and Quit, and the settings' groups)\n- `shell.back()` †: what cancel does: the screen's own back(), or close it (back to the screen under it; closing the pause screen resumes)\n- `shell.dispose()` †: take its elements away and let go of the game (game.dispose() does it)\n- `shell.hide()` †: close every screen (and resume, when the menu paused the game)\n- `shell.hud(st = {})` †: the HUD, from this step's state (call it every step; a piece left out is hidden, and only what changed is redrawn)\n- `shell.hud({ objective })` †: { step: '01 / 04', title, text, at: { x, y, z }, from: hero } (the distance in meters, and above or below)\n- `shell.hud({ status, place, tip })` †: status: 'UNSEEN' or { text, color }; place: 'The Old Harbour'; tip: 'text' or { title, text }\n- `shell.hud({ bars, counts })` †: bars: [{ label, value, max, kind: 'bar' | 'pips', color }] (health, stamina, a meter); counts: [[label, value]]\n- `shell.hud({ prompt })` †: { key: 'E' (or act: 'interact': its key on the player's device), label, hint, progress: 0..1 }\n- `shell.hud({ keys, buttons })` †: keys: [['WASD', 'Move'], ...] (hidden on touch screens); buttons: [[label, fn or action]] (top right: pause and map where there is no Escape key)\n- `shell.hud({ minimap })` †: { map, at (with facing), markers: [{ x, y, kind: 'dot' | 'diamond' | 'ring' | 'cross', color }], onClick(x, y) (the world point clicked), fog (an E.Fog: unseen cells black, seen ones dim), camera: true (the ground the screen shows) }\n- `shell.screen` †: the name of the open screen ('pause', 'settings', 'controls', ...), or null while the game plays\n- `shell.settings` †: the player's settings: game.settings (the standard ones and the game's own, by key)\n- `shell.show(name, spec = {})` †: open a screen: 'title' | 'pause' | 'settings' | 'help' | 'results' | 'map' or a name of your own, from spec over o.screens[name]. A spec: { kicker, title, text (strings or functions), actions: [[label, fn] or { label, fn, act, primary, disabled }], back (fn for cancel), rows: ['glyphs', 'invertY', '#A heading'] (settings' rows, changed as on the settings screen) }. From another screen it stacks (back() returns); shown again, it updates (the new spec over the old). 'settings' takes its items\n- `shell.show('title')` †: { name, subtitle, meta: [...], footer }\n- `shell.show('help')` †: { keys: [[key, what]], sections: [[heading, text]] }\n- `shell.show('results')` †: { emblem, stats: [[value, label]], medals: [[label, earned]] }\n- `shell.show('map')` †: { map, at, markers (a list or a function), labels: [[text, x, y]], onPick(x, y) }\n- `shell.toast(title, text = '', seconds = 4)` †: a message that slides in at the top for a few seconds\n- `shell.tutorial(title, text = '', seconds = 15)` †: a tutorial card (bottom left, dismissable) for some seconds; tutorial(null) takes it away\n- `shell.root = null` †: game: the game it is over; o: its options; root: its DOM element (null in a headless game)\n\n## 22. Gpu lighting (webgpu)\n\n- `game.gpu.active(view)` †: true when it lights frames in this view (ready, enabled and a ground view)\n- `game.gpu.snapshot()` †: offscreen mode only: read the last frame back as a PNG data URL\n- `game.gpu.status()` †: 'loading' | 'on' | 'off' | 'unavailable'\n- `game.gpu.adapterInfo` †: the GPU's description from the browser (vendor, architecture), or null\n- `game.gpu.ambient` †: the unlit color, [r, g, b] 0..1\n- `game.gpu.bands = 6` †: how many light bands (fewer is more retro)\n- `game.gpu.enabled = true` †: false switches it off for now (and the canvas lighting with it, unless game.lights.enabled)\n- `game.gpu.failed = null` †: why it couldn't start, or null\n- `game.gpu.fallback = true` †: false keeps a frame it can't draw unlit (by default the canvas lighting stands in, game.lights.on)\n- `game.gpu.glow = .22` †: the strength of px.glow surfaces\n- `game.gpu.map = null` †: the TileMap it measures walls on\n- `game.gpu.offscreen = false` †: render into a texture instead of the page (automated tests; read it with snapshot())\n- `game.gpu.onStatus = null` †: called (gpu) when its status changes\n- `game.gpu.ready = false` †: true once the GPU is set up\n- `game.gpu.shadows = true` †: casters block light\n- `game.gpu.skipped` †: never queue more than two frames: a slow GPU drops frames instead of building up lag\n- `game.gpu.spill = 1.1` †: how far light spills past its radius\n- `game.gpu.wrap = .45` †: how far light wraps round wall corners, 0..1\n\n## 23. Sessions\n\nclass Shell {\n  /**\n   * new E.Shell(game, { theme, screens: { name: spec }, settings: { items, onChange(settings, key) }, store: 'shell-settings',\n   * meters: .125, standard: true }): an HTML interface over the game (see the section's header)\n   * - theme: CSS variables (ink, paper, accent, muted, danger, line, font: a family, titleFont), and scale: the whole\n   *   interface that many times (a number, or a function of the window) for a TV across a room; tv: true picks one by\n   *   the window's width (14 px text at 875 px, up to 30 at 1,875)\n   * - screens: specs ui.show(name) starts from (the pause screen follows game.paused; screens: { pause: false } leaves it out)\n   * - settings: settings.items: the game's own settings, { key, label, type: 'toggle' | 'slider' | 'select', min, max,\n   *   step, options, value } (kept in game.settings, beside the standard ones)\n   * - store, meters: store: where an older version saved them; meters: meters per world unit for distances\n   * - standard: false leaves out the standard menu (the pause screen's Settings, Controls, Full screen and Quit, and the\n   *   settings' groups)\n   */\n  constructor(game, o = {}) {\n    if (game.shell && game.shell._sys && !o.system) game.shell.dispose();   // the game's own shell takes over from the engine's\n    /** game: the game it is over; o: its options; root: its DOM element (null in a headless game) */\n    this._game = game; this._o = o; this.root = null; this._stack = []; this._keep = new Set(); this._held = new Set(); this._last = {};\n    this._sys = !!o.system; this._std = o.standard !== false && game.o.menu !== false;\n    const old = store.get(o.store || 'shell-settings', null) || {}, S = game.settings;   // (settings saved by an older version are kept)\n    for (const it of this._items()) if (!S.spec(it.key)) { if (S._raw[it.key] === undefined && old[it.key] !== undefined) S._raw[it.key] = old[it.key]; S.define(Object.assign({ group: 'Game' }, it)); }\n    for (const k of ['sound', 'volume', 'motion']) if (S._raw[k] === undefined && old[k] !== undefined && this._items().some(it => it.key === k)) S.set(k, old[k]);\n    if (o.settings && o.settings.onChange) S.onChange = k => o.settings.onChange(S, k);\n    game.shell = this;\n    if (!this._sys && this._pauseSpec()) game.pauseOverlay = false;\n    if (game.headless || typeof document === 'undefined') return;\n    // rebinding: the next key or mouse button goes to the action being bound (before the game's own listeners see it)\n    const signal = game._abort ? game._abort.signal : undefined;\n    addEventListener('keydown', e => { const c = this._cap; if (!c) return; e.preventDefault(); e.stopImmediatePropagation(); if (e.code === 'Escape') this._capEnd('Not changed.'); else if (c.device === 'keys' && !e.repeat) this._capBind(e.code); }, { capture: true, signal });\n    addEventListener('pointerdown', e => { const c = this._cap; if (!c || c.device !== 'keys' || e.pointerType !== 'mouse') return; e.preventDefault(); e.stopImmediatePropagation(); this._capBind('Mouse' + e.button); }, { capture: true, signal });\n    addEventListener('wheel', e => { const c = this._cap; if (!c || c.device !== 'keys' || !e.deltaY) return; e.preventDefault(); e.stopImmediatePropagation(); this._capBind(e.deltaY < 0 ? 'WheelUp' : 'WheelDown'); }, { capture: true, signal, passive: false });\n    if (!document.getElementById('esh-css')) { const st = document.createElement('style'); st.id = 'esh-css'; st.textContent = SHELL_CSS; document.head.appendChild(st); }\n    const r = this.root = this._el('div', 'esh' + (game._corner ? ' esh-cornered' : '')), th = Object.assign({}, SHELL_THEME, o.theme);   // (the top-right column starts below the corner's buttons)\n    for (const k in th) r.style.setProperty('--' + (k === 'titleFont' ? 'title' : k), th[k]);\n    if (th.font && /\\d|\\b(bold|italic|normal|oblique)\\b/.test(th.font)) warn('shell:font', 'E.Shell theme.font is a family (\"Georgia, serif\"), not a CSS shorthand (\"' + th.font + '\"): the size comes from theme.scale');\n    const K = th.scale !== undefined ? th.scale : o.tv ? () => clamp(innerWidth * .016, 18, 30) / 14 : 1;   // (for ten feet: the whole interface that many times, still filling the window)\n    if (K !== 1) { const fit = () => { const k = Math.max(.25, +(typeof K === 'function' ? K(window) : K) || 1); Object.assign(r.style, { transform: 'scale(' + k + ')', transformOrigin: '0 0', inset: 'auto', left: '0', top: '0', width: 100 / k + 'vw', height: 100 / k + 'vh' }); }; fit(); addEventListener('resize', fit, { signal }); }\n    const host = document.body; host.appendChild(r);\n    const E2 = (cls, parent = r, tag = 'div') => { const e = this._el(tag, cls); e.hidden = true; parent.appendChild(e); return e; };\n    const col = this._el('div', 'esh-col'); r.appendChild(col);\n    /** the HUD's elements, by piece (hb, obj, vit, toast, tut, pr, tip, place, mini, keys) and the screen layer (scr) */\n    this._els = { hb: E2('esh-hb', col), obj: E2('esh-obj esh-pan'), vit: E2('esh-vit esh-pan', col), place: E2('esh-place', col), tip: E2('esh-tip esh-pan'), pr: E2('esh-pr esh-pan'), keys: E2('esh-keys'),\n      tut: E2('esh-tut esh-pan'), mini: E2('esh-mini', r, 'canvas'), toast: E2('esh-toast esh-pan'), scr: this._el('div', '') };\n    r.appendChild(this._els.scr); this._els.toast.hidden = false;\n    const mini = this._els.mini; mini.width = 176; mini.height = 158;\n    mini.onclick = e => { const m = this._miniLast, X = mini._xf; if (!m || !m.onClick) return; const rc = mini.getBoundingClientRect(), u = (e.clientX - rc.left) * mini.width / (rc.width || 1), v = (e.clientY - rc.top) * mini.height / (rc.height || 1); m.onClick(X ? (u - X.ox) / X.k : 0, X ? (v - X.oy) / X.k : 0); };   // (the world point clicked: a strategy game's camera goes there)\n  }\n  /** the name of the open screen ('pause', 'settings', 'controls', ...), or null while the game plays */\n  get screen() { const t = this._stack[this._stack.length - 1]; return t ? t.name : null; }\n  /** the player's settings: game.settings (the standard ones and the game's own, by key) */\n  get settings() { return this._game.settings; }\n  /** the pause screen's spec ({} for the standard one), or null without one */\n  _pauseSpec() { const sc = this._o.screens; return sc && 'pause' in sc ? sc.pause || null : this._std ? {} : null; }\n  /** does this shell give the standard menu (the corner's menu button and game.menu() open it)? */\n  _menu() { return this._std; }\n  /** open a screen: 'title' | 'pause' | 'settings' | 'help' | 'results' | 'map' or a name of your own, from spec over\n   *  o.screens[name]. A spec: { kicker, title, text (strings or functions), actions: [[label, fn] or { label, fn, act,\n   *  primary, disabled }], back (fn for cancel), rows: ['glyphs', 'invertY', '#A heading'] (settings' rows, changed as on\n   *  the settings screen) }. From another screen it stacks (back() returns); shown again, it updates\n   *  (the new spec over the old). 'settings' takes its items\n   *  - 'title': { name, subtitle, meta: [...], footer }\n   *  - 'help': { keys: [[key, what]], sections: [[heading, text]] }\n   *  - 'results': { emblem, stats: [[value, label]], medals: [[label, earned]] }\n   *  - 'map': { map, at, markers (a list or a function), labels: [[text, x, y]], onPick(x, y) } */\n  show(name, spec = {}) {\n    const top = this._stack[this._stack.length - 1], again = top && top.name === name, s = Object.assign({}, this._o.screens && this._o.screens[name], again ? top.s : null, spec);\n    if (again) this._stack.pop();   // the same screen again: updated in place\n    else { if (top) top.focus = this._focusAt(); this._status = ''; }   // (the focus comes back here when the new screen closes)\n    this._stack.push({ name, s, focus: again ? top.focus : undefined }); this._capEnd(); this._render(); return this;\n  }\n  /** what cancel does: the screen's own back(), or close it (back to the screen under it; closing the pause screen resumes) */\n  back() {\n    const top = this._stack[this._stack.length - 1]; if (!top) return this;\n    if (top.s.back) { top.s.back(); return this; }\n    this._stack.pop(); this._capEnd(); if (top.name === 'pause') this._game.resume();\n    this._closed(); this._render(); return this;\n  }\n  /** close every screen (and resume, when the menu paused the game) */\n  hide() { const p = this._stack.some(t => t.name === 'pause'); this._stack.length = 0; this._capEnd(); if (p) this._game.resume(); this._closed(); this._render(); return this; }\n  /** the last screen closed: a game the menu paused (a title under its settings) goes on */\n  _closed() { if (!this._stack.length && this._ownPause) { this._ownPause = false; this._game.resume(); } }\n  /** which focusable element of the open screen has the focus (its index), or -1 */\n  _focusAt() { if (!this.root) return -1; const all = this._focusables(); return all.indexOf(document.activeElement); }\n  _focusables() { return [...this._els.scr.querySelectorAll('.esh-sh button:not(:disabled), .esh-sh input:not(:disabled)')]; }\n  /** close the menu: every screen over the title (a game's own title screen stays), resuming a game the menu paused */\n  _close() { const i = this._stack.findIndex(t => t.name === 'title'); if (i < 0) return this.hide(); this._stack.length = i + 1; this._capEnd(); this._render(); return this; }\n  /** a close or back button over the screen (an icon, 44 px; the keys have Escape and Start, so it takes no focus) */\n  _navBtn(cls, label, d, fn) {\n    const b = this._el('button', 'esh-nav ' + cls); b.type = 'button'; b.tabIndex = -1; b.setAttribute('aria-label', label); b.title = label; b.innerHTML = cornerIcon(d);\n    b.onclick = e => { e.stopPropagation(); fn(); }; return b;\n  }\n  /** a sideways swipe on a screen goes back: the panel follows the finger and goes back past 70 px (a slider keeps its own) */\n  _swipe(sh, box, title) {\n    if (title) return; let s0 = null, swiped = false;\n    const end = e => { if (!s0 || e.pointerId !== s0.id) return; const dx = e.clientX - s0.x, go = s0.on && Math.abs(dx) > 70 && e.type === 'pointerup'; swiped = s0.on; s0 = null;\n      box.classList.add('esh-sw'); box.style.transform = go ? 'translateX(' + Math.sign(dx) * 110 + '%)' : ''; box.style.opacity = go ? '0' : '';\n    const I = this._ctlI(), r = I.rebind(c.a, c.device, code), names = I.names || {}, nm = a => typeof names[a] === 'string' ? names[a] : actionName(a);\n    if (r === 'reserved') { this._status = I.codeLabel(code) + ' is kept for the menus. Choose another, or press Escape.'; this._render(); return; }\n    if (r) { this._status = I.codeLabel(code) + ' is already ' + nm(r) + '. Rebind ' + nm(r) + ' first, or choose another.'; this._render(); return; }\n    this._capEnd(nm(c.a) + ': ' + I.codeLabel(code) + '. Saved.');\n  }\n  /** stop listening for a new binding (msg: what the status line says) */\n  _capEnd(msg) { if (!this._cap) { if (msg !== undefined) this._status = msg; return; } this._cap = null; this._status = msg || ''; this._ctlI().clear(); this._render(); }\n  /** a button: [label, fn] or { label, fn, act, primary, disabled } */\n  _btn(a, i, pri = true) {\n    const b = Array.isArray(a) ? { label: a[0], fn: a[1] } : a, e = this._el('button', b.primary || (b.primary === undefined && i === 0 && pri) ? 'pri' : '', b.label);\n    e.disabled = !!b.disabled;\n    if (b.down) {   // (a press, timed: the event's own time, not the click's after the finger lifts)\n      e.onpointerdown = ev => { ev.preventDefault(); b.down(ev.timeStamp); };\n      e.onkeydown = ev => { if ((ev.key === ' ' || ev.key === 'Enter') && !ev.repeat) { ev.preventDefault(); b.down(ev.timeStamp); } };\n    } else e.onclick = () => { if (b.fn) b.fn(); else if (b.act) { this._game.input.tap(b.act); this._held.add(b.act); } };\n    return e;\n  }\n  /** the audio offset's calibration screen: clicks on the beat, a Tap button (or Space) on each one heard; after eight\n   *  the offset found, kept with Keep it */\n  _calibrate(key) {\n    const K = this._game.audio.calibrate(), close = () => { K.stop(); this.back(); };\n    this.show('calibrate', { kicker: 'Sound', title: 'Audio offset', back: close,\n      text: () => K.done ? 'Your sound comes ' + K.result + ' ms after the beat. Keep it, or tap on to measure again.' : 'Tap on each click you hear, in time with it, not before (' + K.taps + ' of 8). The higher click starts each bar.',\n      actions: () => [{ label: 'Tap', primary: true, down: t => { K.tap(t); this.show('calibrate', {}); } }, { label: 'Keep it', disabled: !K.done, fn: () => { this._game.settings.set(key, K.result); close(); } }, ['Cancel', close]] });\n  }\n  /** build the open screen */\n  _render() {\n    if (!this.root) return;\n    const scr = this._els.scr, top = this._stack[this._stack.length - 1];\n    if (!top) { scr.replaceChildren(); return; }\n    for (const k of ['hb', 'obj', 'vit', 'place', 'tip', 'pr', 'keys', 'mini']) { this._els[k].hidden = true; this._last[k] = null; }   // the HUD hides under a screen (a paused game calls no hud())\n    const { name, s } = top, v = x => typeof x === 'function' ? x() : x, title = name === 'title';\n    const sh = this._el('div', 'esh-sh' + (title ? ' esh-ttl' : '')), box = this._el('div', title ? '' : 'esh-pan esh-mod' + (name === 'map' ? ' esh-wide' : ''));\n    sh.appendChild(box); sh.setAttribute('role', 'dialog'); sh.setAttribute('aria-label', v(s.title || s.name) || name);\n    const add = (...c) => box.append(...c.filter(Boolean));\n    add(s.emblem && this._el('div', 'esh-emb', s.emblem), s.kicker && this._el('div', 'esh-k', v(s.kicker)));\n    if (title) add(this._el('h1', '', v(s.name || s.title)), s.subtitle && this._el('div', 'esh-sub', v(s.subtitle)));\n    else add(this._el('h2', '', v(s.title) || { pause: this._game._players && this._game._players.length > 1 && this._game.pausedBy ? 'Paused by P' + this._game.pausedBy : 'Paused', settings: 'Settings', controls: 'Controls', help: 'Help', map: 'Map' }[name] || ''));   // (several players: who paused)\n    add(v(s.text) && this._el('p', title ? '' : 'esh-m', v(s.text)));\n    for (const key of v(s.rows) || []) add(key[0] === '#' ? this._el('div', 'esh-k esh-sec', key.slice(1)) : this._row(key));   // (setting rows on a screen of the game's own: '#' a heading)\n    if (name === 'settings') this._settingsRows(add);\n    if (name === 'controls') this._controls(add);\n    if (s.keys) { const g = this._el('div', 'esh-grid'); for (const [k, w] of v(s.keys)) g.append(this._el('kbd', '', k), this._el('span', '', w)); add(g); }\n    for (const [h, t] of v(s.sections) || []) add(this._el('div', 'esh-k esh-sec', h), this._el('p', 'esh-m', t));\n    if (s.stats) { const g = this._el('div', 'esh-stats'); for (const [val, lab] of v(s.stats)) { const c = this._el('div'); c.append(this._el('b', '', val), this._el('small', '', lab)); g.appendChild(c); } add(g); }\n    if (s.medals) { const g = this._el('div'); for (const [lab, got] of v(s.medals)) g.appendChild(this._el('span', 'esh-med' + (got ? '' : ' off'), (got ? '✓ ' : '') + lab)); add(g); }\n    if (name === 'map' && s.map) {\n      const cv = this._el('canvas', 'esh-map'); cv.width = 720; cv.height = Math.round(720 * s.map.h / s.map.w); this._map(cv, s, true); add(cv);\n      if (s.onPick) cv.onclick = e => { const b = cv.getBoundingClientRect(), t = cv._xf, x = ((e.clientX - b.left) * cv.width / b.width - t.ox) / t.k, y = ((e.clientY - b.top) * cv.height / b.height - t.oy) / t.k; s.onPick(x, y); this._map(cv, s, true); };\n    }\n    const acts = (name === 'pause' ? [['Resume', () => this.hide()]] : []).concat(v(s.actions) || [], name === 'pause' && this._std && v(this._game.o.menu && this._game.o.menu.items) || []).filter(Boolean);\n    if (name === 'pause') this._pauseActs(acts);\n    if (name === 'settings' && this._std) acts.push(['Controls', () => this.show('controls')], ['Restore defaults', () => { for (const g of SHELL_GROUPS.concat('Game')) this._game.settings.reset(g); this.show('settings'); }]);\n    if (name === 'controls') acts.push(['Restore defaults', () => { this._ctlI().resetBindings(); this._game.settings.reset('Controller'); this._game.settings.reset('Touch'); this._status = 'Every control is back to its default.'; this.show('controls'); }]);\n    if (!acts.length && !title || name === 'settings' || name === 'controls') acts.push(['Back', () => this.back()]);\n    const btns = this._el('div', 'esh-btns'), lists = name === 'settings' || name === 'controls'; acts.forEach((a, i) => btns.appendChild(this._btn(a, i, !lists))); add(btns);\n    if (s.meta) { const g = this._el('div', 'esh-tags'); for (const t of v(s.meta)) g.appendChild(this._el('span', '', t)); add(g); }\n    add(s.footer && this._el('div', 'esh-m', v(s.footer)));\n    const keep = top.focus !== undefined ? top.focus : this._shown === top ? this._focusAt() : -1; this._shown = top;   // (redrawn in place: the focus stays where it was)\n    // the way out, always in sight: close at the top right (where the menu button was), back at the top left over another\n    // screen, and a sideways swipe goes back (a phone's edge swipe would leave the page)\n    const nav = [];\n    if (!title) nav.push(this._navBtn('x', 'Close', 'M6 6l12 12M18 6L6 18', () => this._close()));\n    if (this._stack.length > 1) nav.push(this._navBtn('bk', 'Back', 'M15 5l-7 7 7 7', () => this.back()));\n    this._swipe(sh, box, title);\n    this._els.scr.replaceChildren(sh, ...nav);\n    const all = this._focusables(), f = all[keep] || (name === 'settings' || name === 'controls' ? null : sh.querySelector('button.pri:not(:disabled)')) || all[0];\n    top.focus = undefined; if (f) { f.focus({ preventScroll: true }); if (f.scrollIntoView) f.scrollIntoView({ block: 'nearest' }); }\n  }\n  /** the standard pause screen's buttons after Resume and the game's own: Settings, Controls, Full screen, Help, Save\n   *  session (while the page is recorded: E.session), Quit */\n  _pauseActs(acts) {\n    const g = this._game, fs = g.fullscreen, M = g.o.menu || {}, quit = M.quit === false ? null : M.quit || 'title', help = this._o.screens && this._o.screens.help;\n    if (this._std && HOOKS.pause) HOOKS.pause(this, acts);\n    if (this._std || this._items().length) acts.push(['Settings', () => this.show('settings')]);\n    if (!this._std) { if (help) acts.push(['Help', () => this.show('help')]); return; }\n    acts.push(['Controls', () => this.show('controls')]);\n    if (g.o.fullscreen !== false && fs.supported && !fs.standalone) acts.push([fs.on ? 'Leave full screen' : 'Full screen', () => { fs.toggle(); }]);\n    if (help) acts.push(['Help', () => this.show('help')]);\n    // a recorded page (?record=1) saves its session from the menu: a phone has no console (the share sheet, or a download).\n    // Its replay has the button too (doing nothing): the recorded tap on it lands on it, not on the next one (Quit)\n    if (E.session && (E.session.recording || E.session.replaying)) acts.push(['Save session', () => { if (E.session.recording) E.session.share(); }]);\n    if (quit && g.scenes && g.scenes[quit] && g.sceneName !== quit) acts.push(['Quit to ' + (quit === 'title' ? 'title' : actionName(quit).toLowerCase()), () => this.show('confirm', { kicker: 'Quit', title: 'Leave this game?', text: 'Progress since the last save is lost.',\n      actions: [{ label: 'Keep playing', fn: () => this.back() }, { label: 'Quit', fn: () => { this.hide(); g.go(quit); } }] })]);\n  }\n  /** draw a TileMap from above: floor, roofs by height, water and grass, then markers and the body at (an arrow) */\n  _map(cv, s, large) {\n    const m = s.map, g = cv.getContext('2d'), W = cv.width, H = cv.height, T = m.T, ww = m.w * T, hh = m.h * T, pad = large ? 22 : 8;\n    const k = Math.min((W - pad * 2) / ww, (H - pad * 2) / hh), ox = (W - ww * k) / 2, oy = (H - hh * k) / 2, P = (x, y) => [ox + x * k, oy + y * k];\n    cv._xf = { k, ox, oy };\n    if (!m._shellBase || m._shellBase.v !== m.version || m._shellBase.w !== W) {   // the cells, cached until the map changes\n      const b = mkCanvas(W, H), bg = ctx2d(b); bg.fillStyle = '#121b1d'; bg.fillRect(0, 0, W, H);\n      let top = 1; for (let cy = 0; cy < m.h; cy++) for (let cx = 0; cx < m.w; cx++) top = Math.max(top, m.height(cx, cy));\n      for (let cy = 0; cy < m.h; cy++) for (let cx = 0; cx < m.w; cx++) {\n        const c = m.cell(cx, cy), tag = m.floorAt((cx + .5) * T, (cy + .5) * T);\n        bg.fillStyle = c > 0 ? mix('#4a5650', '#d2c296', m.height(cx, cy) / top) : tag === 'water' || tag === 'lava' ? (tag === 'water' ? '#1d3e56' : '#6a2a1a') : tag === 'grass' ? '#29452f' : '#1f2b2c';\n        bg.fillRect(Math.floor(ox + cx * T * k), Math.floor(oy + cy * T * k), Math.ceil(T * k), Math.ceil(T * k));\n      }\n      m._shellBase = { v: m.version, w: W, cv: b };\n    }\n    g.drawImage(m._shellBase.cv, 0, 0);\n    g.textAlign = 'center'; g.font = (large ? 12 : 7) + 'px ' + (this._o.theme && this._o.theme.font || 'sans-serif');\n    if (large) for (const [t, x, y] of s.labels || []) { g.fillStyle = '#cbbf9e'; g.fillText(t, ...P(x, y)); }\n    for (const q of (typeof s.markers === 'function' ? s.markers() : s.markers) || []) {\n      const [x, y] = P(q.x, q.y), r = (q.size || (large ? 6 : 3)); g.strokeStyle = g.fillStyle = q.color || '#ffe0a0'; g.lineWidth = large ? 2 : 1; g.beginPath();\n      if (q.kind === 'diamond') { g.moveTo(x, y - r); g.lineTo(x + r, y); g.lineTo(x, y + r); g.lineTo(x - r, y); g.closePath(); g.stroke(); }\nclass Settings {\n  /**\n   * game.settings: the player's choices, one property each (game.settings.volume), with the game's own (o.menu.settings)\n   * beside the standard ones (STANDARD_SETTINGS). Saved with E.store under 'settings:' + the game's id, with a version;\n   * on load every value is checked and a bad one falls back to its default. Where storage is blocked the game plays on\n   * with the defaults (saved: false)\n   */\n  constructor(game, own = []) {\n    const hide = (k, v) => Object.defineProperty(this, k, { value: v, writable: true });\n    hide('_g', game); hide('_specs', {}); hide('_saved', {}); hide('_key', 'settings:' + (game.o.id || (typeof location !== 'undefined' && location.pathname) || 'game'));\n    hide('saved', true);\n    /** onChange(key, value): called after every change (E.Shell's settings.onChange goes through it) */\n    hide('onChange', null);\n    const raw = store.get(this._key, null);\n    hide('_raw', raw && typeof raw === 'object' && raw.values && typeof raw.values === 'object' ? raw.values : {});   // (a newer version's values are checked like the rest)\n    if (!(raw && raw.v >= 2) && this._raw.fullscreen === false) delete this._raw.fullscreen;\n    game.input._settings = this; game.input._onBindings = b => this.set('bindings', b);\n    for (const k in STANDARD_SETTINGS) if (!(game.o.touch === 'never' && STANDARD_SETTINGS[k].group === 'Touch')) this.define(Object.assign({ key: k }, STANDARD_SETTINGS[k]));   // (touch: 'never': no Touch group)\n    for (const sp of own) this.define(sp && !sp.label && Object.prototype.hasOwnProperty.call(STANDARD_SETTINGS, sp.key) ? Object.assign({ key: sp.key }, STANDARD_SETTINGS[sp.key], sp) : sp);   // (a standard key with no label: the game's fields over the standard ones; with a label it is the game's own)\n  }\n  /** add a setting: { key, label, type: 'toggle' | 'slider' | 'select', value, min, max, step, options: [[value,\n   *  label]] or [value], help, group: 'Game', apply(game, value) }. Its saved value is loaded (when it is a valid one) and\n   *  applied; it shows on the settings screen. Returns its value */\n  define(sp) {\n    if (!sp || !sp.key || typeof sp.key !== 'string') { warn('setting', 'a setting needs a key: { key: \"hints\", label: \"Hints\", value: true }'); return undefined; }\n    if (sp.key in Settings.prototype || sp.key === 'saved' || sp.key === 'onChange' || sp.key[0] === '_') { warn('setting:' + sp.key, 'a setting cannot be called \"' + sp.key + '\" (a name the settings object uses)'); return undefined; }\n    const s = Object.assign({ group: 'Game', type: sp.options ? 'select' : typeof sp.value === 'number' ? 'slider' : typeof sp.value === 'boolean' || sp.value === undefined ? 'toggle' : 'value' }, sp);\n    this._specs[s.key] = s;\n    const saved = settingValue(s, this._raw[s.key]);\n    if (saved !== undefined) this._saved[s.key] = saved;\n    this[s.key] = saved !== undefined ? saved : this.default(s.key);\n    this._apply(s.key);\n    return this[s.key];\n  }\n  /** a setting's default value */\n  default(key) { const s = this._specs[key]; if (!s) return undefined; const v = typeof s.value === 'function' ? s.value(this._g) : s.value; return v === undefined && s.type === 'toggle' ? false : v; }\n  /** the spec a setting was defined with (its label, type, range, options), or undefined */\n  spec(key) { return this._specs[key]; }\n  /** the keys of a group's settings, in order ('Display', 'Sound', 'Comfort', 'Controller', 'Touch', 'Game'), or every key */\n  keys(group) { return Object.keys(this._specs).filter(k => !group || this._specs[k].group === group); }\n  /** change a setting: checked (a slider kept in range, a choice among its options), saved, applied, onChange told.\n   *  Returns the value kept (the old one when v is not a valid value) */\n  set(key, v) {\n    const s = this._specs[key]; if (!s) { warn('setting:' + key, 'unknown setting \"' + key + '\". Settings: ' + this.keys().join(', ')); return undefined; }\n    const ok = settingValue(s, v); if (ok === undefined) return this[key];\n    this[key] = ok; this._saved[key] = ok; this._save(); this._apply(key);\n    if (this.onChange) try { this.onChange(key, ok); } catch (e) { this._g.fail('settings.onChange', e); }\n    return ok;\n  }\n  /** put a group's settings (or all of them) back to their defaults; a game's saves are not touched */\n  reset(group) {\n    for (const k of this.keys(group)) { if (k === 'fullscreen') continue; delete this._saved[k]; this[k] = this.default(k); this._apply(k); if (this.onChange) this.onChange(k, this[k]); }\n    this._save();\n  }\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_22","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '220,430p' B-17-Cross-Channel-Chaos-B-17-Bomber-gpt-6.1-sol-ultra-20261106-043517/vendor/engine/dist/handoff/API.md\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_22","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '220,430p' B-17-Cross-Channel-Chaos-B-17-Bomber-gpt-6.1-sol-ultra-20261106-043517/vendor/engine/dist/handoff/API.md\"","aggregated_output":"## Effects and lighting\n- Particles: `game.particles.explosion(x, y, z, size)` (fireball, smoke, sparks, debris, ring, shake, sound), `fire(x, y, z, n, { size })`, `smoke(x, y, z, n, { size, color })`, `glints(x, y, z, n, color)`, `dust(x, y, z, n)`, `sparks(x, y, z, n, angle)`, `bits(x, y, z, n, colors)`, `ring(x, y, r0, r1, color, dur)`, `text(x, y, z, '12', color, { scale: 2, bounce: true })` (bouncing damage numbers), `add({ kind: 'dust' | 'spark' | 'bit' | 'ember' | 'fire' | 'smoke' | 'glint', ... })`. `explosion(x, y, z, size, { debris, freeze: false, shake: 0 })` for chains of small blasts. Side-scrollers: `particles.ground = (x, y, z) => level.groundBelow(x, z)` so sparks and debris bounce on platforms. Screen flash: `game.flash('#ffffff', .12, strength 0..1)`.\n- Lighting (step 9; every view, side-scrollers included, no WebGPU needed): `game.lights.add(x, y, z, radius, intensity, { color: '#ffa050' })` every draw. Dark areas get a smooth cool tint, lights add their own color, and emissive items (flames, sparks, bullets, `emissive: true`) stay bright. `lights.darkness` (0..1) and `lights.tint` tune it; after setting `lights.dark = [r, g, b]`, `levels` or `glow`, call `lights.refresh()`. Props with flames can light the scene: `r.prop('torch', x, y, z, { light: true })`. Lamps, street lamps, lanterns and crystals glow on their own (`haloR`, `haloColor`, `halo: false`); `cone: true` adds a light cone under a street lamp.\n- Hits: `game.hitFx(x, y, z, { power: 1, angle, damage: 12, textScale: 2, textZ: 22 })` does hit-stop, shake, an impact star, sparks, a bouncing damage number (`bounce: false` floats it) and a sound in one call; `particles.impact(x, y, z, size, color)` for the star alone.\n- GPU lighting (optional, ground views with a TileMap): `const gpu = game.enableGPU({ map })`; mark glowing things with `px.glow(g, 1)`; add `lights.caster(x, y, r, top)` and `lights.heat(x, y, z, w)`. Where it can't draw (no WebGPU, a side view) the canvas lighting stands in, with `game.lights.ambient` (`gpu.fallback = false`: unlit).\n\n## Genre playbook (NES, SNES, Genesis, N64, PS1)\n| Genre (examples) | View | Build it with | Copy slice |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Platformer (Mario, Mega Man, Sonic, Castlevania) | `side` (+ `brawler` for 2.5D) | PlatformMap, Platformer, Humanoid, sprites, Bullets `'side'` | PLATFORMER |\n| Metroidvania (Metroid, Symphony of the Night) | `side` | an `E.World` of PlatformMaps (the rooms module: doors at open edges, a slide, the explored map, gates opened by abilities, saves), a Platformer given `airJumps` and `dash` as they are found, its further moves, an arm cannon aimed eight ways (`point`, `aim`, `rig.tip()`, Bullets) | METROIDVANIA |\n| Action adventure (Zelda, Secret of Mana) | `threequarter` or `topdown` | TileMap rows, `cam.room`, Body, Humanoid + `E.Attack` sword, Dialog, `E.ui.hearts` | ADVENTURE |\n| Point-and-click adventure (Monkey Island, Day of the Tentacle, Broken Sword) | none: rooms painted in screen pixels (`r.overlay`) | `E.Click` (the click module): rooms with walk areas and holes (`E.Walkbox`), depth scale, hotspots, the nine verbs, Sierra's icons or a verb coin, an inventory, puzzles as rules; talk through `E.Story` | POINT-AND-CLICK |\n| Visual novel (Phoenix Wright, Snatcher, Clannad) | none | `E.Story` nodes and choices over a painted backdrop, `rig.drawPortrait` at size, `story.log` (the backlog), `story.auto`, `story.skip`; `game.saves` | POINT-AND-CLICK |\n| Action RPG / dungeon (Diablo, Landstalker) | `iso` | TileMap, FlowField, Body (jump onto blocks), GPU lighting | ADVENTURE |\n| Beat-'em-up (Final Fight, Streets of Rage, TMNT) | `brawler` | TileMap street strip, Body, Humanoid (`weapon: null`) + `E.Combo` punches and `kick: true` kicks, `E.knockback`, waves that lock the screen; a second player drops in (`game.allowJoin`, `cam.frame` on both) | BRAWLER |\n| Fighting (Street Fighter II, Darkstalkers) | `side` | two `E.Fighter`s in an `E.Match` (the fight module): moves with frame data, guards, throws, specials by motion (`'236'`) or charge, a meter, projectiles; `E.FightAI`, `E.FightSelect`, training | FIGHTING |\n| Shoot-'em-up (1942, Gradius, R-Type) | `overhead` (vertical, and horizontal: world x scrolls) | sprites, Bullets, `E.pattern`, a timeline of waves; horizontal: rock edges as functions of x, a power bar, options on the ship's past path, `E.Path` loops; `E.Arcade` for the continue and the table | SHOOTER (both stages) |\n| Pinball (Pinball Fantasies, Space Cadet, Devil's Crush) | a steep table view of its own (`new E.View('pinball', 'Table', 0, 62, 1, 1)`) | `E.Physics`: chains for the walls, `flipper`, `bumper`, `slingshot`, `kicker`, a ramp on a layer of its own, the ball a `bullet`; `input.zones` flip on a phone; `E.Arcade` for the score and table. Breakout and Asteroids with real collisions are its recipes | PINBALL |\n| Artillery (Worms, Scorched Earth) | `side` at a whole scale (`new E.View(id, label, 0, 0, 1, 1)`) | `E.Terrain` (`carve` the blasts, `walk` the soldiers, `ray` the shots), grenades as `E.Physics` bodies on `land.collider()`, `E.Turns`; a drag aims (`steer = 'drag'`, `drag()`, `stickOn`); a CPU tries its shots in simulation | ARTILLERY |\n| Golden-age arcade (Pac-Man, Galaga, Asteroids) | `overhead` (one fixed screen, cabinet art on the sides) | `E.Arcade` (score, lives, extra lives, turns, initials, tables, attract mode); a maze of `E.GridMover`s; moths on `E.Path`s turned by `rot`; `E.wrap` and `wrap: [w, h]` | ARCADE |\n| Twin-stick / run-and-gun (Smash TV, Contra) | `topdown` / `side` | Body or Platformer, Bullets, `weapon: 'gun'`, `point: true` | SHOOTER + ADVENTURE |\n| JRPG (Dragon Quest, Final Fantasy, EarthBound) | `threequarter` town, `brawler` battles | TileMap towns and a big world map, the story and rpg modules, Dialog with markup, `game.saves` slots | RPG |\n| Puzzle (Tetris, Dr. Mario, Puyo, Columns) | `side` (a field in screen pixels) | a cell array, a bag from `E.rng`, `input.repeat` (auto-shift), `grid.groups` (chains), `input.drag()` and `clicked()` for touch; versus: two fields, rows sent across (`game.players`) | PUZZLE |\n| Roguelike (Rogue, Mystery Dungeon, Shiren) | `threequarter` / `iso` | `E.gen` floors, a TileMap of its rows, `E.Grid.from(map)` paths and `fov`, `E.Fog`, `E.Turns` by speed, `game.tween` steps | ROGUELIKE |\n| Tactics (Final Fantasy Tactics, Tactics Ogre, Fire Emblem) | `iso`, turned a quarter | TileMap of block heights, `map.pick` under the cursor, `E.Grid.from(map, { tops: true })` reach over heights, `grid.shape`, `grid.side`, `grid.threat`, `E.Turns` charge time, `E.Story` | TACTICS |\n| Real-time strategy (Warcraft II, StarCraft, Dune II) | `iso` | `E.Strategy` (the strategy module): kinds as data, selection by click, box and group, orders, gold, building, training, fog, an AI's build order and waves; `cam.free`, `{ pick: unit }` and `r.pick`, buildings as `E.SHAPES`, E.Shell's minimap; bodies drawn `every: 3` | RTS |\n| Theme park or city sim (Theme Park, RollerCoaster Tycoon, SimCity) | `iso` | paths as floor tags walked on an `E.Grid`, agents with `E.needs` picking by `E.choose`, `E.Clock` days and light, `game.timeScale` 0 to 4, `E.overlay`, `E.tooltip`; rides as shapes stepped through angles (`params`, `facing`) | SIM |\n| 3D platformer or adventure remake (Mario 64, Ocarina, Crash) | `iso` / `threequarter` / `brawler` | TileMap blocks of different heights + Body `jump()` (z is real height); in real 3D: `E.World3D` (the 3D engine's manual), `camera.lock` | ADVENTURE; 3D ACTION, 3D PLATFORMER |\n| Survival horror (Resident Evil, Alone in the Dark) | the 3D engine's `'zones'` camera | `camera.zones` (fixed cameras by room), `camera.steer` (tank controls), `camera.lock` to aim, `world.through` doors, `world.flashlight`, fog; `E.RPG` inventory, `game.saves` | 3D HORROR |\n| First-person dungeon (Wizardry, Dungeon Master, Eye of the Beholder) | the 3D engine's `'fixed'` camera at the party's eyes | cells of 2 x 2 tiles stepped and turned a quarter at a time (tweened), `E.Grid` paths for the monsters, `E.Turns` `'atb'` (real time) or `'speed'` (turns), `E.Fog` for the automap, `world.thing('door')` gates and `world.unlock`, `rig.drawPortrait` for the party | 3D CRAWLER |\n| Rhythm (Dance Dance Revolution, PaRappa, Beatmania, Space Channel 5) | any (a highway on the overlay) | `E.Rhythm` (the rhythm module): a chart of lane strings in parts on a song's steps, judged in ms of the music clock, combo, life, grade, holds, calls a teacher plays and you answer, `rh.draw` (`arrows: true`); the songbook's songs (`E.Songbook`); lanes as `input.zones` on a phone; `audio.onBeat` moves the dancer | RHYTHM |\n| Sports (Sensible Soccer, NBA Jam) | `threequarter` / `topdown` | the ball an `E.Body` (`bounce`; curl: turn its velocity across its path), passes led to the teammate, `E.arc` for a lob, a shot's meter, formations by where the ball is, `game.allowJoin({ max: 4 })` | SPORTS |\n| Third-person stealth (Assassin's Creed, Metal Gear, Tenchu) | `iso` / `threequarter` | TileMap roofs, Mover, `E.sees`, `E.Suspicion`, FlowField `jump` | STEALTH |\n| Kart racing (Super Mario Kart, F-Zero) | Mode 7 (the mode7 module, over any view) | `E.Mode7` over a TileMap track (floor tags: grass, sand, boost), `E.Car` karts (`kart: true`: hop, drift, boost) in an `E.Race` round an `E.Path` (laps, checkpoints, drivers, items), rigs in karts as billboards, `game.splitScreen(2)` for two | KART |\n| 3D kart racing (Mario Kart 64, Crash Team Racing) | the 3D engine's `'behind'` camera | `world.track` (banked, walls, pads, `gaps` for a shortcut), `world.vehicle` karts raced by `E.Race`, split screen through `world.cameras` | 3D RACING |\n| Rail shooters (Star Fox 64, Panzer Dragoon) | the 3D engine's `'behind'` camera | `world.flyer` on rails or free in bounds, rolls (`f.rolling`) turn shots aside, `f.seek` for a charged lock, `Dialog`'s radio | 3D FLIGHT |\n| Road racing (OutRun, Pole Position, Road Rash) | the pseudo-3D road (the road module) | `E.Road` segments (curves, hills, tunnels), scenery and traffic placed on it, `curveAt` throwing the car outward, a clock and checkpoints | ROAD |\n| Top-down racing and driving (Micro Machines, RC Pro-Am, GTA) | `topdown` / `iso` | `E.Car` on a TileMap (its floor tags slow it, its walls bounce it), `E.Race` for laps and drivers, cars drawn with `px.poly` on `r.w()` corner points | KART |\n| First-person shooter (Doom, GoldenEye 007, Apex Legends) | the 3D engine's first person (or third) | a level of text rows or a terrain, `world.ray` hitscan, recoil and reloads, doors (`world.thing('door')`), raiders on `world.flow()` | 3D SHOOTER |\n| Bomberman, Frogger, Sokoban, Gauntlet, Robotron; Sonic, Prince of Persia; light guns | as the recipe says | `AI_GUIDE.md`'s Genre recipes: each on the kit closest to it | (a recipe) |\n\n**Sizes:** heroes 40-60 px tall at 320x240 (`size: 1.2-1.4`), bosses 1.8-2.4. Small things (coins, bullets, ships, pickups) are string sprites designed at 8-16 px, drawn at scale 2 if they are the player's ship. Keep hitboxes smaller than the art.\n\n**Feel numbers** (world units per second, tile = 16): walk 70-90, run 95-140, jump 250-320 with gravity 800, fall cap 330, dash 200-260, bullets 250-320 (player) and 70-120 (enemy), enemy walk 25-45. Hit feedback: `game.hitFx` (Effects).\n\n## More: animation and examples outside this card\nThe repo (github.com/michaelcrosato/my-3d2dge; any file at `https://raw.githubusercontent.com/michaelcrosato/my-3d2dge/main/<path>`) holds more to take from. Its files are large: search them and take only what the game needs. Real 3D (`E.World3D`: first person, racing, flight) is there: `engine/my-3d2dge-3d.js`.\n- **Motion clips**: 325 curated and 2,548 motion-capture takes that play on any Humanoid: find one in `src/mocap/catalogs/`, cut a small set with `tools/anim-set.mjs`, then `Mocap.drive(rig, lib)` (`AI_GUIDE.md`, Where to find more; `docs/MOCAP.md`).\n- **Objects and materials** (full engine): `r.shape('barrel', x, y, 0, { facing })` draws a still object from any view and facing, `map.solid(...)` makes it solid; `E.MATERIALS` dresses floors (`floorMat`), walls (`face`, `roof`) and platform tiles (`mat`). `docs/ASSETS.md` is the card: the format, the library, writing one and checking it with `node tools/asset-sheet.mjs`.\n- **Worked examples**: Emberdeep (`src/emberdeep/`), a whole game on this engine: 29 monster, boss and dummy bodies, 3 heroes and 30 skills, registered with `def(kind, id, spec)` (one search lists them); adapt them, they lean on the game's own helpers. `docs/CHARACTERS.md` is the recipe for a new body.\n- **Modules** (`engine/modules/<name>.js`; `modules/` in the handoff package): general systems in files of their own, each a `<script>` after the engine, its header its manual (read it there, or its section of the index). A kit carries the modules its slice names (`@modules` in its header); the full engine (`dist/my-3d2dge.js`; `my-3d2dge.js` in the handoff package) carries them all.\n  - `grid`: square and hex grids: A* paths, move ranges over heights and past allies, fields of view, `E.Fog`, groups, shapes of effect, threat maps, `E.GridMover`, `E.Turns` (speed, charge time, phases, ATB). ROGUELIKE, PUZZLE, TACTICS, ARCADE, ARTILLERY, RTS, SIM, 3D CRAWLER.\n  - `gen`: generated maps from a seed: rooms and corridors, BSP, caves, mazes, Poisson scatter, as ASCII rows a TileMap reads. ROGUELIKE, ARCADE.\n  - `fight` (the full engine only): one-on-one fighting: `E.Fighter` (frame data, hurt boxes from the rig's joints, guards, throws, cancels, juggles, specials by motion or charge, a meter, projectiles), `E.Match` (rounds, KO, the HUD, training), `E.FightAI`, `E.FightSelect`. FIGHTING.\n  - `rooms`: a world of rooms on a grid of screens (`E.World`): walking between them at open edges, the explored map (`drawMap`, or `shellMap()` for `E.Shell`), gates that abilities or keys open, saves in `E.store`. METROIDVANIA.\n  - `mode7`: the SNES's Mode 7 (`E.Mode7`): a camera over a flat floor (a TileMap's, a function's or a canvas), a turning sky, billboards far to near (rigs, sprites, shapes, your drawing), fog, `project` and `toFloor`, split screens. KART.\n  - `road`: the pseudo-3D road (`E.Road`): segments with curves and hills, lanes, rumble strips, tunnels, scenery and cars scaled by distance and hidden past a crest, the sky's parallax on curves. ROAD.\n  - `drive`: cars on the ground plane (`E.Car`: grip and slide, a kart's hop and drift boost, floor tags, walls and cars it bounces off) and races (`E.Race`: checkpoints along an `E.Path`, laps, places, drivers that pass and rubber-band, items, the HUD; the 3D engine's `world.vehicle` too). KART.\n  - `story`: dialogue as data (`E.Story`): lines with speakers and portraits, choices with conditions, flags and values, gotos, the game's events, a quest log, balloons over heads, a backlog, auto and skip; its state for a save. RPG, POINT-AND-CLICK, TACTICS.\n  - `rpg`: a role-playing game's rules (`E.RPG`): items, bags (slots or a grid of sizes), members with stats, levels and gear, status effects, a party (items used, rewards shared), shops, damage, random encounters by zone, list and card windows. RPG, 3D HORROR.\n  - `strategy` (the full engine only; needs `grid`): `E.Strategy` for real-time strategy (selection by click, box and group; queued orders; formations; production, resources, placement; fog, the minimap; an AI's build order and waves) and for sims `E.Clock` (days, the light), `E.needs` and `E.choose`, `E.overlay`, `E.tooltip`. RTS, SIM.\n  - `click` (the full engine only): point-and-click adventures (`E.Click`): painted rooms, walk areas with holes (`E.Walkbox`), depth scale, hotspots with verbs, SCUMM's nine verbs, Sierra's icons, a verb coin or two buttons, an inventory, rules as data, exits, `story`'s talk; taps on a phone. POINT-AND-CLICK.\n  - `physics`: 2D rigid bodies (`E.Physics`): circles, boxes, polygons, segments, chains and arcs; bounce, friction, sensors, layers, sleep; fast balls swept, never passing through; the same world at any refresh rate; flippers, bumpers, slingshots, kickers. PINBALL, ARTILLERY.\n  - `terrain`: destructible ground in the side plane (`E.Terrain`): carved and added by circles and polygons, the ground below a point and its normal, rays for shots, walkers on slopes, a collider for `physics`. ARTILLERY.\n  - `songs`: the songbook (`E.Songbook`): songs by mood (field, town, battle, race, horror, chase, dance ...) and jingles (stage clear, game over, level up); `get(id)`, `find(mood)`. RHYTHM.\n  - `rhythm` (the full engine only): `E.Rhythm`: charts on a song's steps, judgments in ms of the music clock, combo, score, a life gauge, grades, holds, call and response, a note highway in any direction. RHYTHM.\n  - `arcade`: the coin-op's frame: scores that float up, extra lives, two players taking turns, credits and a continue, high-score tables with initials on a letter wheel, stage cards, the attract mode (a demo, the table, the title). ARCADE, SHOOTER, PINBALL.\n- **Everything running**: https://my-3d2dge.vercel.app/labs\n\n## Before you hand the game back\n- One IIFE starting with `const E = My3D2dge` (between the markers in a single file; `game/game.js` in the handoff package). Only your game: no leftover starter menu or unused slices. No network, no libraries.\n- Title screen and game-over screen as scenes; `pausable: true` on gameplay scenes. No pause, settings, rebinding or full-screen code of your own (they're standard); prompts from `game.input.label(action)`.\n- The camera follows the player (`game.focus` every update) and shows the level; the HUD uses screen pixels, or `E.Shell`'s HTML for a modern game (the STEALTH kit; the handoff package's template).\n- Sound effects on jump, hit, pickup and death; music per scene.\n- The look target list above: backdrop, textured tiles, props, sized and dressed HD characters, effects, title font, lights. Compare your screenshots with Symphony of the Night or Metal Slug, not with NES games.\n- If you can run commands: `node tools/check.mjs game/index.html` (your page; add `#scene` to jump to a scene). It presses start, plays, cycles the views, prints how much of the screen is filled and how many colors it uses, adds look notes (flat areas, checkerboard dithering, low contrast, a thin palette), and fails on any error. Act on every look note. `node tools/filmstrip.mjs game/index.html#scene --steps \"wait:1500 press:Enter wait:800 rec:16:2 press:KeyJ\" --crop x,y,w,h` records an animation frame by frame into one contact sheet: check every attack with it (a swing must wind up, strike, and settle back without jerks or backward sweeps).\n- Animation variety: every character has its own moves from `E.MOVES` (not one shared swing), enemies telegraph with a visible wind-up, and reactions play out (hurt, knockback, `down`, victory `cheer`).\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
