{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_39","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc 'tail -40 PROGRESS.md'","aggregated_output":"# B-17 Cross Channel Chaos — build progress\n\n## Requirements and identity\n- Build `PLAN.md`, exact packaging/metadata from `TASK.md`.\n- Title drawn using Node crypto.randomInt from 50 silently authored candidates: **B-17 Cross Channel Chaos** (draw 42).\n- Dev directory: `B-17-Cross-Channel-Chaos-B-17-Bomber-gpt-6.1-sol-ultra-20261106-043517/`.\n- Root deliverables: matching `.html`, `exit-interview.json`, this progress file.\n- Native my-3d2dge engine + World3D; 1–2 crew, complete sortie, AI Hub integration, procedural audio, couch/touch/pad UI, practice/dev/attract.\n\n## Current stage\n1. Read entire task and plan; game-toolchain skill read.\n2. Downloading engine and AI Hub repositories into dev/vendor. Source research delegated.\n3. Next: pin/read contracts, prove portable native 3D, define simulation/renderer/online contracts and delegate bounded modules.\n\n## Constraints\n- Keep all generated/dev files inside own dev folder, final artifacts at root.\n- No neighboring-run inspection, fixed ports, foreign process termination, or GUI.\n- One quiet verification command, actual public-input playthrough, Hub harness scenarios, metadata from evidence.\n- Final chat and game About include Source Information, Testing Feedback, Engine Feedback, Prompt Feedback. Usage = added on import.\n\n## Verification / issues\nNot yet run. Record observed failures and critical counts here and in docs/testing.md.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_40","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"cat >> PROGRESS.md <<'EOF'\n\n## Stage update: modules built\n- Engine pinned 8ecc2f6, 0.89.1; Hub pinned 35a1047, client 1.4.0.\n- Read native handoff API and World3D manual, source research saved docs/research.md.\n- src/sim.js + content/mission.js: coupled flight/resources/stations/combat/flak/bombs/damage/mission/recovery/practice/dev.\n- src/view.js: native 3D custom bomber/harbor/cockpit/four gun cameras/sight/clouds/split, no engine fork. Default native WebGL2; software WebGPU loses device in environment (explicit diagnostic route remains).\n- src/audio.js: procedural native buses/music/gibberish; 32 OfflineAudio checks passed.\n- src/online.js: Hub host authority/8Hz live + periodic reliable checkpoint, 28 unit/integration checks passed; actual harness pending package.\n- src/ui.js + app.js: native E.Shell screens, briefing map/settings/dev/practice/about/HUD, native input, touch, coop and attract. Initial bundler caught UI arrow-function syntax typo; fixing before browser boot.\n- Full simulation suite: 129 checks passed, all 9 loadout/difficulty complete sorties 590–646s, return fuel 24–49%, no cheats. See docs/testing.md.\n\n## Observed issues so far\n- Flak volume too large for evasion: reduced radius, lengthened telegraph.\n- Replay retained once-only warning flags: reset fixed.\n- Urgent audio interruption retained queued chatter: fixed.\n- Renderer visual fixes: cockpit gauge crop, cloud outlines, false fire animation, gun reticle pitch mismatch.\n- UI audit fixes in progress: recursive settings back, live map pause stack, dev sliders exposed in settings, transient HUD click target, cropped portrait, P2 pause focus.\n- Build syntax error: UI selector arrow declaration. Fix in progress.\n\n## Next\nBuild portable artifact, run actual browser inputs and Hub harness, fix integration failures, consolidate quiet verify, fill metadata from evidence and copy exact final root artifacts. App currently owns independent host setInterval simulation; native fixed-step handles standalone. Window.__bomber exposes game/sim/view/audio/online/ui inspection. No full final artifact tested yet.\nEOF\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
