{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_58","type":"agent_message","text":"AI Hub passed all five required scenarios, including latency/loss, either player leaving, and a playerless authoritative server. The checks confirmed shared station control, one-time bomb consumption, state correction, and audio/send cleanup at session end. Standalone keyboard/mouse, controller-stub, touch, and portability checks are still running.\n"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_59","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"cat >> PROGRESS.md <<'EOF'\n\n## Integration evidence\n- Portable self-contained HTML built, ~4.67 MB, native engine + Three/Rapier + Hub client inlined. No CDN or server required to play standalone.\n- Chromium file-origin smoke: ready=true, no console/page/native errors; title, briefing and cockpit rendered. Briefing requires opening animation settle before screenshot (not a defect).\n- Hub actual harness: ALL FIVE PASS (normal, 150ms+50ms jitter+5% loss, guest leave, host leave, playerless server). 66 admission checks plus gameplay assertions; no AIHub warnings. Both players act, salvo consumes once, state corrects, departed duties return to AI, each host reports once, sound and sends stop. docs/hub-results.json.\n- Simulation extended regression: 132 checks PASS; station exchange now transfers commandOwner to displaced pilot, same-station claims no-op, dogleg reduces coastal barrage cadence.\n- Fixed integration: co-op native scene entry clears split so reapply split in play.enter; P2-owned native menu wrapper; map owner retained; UI buttons inherit TV-sized font; initial/persistent independent voice bus; movable free camera; coarse damaged sight; touch gun hold and deliberate jettison with pointer capture; manual throttle overrides automatic power.\n- Root public keyboard/mouse full playthrough running via tests/public-playthrough.py. Native_view agent running browser-verify.py with pad stubs, touch profiles, all menu routes, dev/attract, portability, WebKit and Firefox fallback. Max two browsers respected; Hub browser/server fully closed.\n\n## Remaining release work\n- Resolve any browser/full-input failures.\n- Add quiet aggregate npm run verify and standalone handbook/build docs.\n- Consolidate issue count from real audits/tests, update credits.json -> root exit-interview.json and rebuild embedded About.\n- Final package metadata/JSON parse/offline copied artifact verification and cleanup own test artifacts/processes only.\nEOF\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_59","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"cat >> PROGRESS.md <<'EOF'\n\n## Integration evidence\n- Portable self-contained HTML built, ~4.67 MB, native engine + Three/Rapier + Hub client inlined. No CDN or server required to play standalone.\n- Chromium file-origin smoke: ready=true, no console/page/native errors; title, briefing and cockpit rendered. Briefing requires opening animation settle before screenshot (not a defect).\n- Hub actual harness: ALL FIVE PASS (normal, 150ms+50ms jitter+5% loss, guest leave, host leave, playerless server). 66 admission checks plus gameplay assertions; no AIHub warnings. Both players act, salvo consumes once, state corrects, departed duties return to AI, each host reports once, sound and sends stop. docs/hub-results.json.\n- Simulation extended regression: 132 checks PASS; station exchange now transfers commandOwner to displaced pilot, same-station claims no-op, dogleg reduces coastal barrage cadence.\n- Fixed integration: co-op native scene entry clears split so reapply split in play.enter; P2-owned native menu wrapper; map owner retained; UI buttons inherit TV-sized font; initial/persistent independent voice bus; movable free camera; coarse damaged sight; touch gun hold and deliberate jettison with pointer capture; manual throttle overrides automatic power.\n- Root public keyboard/mouse full playthrough running via tests/public-playthrough.py. Native_view agent running browser-verify.py with pad stubs, touch profiles, all menu routes, dev/attract, portability, WebKit and Firefox fallback. Max two browsers respected; Hub browser/server fully closed.\n\n## Remaining release work\n- Resolve any browser/full-input failures.\n- Add quiet aggregate npm run verify and standalone handbook/build docs.\n- Consolidate issue count from real audits/tests, update credits.json -> root exit-interview.json and rebuild embedded About.\n- Final package metadata/JSON parse/offline copied artifact verification and cleanup own test artifacts/processes only.\nEOF\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_60","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '70,250p' tests/browser-verify.py\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_60","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '70,250p' tests/browser-verify.py\"","aggregated_output":"def menus(browser):\n    context,page,errors,requests=open_game(browser)\n    try:\n        check(page.title()==IDENTITY['title'],'Artifact title matches deliverable')\n        check(page.evaluate('My3D2dge.World3D.backend')=='WebGL 2','Native WebGL2 backend selected')\n        check(abs(page.evaluate('game.settings.music')-.1)<1e-9,'First-run music defaults to10%')\n        page.screenshot(path=str(OUT/'title-tv.png'))\n        click(page,'Settings')\n        check(page.evaluate('__bomber.ui.shell.screen')=='preferences','Settings use filtered preferences')\n        check(not page.get_by_label('Fighter accuracy',exact=True).count(),'Normal settings do not expose developer tuning')\n        slider=page.get_by_label('Aim sensitivity',exact=True);slider.focus()\n        before=page.evaluate('game.settings.aimSensitivity');key(page,'ArrowRight')\n        check(page.evaluate('game.settings.aimSensitivity')>before,'Keyboard adjusts native live slider')\n        key(page,'Escape')\n        check(page.evaluate('__bomber.ui.shell.screen')=='title','Settings Escape back restores title without recursion')\n        click(page,'About / Credits')\n        for tab in ['Source Information','Testing Feedback','Engine Feedback','Prompt Feedback']:\n            click(page,tab);check(page.get_by_role('heading',name=tab,exact=True).count()==1,'Credits tab '+tab)\n        key(page,'Escape');check(page.evaluate('__bomber.ui.shell.screen')=='title','About back restores title')\n        # Hover changes focus through native shell-compatible extension.\n        page.get_by_role('button',name='Practice',exact=True).hover()\n        check(page.evaluate('document.activeElement.textContent')=='Practice','Pointer hover moves menu focus')\n        click(page,'Fly a sortie');page.wait_for_timeout(350);page.screenshot(path=str(OUT/'briefing-tv.png'))\n        check(page.locator('.map-board svg').count()==1,'Interactive briefing chart exists')\n        page.locator('[data-target=\"battery\"]').click()\n        check('CLIFF BATTERY' in page.locator('.brief-copy h3').inner_text(),'Map target preview responds to pointer')\n        no_errors(page,errors,requests)\n    finally:context.close()\n\n\ndef pause_dev(browser):\n    context,page,errors,requests=open_game(browser)\n    try:\n        launch(page);advance(page,25)\n        key(page,'Escape');check(page.evaluate('game.paused'),'Escape pauses standalone')\n        before=state(page)['t'];advance(page,2)\n        check(abs(state(page)['t']-before)<1e-8,'Standalone shared simulation freezes while paused')\n        click(page,'Mission map');check(page.evaluate('__bomber.ui.shell.screen')=='navigation','Pause→map remains open')\n        before=state(page)['t'];advance(page,1)\n        check(state(page)['t']>before+.9,'Map continues actual flight and fuel')\n        click(page,'Back to station');check(not page.evaluate('__bomber.ui.shell.screen'),'Map back restores station')\n        key(page,'Escape');click(page,'Dev mode')\n        check(state(page)['cheated'],'Opening dev tools visibly marks run')\n        slider=page.get_by_label('Fuel burn',exact=True)\n        slider.evaluate('(e)=>{e.value=1.7;e.dispatchEvent(new Event(\"input\",{bubbles:true}));}')\n        check(abs(page.evaluate('__bomber.sim.balance.fuelConsumption')-1.7)<1e-7,'Dev slider changes real fuel tuning')\n        click(page,'Reset tuning')\n        check(abs(page.evaluate('__bomber.sim.balance.fuelConsumption')-1)<1e-7,'Reset restores canonical dependent tuning')\n        click(page,'Start engine fire');check(state(page)['aircraft']['fire']>0,'Dev fire applies subsystem consequence')\n        click(page,'Repair all systems');check(state(page)['aircraft']['fire']==0,'Repair clears real fire')\n        click(page,'Spawn nose fighter');check(any(e['alive'] for e in state(page)['enemies']),'Dev fighter spawns real enemy')\n        click(page,'Spawn flak danger');check(len(state(page)['flak'])>0,'Dev flak spawns real danger')\n        click(page,'Jump: bomb approach');check(state(page)['aircraft']['x']==312000,'Beat jump reaches authored approach')\n        # State export runs through actual in-game download action.\n        with page.expect_download() as download:page.get_by_role('button',name='Export state JSON',exact=True).click()\n        path=OUT/'exported-state.json';download.value.save_as(path)\n        exported=json.loads(path.read_text());check(exported['version']==1 and exported['cheated'],'Dev state download parses and marks test')\n        click(page,'Mission authoring')\n        check(page.locator('#edit-x').count()==1,'Finished mission editor opens')\n        page.locator('#edit-x').fill('21240');page.locator('#edit-y').fill('1120')\n        click(page,'Apply waypoint & associated target')\n        check(page.evaluate('__bomber.sim.definition.waypoints.harbor.x')==21240*16,'Mission editor applies real world units')\n        with page.expect_download() as download:page.get_by_role('button',name='Export mission JSON',exact=True).click()\n        path=OUT/'exported-mission.json';download.value.save_as(path)\n        definition=json.loads(path.read_text());check(definition['waypoints']['harbor']['x']==21240*16,'Mission export preserves edits')\n        key(page,'Escape');check(page.evaluate('__bomber.ui.shell.screen')=='dev','Editor back restores developer desk')\n        click(page,'Free camera: OFF');click(page,'Resume test flight');advance(page,.2)\n        pose=page.evaluate('__bomber.view.freePose');check(bool(pose),'Free camera has independent persistent pose')\n        key(page,'w',.5)\n        after=page.evaluate('__bomber.view.freePose')\n        check(abs(after['x']-pose['x'])+abs(after['y']-pose['y'])+abs(after['z']-pose['z'])>100,'Developer free camera translates with public input')\n        page.screenshot(path=str(OUT/'dev-free-camera.png'))\n        no_errors(page,errors,requests)\n    finally:context.close()\n\n\ndef attract(browser):\n    context,page,errors,requests=open_game(browser)\n    try:\n        initial=page.evaluate('({music:game.settings.music,glyphs:game.settings.glyphs})')\n        advance(page,10.2)\n        check(page.evaluate('__bomber.attract'),'Attract starts after10 seconds idle')\n        check(not page.locator('#attract-label').is_hidden(),'Attract is visibly labeled demonstration')\n        key(page,'Enter')\n        check(not page.evaluate('__bomber.attract'),'Keyboard exits attract immediately')\n        check(page.evaluate('__bomber.ui.shell.screen')=='title','Exit key is consumed before title selection')\n        check(page.evaluate('({music:game.settings.music,glyphs:game.settings.glyphs})')==initial,'Attract leaves player settings intact')\n        advance(page,10.1);check(page.evaluate('__bomber.attract'),'Attract loops on next idle')\n        page.mouse.click(1800,900);advance(page,.1)\n        check(not page.evaluate('__bomber.attract'),'Pointer exits attract')\n        check(page.evaluate('__bomber.ui.shell.screen')=='title','Pointer exit does not launch a sortie')\n        advance(page,10.1);page.evaluate('__pads=[__makePad(0)]');pad(page,0,0)\n        check(not page.evaluate('__bomber.attract'),'Controller exits attract')\n        check(page.evaluate('__bomber.ui.shell.screen')=='title','Controller exit is consumed')\n        # Stick drift below deliberate-input threshold must not block the kiosk timer.\n        page.evaluate('__pads[0].axes=[.05,-.04,0,0]');advance(page,10.2)\n        check(page.evaluate('__bomber.attract'),'Small pad drift does not block attract mode')\n        no_errors(page,errors,requests)\n    finally:context.close()\n\n\ndef mixed_coop(browser):\n    context,page,errors,requests=open_game(browser)\n    try:\n        page.evaluate('__pads=[__makePad(0)]')\n        click(page,'Co-op crew');click(page,'Keyboard + controller');click(page,'Launch sortie');advance(page,22)\n        check(len(state(page)['players'])==2,'Public mixed-coop setup creates two crew members')\n        check(page.evaluate('game.players.length')==2,'Native independent inputs created')\n        check(page.evaluate('game.viewports.length')==2,'Native horizontal split has two viewports')\n        check(page.evaluate('__bomber.view.world.cameras.length')==2,'Native world supplies two cameras')\n        before=state(page)['mounts']['nose']['ammo']\n        page.keyboard.down('d');page.evaluate('__pads[0].axes[2]=.9;__pads[0].buttons[7]={pressed:true,value:1,touched:true}')\n        advance(page,.35)\n        page.keyboard.up('d');page.evaluate('__pads[0].axes[2]=0;__pads[0].buttons[7]={pressed:false,value:0,touched:false}')\n        advance(page,.1)\n        s=state(page)\n        check(s['aircraft']['bank']>.02,'P1 keyboard controls bomber while P2 aims')\n        check(s['players'][1]['aim']['yaw']>.1,'P2 pad aim changes only its mount')\n        check(s['mounts']['nose']['ammo']<before,'P2 trigger fires finite shared ammunition')\n        check(page.evaluate('game.players[1].lastDevice')=='gamepad','P2 retains its own controller prompts')\n        key(page,'Tab');page.get_by_role('button',name=re.compile('12 O’CLOCK.*NOSE')).click();advance(page,.1)\n        check(state(page)['players'][0]['station']=='pilot','Busy station first requests a handover')\n        page.get_by_role('button',name=re.compile('12 O’CLOCK.*NOSE')).click();advance(page,.1)\n        s=state(page);check(s['players'][0]['station']=='nose' and s['players'][1]['station']=='pilot','Confirmed handover exchanges useful stations')\n        check(s['commandOwner']==2,'Pilot handover transfers flight-command permission')\n        pad(page,0,9);check(page.evaluate('game.paused'),'P2 Options pauses shared sortie')\n        check(page.evaluate('game.pausedBy')==2,'Pause records P2 focus ownership')\n        active=page.evaluate('document.activeElement.textContent');pad(page,0,13)\n        changed=page.evaluate('document.activeElement.textContent');check(changed!=active,'P2 navigates its pause menu')\n        key(page,'ArrowDown');check(page.evaluate('document.activeElement.textContent')==changed,'P1 cannot move P2-owned pause focus')\n        pad(page,0,1);check(not page.evaluate('game.paused'),'P2 Circle backs out and resumes')\n        page.screenshot(path=str(OUT/'mixed-coop-tv.png'))\n        page.evaluate(\"__pads[0].connected=false;const e=new Event('gamepaddisconnected');e.gamepad=__pads[0];dispatchEvent(e)\");advance(page,.2)\n        s=state(page);check(not s['players'][1]['connected'],'Guest pad departure clears the player')\n        check(s['owners']['pilot']=='AI','Departed pilot duty returns to AI')\n        check(s['commandOwner']==1,'Remaining human inherits flight-command permission')\n        check(page.evaluate('game.viewports.length')==0,'Departure collapses native split to solo')\n        no_errors(page,errors,requests)\n    finally:context.close()\n\n\ndef two_pads(browser):\n    context,page,errors,requests=open_game(browser)\n    try:\n        page.evaluate('__pads=[__makePad(0),__makePad(1)]')\n        click(page,'Co-op crew');click(page,'Two controllers');click(page,'Launch sortie');advance(page,22)\n        check(page.evaluate('game.players.map(p=>p.pad)')==[0,1],'Two-pad setup assigns distinct standard pad indices')\n        page.evaluate('__pads[0].axes[0]=-.8;__pads[1].axes[2]=.8')\n        advance(page,.4);s=state(page)\n        check(s['aircraft']['bank']<-.04,'First controller flies independently')\n        check(s['players'][1]['aim']['yaw']>.1,'Second controller traverses gun independently')\n        page.evaluate('__pads[0].axes=[0,0,0,0];__pads[1].axes=[0,0,0,0]');advance(page,.1)\n        key(page,'Escape');click(page,'Settings')\n        symbols=page.get_by_role('button',name=re.compile('Button symbols:'))\n        for _ in range(5):\n            if page.evaluate('game.settings.glyphs')=='xbox':break\n            symbols.click();advance(page,.05)\n        check(page.evaluate('game.settings.glyphs')=='xbox','Settings offer Xbox glyphs')\n        pad(page,0,7)\n        check(page.evaluate('game.players[0].label(\"wheel\")')=='Y','Native prompts render Xbox Y')\n        no_errors(page,errors,requests)\n    finally:context.close()\n\n\ndef touch(browser):\n    context=browser.new_context(viewport={'width':390,'height':844},device_scale_factor=2,is_mobile=True,has_touch=True)\n    context.add_init_script(PAD_STUB);page=context.new_page();errors=[];requests=[]\n    page.on('pageerror',lambda e:errors.append(str(e)));page.on('requestfailed',lambda r:requests.append({'url':r.url,'failure':r.failure}))\n    try:\n        page.goto(ARTIFACT.as_uri()+'?backend=webgl');page.wait_for_function('window.__bomber?.ready',timeout=90000);page.wait_for_timeout(300);page.evaluate('game.stop()');advance(page,.1)\n        page.get_by_role('button',name='Fly a sortie',exact=True).tap();advance(page,.1)\n        page.get_by_role('button',name='Launch sortie',exact=True).tap();advance(page,.4)\n        check(page.evaluate('__bomber.touch.active'),'Touch device selects assisted touch UI')\n        check('touch-mode' in page.locator('#hud').get_attribute('class'),'Touch hides dense station controls')\n        cdp=context.new_cdp_session(page)\n        cdp.send('Input.dispatchTouchEvent',{'type':'touchStart','touchPoints':[{'x':70,'y':590,'id':1},{'x':310,'y':590,'id':2}]})\n        cdp.send('Input.dispatchTouchEvent',{'type':'touchMove','touchPoints':[{'x':110,'y':550,'id':1},{'x':340,'y':560,'id':2}]})\n        advance(page,.2)\n        check(page.evaluate('__bomber.touch.fingers.size')==2,'Two touch contacts are tracked simultaneously')\n        check(page.evaluate('Math.abs(__bomber.touch.left[0])>0&&Math.abs(__bomber.touch.right[0])>0'),'Invisible thumb regions provide independent flight and aim')\n        cdp.send('Input.dispatchTouchEvent',{'type':'touchEnd','touchPoints':[]});advance(page,.1)\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_61","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '1,33p' src/ui.js && tail -85 tests/browser-verify.py && cat docs/acceptance.md | tail -45\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_61","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '1,33p' src/ui.js && tail -85 tests/browser-verify.py && cat docs/acceptance.md | tail -45\"","aggregated_output":"import {LABELS,STATIONS,LOADOUTS,DIFFICULTIES,TUNING,DEFAULT_BALANCE,MISSION,U} from '../content/mission.js';\nimport CREDITS from '../content/credits.json';\nconst esc=s=>String(s).replace(/[&<>\"']/g,c=>({'&':'&amp;','<':'&lt;','>':'&gt;','\"':'&quot;',\"'\":'&#39;'}[c]));\nconst $=(s,r=document)=>r.querySelector(s);\nconst minutes=t=>`${Math.floor(t/60)}:${String(Math.floor(t%60)).padStart(2,'0')}`;\nexport class BomberUI{\n constructor(app){Object.assign(this,app);this.hud=$('#hud');this.lastHud=0;this.setup={loadout:'balanced',difficulty:'normal',route:'direct',coop:false};this.wheelPlayer=null;this.preview='harbor';this.dev={freeCamera:false,debug:false,paused:false};\n  this.shell=new this.E.Shell(this.game,{theme:{scale:1,font:'Arial, sans-serif',titleFont:'Impact, sans-serif',ink:'#f2e8cb',paper:'#102f38',accent:'#ebbd6c'},screens:{pause:{kicker:'FLIGHT DESK',title:'Crew at ease',text:'The aircraft waits here. Resume when the crew is ready.',actions:[['Mission map',()=>this.map()],['Flight handbook',()=>this.controls()],['Emergency actions',()=>this.emergency()],['Dev mode',()=>this.devMenu()],['Leave sortie',()=>this.leaveMenu()]]}},standard:true});\n  const nativeShow=this.shell.show.bind(this.shell);this.shell.show=(name,spec={})=>{if(name==='settings'){this.settings();return this.shell;}return nativeShow(name,spec);};\n  for(const [key,label,min,max,step,unit]of TUNING)this.game.settings.define({key:'dev_'+key,label,type:'slider',value:DEFAULT_BALANCE[key],min,max,step,unit,group:'Flight tuning'});\n  this.game.settings.onChange=(key,value)=>{if(key.startsWith('dev_')&&!this.online.active){this.sim.balance[key.slice(4)]=value;this.sim.state.cheated=true;}if(key==='voice'){this.game.audio.voiceVolume=value;this.game.audio.applyVolume();}if(key==='captions')this.hud.style.setProperty('--caption-scale',value);};\n  this.shell.root.addEventListener('pointerover',e=>{const b=e.target.closest('button,input');if(b&&!b.disabled)b.focus({preventScroll:true});});\n  this.shell.root.addEventListener('pointerdown',()=>this.activity(),{passive:true});\n }\n show(name,spec){this.shell.show(name,spec);this.screenStamp++;this.hud.hidden=true;return this.shell;}\n clear(){clearTimeout(this.jettisonTimer);this.jettisonTimer=null;this.shell.hide();this.menuOwner=1;if(this.clearActions)this.clearActions();this.game.input.clear();for(const i of this.game.players)i.clear();this.activity();}\n title(){this.clear();this.show('title',{kicker:'A CREW. A BOMBER. A WAY HOME.',name:'B-17\\nCROSS CHANNEL\\nCHAOS',subtitle:'Cross the water. Answer the warning.\\nBring everyone home.',actions:[['Fly a sortie',()=>this.brief(false)],['Co-op crew',()=>this.coopMenu()],['Practice',()=>this.practiceMenu()],['Settings',()=>this.settings()],['About / Credits',()=>this.about()]],meta:['1–2 CREW','10–12 MIN SORTIE','OPERATION COPPER TIDE'],footer:'An original flight game inspired by B-17 Bomber (1982).\\nIdle for a crew demonstration.'});this.activity();}\n settings(){this.show('preferences',{title:'Make it your aircraft',text:'Your settings stay with this device.',rows:['#Sound','volume','music','effects','voice','#Flight & comfort','invertFlight','aimSensitivity','captions','glyphs','motion','shake','invertY','deadzone'],actions:[['Controls & rebinding',()=>this.shell.show('controls')],['Back',()=>this.shell.back()]]});}\n controls(){this.show('help',{kicker:'FLIGHT HANDBOOK',title:'Every station matters',text:'Route hold flies the selected course. Any flight stick input takes the aircraft back. The crew never releases your bombs.',keys:[['WASD / Left stick','Bank and pitch'],['Mouse / Right stick','Aim or look'],['Click · Space / R2','Fire gun / release bombs'],['Q · E / L1 · R1','Decrease / increase power'],['Tab / △','Station wheel'],['1 · 2 · 3','Pilot · threatened gun · bombsight'],['Arrows / D-pad','Guns: 12 · 3 · 6 · 9 o’clock'],['M / □','Operational map'],['H / L3','Toggle navigation hold'],['B · V / L1 · R1 in sight','Bomb doors · salvo size'],['F / ○','Extinguish engine fire (one bottle)'],['Hold J / R3 for 1.5s','Jettison remaining payload'],['Esc / Options','Pause / menu']],sections:[['Bombing','The gold impact ring predicts where your bomb will land, including velocity and wind. Open the sight early, keep the ship inside the ring, and release deliberately. The last bomb never prevents a return.'],['Crew assistance','Unattended guns suppress fighters. Leave a station to AI by taking another. An occupied station requires a second selection to exchange duties. Fire after the transition.'],['Touch','Drag the left half to fly and the right half to aim. Context actions appear for threats, bombing and return. The menu opens the map and emergency actions.']]});}\n coopMenu(){this.show('coop',{kicker:'TWO PEOPLE · ONE AIRCRAFT',title:'Assemble your crew',text:'One flies. One watches the glass. Both may change stations. Connect two standard pads, or use keyboard/mouse plus one pad. The shared sortie pauses for either crew member.',actions:[['Keyboard + controller',()=>{this.setup.coop=true;this.setup.coopMode='mixed';this.brief(true);}],['Two controllers',()=>{this.setup.coop=true;this.setup.coopMode='pads';this.brief(true);}],['Back',()=>this.shell.back()]]});}\n brief(coop=false){this.setup.coop=coop;this.show('brief',{kicker:'OPERATION 01 / COPPER TIDE',title:'Greyhaven. Then home.',text:'Destroy the armed transport at Greyhaven docks. Everything after that is your decision.',actions:[['Launch sortie',()=>this.start(this.setup)],['Route: '+(this.setup.route==='direct'?'Direct':'Northern dogleg'),()=>{this.setup.route=this.setup.route==='direct'?'dogleg':'direct';this.brief(coop);}],['Payload: '+LOADOUTS[this.setup.loadout].name,()=>{const a=Object.keys(LOADOUTS),i=a.indexOf(this.setup.loadout);this.setup.loadout=a[(i+1)%a.length];this.brief(coop);}],['Skill: '+DIFFICULTIES[this.setup.difficulty].name,()=>{const a=Object.keys(DIFFICULTIES);this.setup.difficulty=a[(a.indexOf(this.setup.difficulty)+1)%a.length];this.brief(coop);}],['Back',()=>this.shell.back()]]});\n  const grid=document.createElement('div');grid.className='brief-grid';grid.innerHTML=`<div class=\"map-board\">${this.mapSvg(false)}<div class=\"map-key\"><span>CHANNEL SECTOR / 06:40</span><span>N ↑ · 5 KM GRID</span></div></div><div class=\"brief-copy\"><h3>THE TRANSPORT IS THE TARGET</h3><p>A naval transport shelters between the cranes. One accurate two-bomb salvo can finish the primary.</p><p>Direct: shorter crossing, defended coast.<br>Dogleg: longer flight, a quieter approach.</p><div class=\"loadout\"><strong>${LOADOUTS[this.setup.loadout].name}</strong><p>${LOADOUTS[this.setup.loadout].desc}<br>${LOADOUTS[this.setup.loadout].reserve}</p></div><p>Guns can jam. A sight can fail. One fire bottle buys a second chance. Home repairs, refuels and rearms.</p></div>`;\n  $('.esh-mod',this.shell.root).insertBefore(grid,$('.esh-btns',this.shell.root));this.bindMap(grid,false);\n }\n mapSvg(live=true){const s=this.sim.state,a=s.aircraft,kx=x=>55+(x+10000)/460000*620,ky=y=>130+(y+10000)/230000*220,home=[kx(0),ky(0)],harbor=[kx(340000),ky(18000)],dog=[kx(140000),ky(-66000)];\n  return `<svg viewBox=\"0 0 720 330\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Operational map of the Channel, Rookfield, Greyhaven and Bracken\"><defs><pattern id=\"chart-grid\" width=\"72\" height=\"55\" patternUnits=\"userSpaceOnUse\"><path d=\"M72 0H0V55\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#45665f\" stroke-width=\".6\" opacity=\".6\"/></pattern></defs><rect width=\"720\" height=\"330\" fill=\"#143745\"/><path d=\"M0 0H95L108 65 92 100 110 150 98 205 120 245 90 330H0Z\" fill=\"#536b50\" stroke=\"#b3b18a\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><path d=\"M470 0L454 56 476 94 451 122 480 154 460 180 476 208 460 250 492 288 480 330H720V0Z\" fill=\"#5c7051\" stroke=\"#b3b18a\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><path d=\"M470 153 Q530 150 564 165 L550 178 478 174\" fill=\"#143745\"/><rect width=\"720\" height=\"330\" fill=\"url(#chart-grid)\"/><text x=\"14\" y=\"26\" class=\"map-minor\">ENGLAND</text><text x=\"548\" y=\"28\" class=\"map-minor\">OCCUPIED COAST</text><text x=\"238\" y=\"276\" class=\"map-label\" opacity=\".5\" transform=\"rotate(-8,238,276)\">THE CHANNEL</text><path d=\"M${home}L${this.setup.route==='dogleg'?dog+'L':''}${harbor}\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#ebbd6c\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-dasharray=\"7 6\"/><circle cx=\"${kx(270000)}\" cy=\"${ky(-12000)}\" r=\"26\" fill=\"#d5764c\" opacity=\".2\"/><circle cx=\"${harbor[0]}\" cy=\"${harbor[1]}\" r=\"35\" fill=\"#d5764c\" opacity=\".13\"/>\n ${Object.entries(MISSION.waypoints).map(([id,t])=>{const x=kx(t.x),y=ky(t.y);return `<g class=\"map-hit\" data-target=\"${id}\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"button\" aria-label=\"Preview ${esc(t.label)}\"><circle cx=\"${x}\" cy=\"${y}\" r=\"${id==='harbor'?8:5}\" fill=\"${id==='home'?'#9fc8a2':id==='harbor'?'#ebbd6c':'#b5c5ae'}\" stroke=\"#0e2a32\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><circle cx=\"${x}\" cy=\"${y}\" r=\"20\" fill=\"transparent\"/><text class=\"map-label\" x=\"${x+(id==='refinery'?-130:12)}\" y=\"${y+(id==='home'?-12:5)}\">${esc(t.label)}</text></g>`;}).join('')}\n ${live?`<g transform=\"translate(${kx(a.x)},${ky(a.y)}) rotate(${a.yaw*180/Math.PI+90})\"><path d=\"M0 -12L8 8 0 4 -8 8Z\" fill=\"#fff3cf\" stroke=\"#122d33\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g>`:''}<text x=\"680\" y=\"30\" class=\"map-label\">N ↑</text></svg>`;\n }\n bindMap(root,live){root.querySelectorAll('[data-target]').forEach(e=>{const f=()=>{this.preview=e.dataset.target;if(live)this.map();else{const copy=$('.brief-copy',root);const t=MISSION.waypoints[this.preview];copy.querySelector('h3').textContent=t.label;copy.querySelector('p').textContent=this.targetDescription(this.preview);}};e.addEventListener('click',f);e.addEventListener('keydown',ev=>{if(ev.key==='Enter'||ev.key===' '){ev.preventDefault();f();}});});}\n targetDescription(id){return{harbor:'Primary: armed transport. Two direct hits, or one centered salvo. Harbor tanks and works offer optional score.',battery:'Optional: cliff battery. Destroy it to suppress this coast’s barrage. It is not required for the primary.',refinery:'Optional: Bracken refinery. Two hits. Only continue if fuel and ordnance permit.',home:'Rookfield: cross the approach circle to trigger assisted recovery. A safe abort saves the crew.',dogleg:'Northern dogleg. Longer distance; more time to answer fighter warnings before the coast.'}[id];}\n map(owner){this.menuOwner=owner||this.menuOwner||this.game.pausedBy||1;if(this.game.paused){this.shell.hide();this.game.resume();}const s=this.sim.state;this.show('navigation',{kicker:'NAVIGATOR / AIRCRAFT CONTINUES',title:'Choose your next move',text:'Fuel and flight continue while this chart is open. Only the flight commander can commit a course.',actions:[{label:'Fly to '+MISSION.waypoints[this.preview].label,disabled:s.commandOwner!==this.menuOwner,fn:()=>{this.send({type:'route',target:this.preview},this.menuOwner);this.clear();}},['Primary: Greyhaven',()=>{this.preview='harbor';this.map();}],['Return: Rookfield',()=>{this.preview='home';this.map();}],['Optional: Refinery',()=>{this.preview='refinery';this.map();}],['Optional: Battery',()=>{this.preview='battery';this.map();}],['Back to station',()=>this.clear()]]});\n  const board=document.createElement('div');board.className='brief-grid';board.innerHTML=`<div class=\"map-board\">${this.mapSvg()}<div class=\"map-key\"><span>LIVE POSITION</span><span>NO PAUSE</span></div></div><div class=\"brief-copy\"><h3>${MISSION.waypoints[this.preview].label}</h3><p>${this.targetDescription(this.preview)}</p><div class=\"loadout\"><strong>RETURN FORECAST</strong><p>${Math.round(s.aircraft.fuel/s.aircraft.maxFuel*100)}% fuel · ${s.bombsLeft} bombs<br>${Math.max(0,Math.round(s.reserve||0))} seconds above estimated home fuel.<br>Home approach is always available.</p></div></div>`;$('.esh-mod',this.shell.root).insertBefore(board,$('.esh-btns',this.shell.root));this.bindMap(board,true);this.game.resume();\ndef touch(browser):\n    context=browser.new_context(viewport={'width':390,'height':844},device_scale_factor=2,is_mobile=True,has_touch=True)\n    context.add_init_script(PAD_STUB);page=context.new_page();errors=[];requests=[]\n    page.on('pageerror',lambda e:errors.append(str(e)));page.on('requestfailed',lambda r:requests.append({'url':r.url,'failure':r.failure}))\n    try:\n        page.goto(ARTIFACT.as_uri()+'?backend=webgl');page.wait_for_function('window.__bomber?.ready',timeout=90000);page.wait_for_timeout(300);page.evaluate('game.stop()');advance(page,.1)\n        page.get_by_role('button',name='Fly a sortie',exact=True).tap();advance(page,.1)\n        page.get_by_role('button',name='Launch sortie',exact=True).tap();advance(page,.4)\n        check(page.evaluate('__bomber.touch.active'),'Touch device selects assisted touch UI')\n        check('touch-mode' in page.locator('#hud').get_attribute('class'),'Touch hides dense station controls')\n        cdp=context.new_cdp_session(page)\n        cdp.send('Input.dispatchTouchEvent',{'type':'touchStart','touchPoints':[{'x':70,'y':590,'id':1},{'x':310,'y':590,'id':2}]})\n        cdp.send('Input.dispatchTouchEvent',{'type':'touchMove','touchPoints':[{'x':110,'y':550,'id':1},{'x':340,'y':560,'id':2}]})\n        advance(page,.2)\n        check(page.evaluate('__bomber.touch.fingers.size')==2,'Two touch contacts are tracked simultaneously')\n        check(page.evaluate('Math.abs(__bomber.touch.left[0])>0&&Math.abs(__bomber.touch.right[0])>0'),'Invisible thumb regions provide independent flight and aim')\n        cdp.send('Input.dispatchTouchEvent',{'type':'touchEnd','touchPoints':[]});advance(page,.1)\n        check(page.evaluate('__bomber.touch.left[0]===0&&__bomber.touch.right[0]===0'),'Lifting contacts clears held touch commands')\n        page.screenshot(path=str(OUT/'phone-flight.png'))\n        # A long press outlives multiple HUD rebuilds: pointerdown must still open the menu.\n        box=page.locator('.menu-toggle').bounding_box();x=box['x']+box['width']/2;y=box['y']+box['height']/2\n        cdp.send('Input.dispatchTouchEvent',{'type':'touchStart','touchPoints':[{'x':x,'y':y,'id':3}]});advance(page,.3)\n        check(page.evaluate('game.paused'),'Touch menu activates before periodic HUD replacement')\n        cdp.send('Input.dispatchTouchEvent',{'type':'touchEnd','touchPoints':[]});advance(page,.1)\n        page.get_by_role('button',name='Resume',exact=True).tap();advance(page,.2)\n        # The public touchscreen exit is consumed in attract just like the keyboard.\n        page.evaluate('__bomber.toTitle()');advance(page,10.2)\n        check(page.evaluate('__bomber.attract'),'Touch title enters attract')\n        page.touchscreen.tap(195,300);advance(page,.1)\n        check(not page.evaluate('__bomber.attract'),'Tap exits attract')\n        check(page.evaluate('__bomber.ui.shell.screen')=='title','Attract touch exit does not select a menu item')\n        no_errors(page,errors,requests)\n    finally:context.close()\n\n\ndef portable(browser):\n    folder=OUT/'portable';folder.mkdir(exist_ok=True);copied=folder/'bomber.html';shutil.copyfile(ARTIFACT,copied)\n    context=browser.new_context(viewport={'width':1280,'height':720});page=context.new_page();errors=[];requests=[]\n    page.on('pageerror',lambda e:errors.append(str(e)));page.on('requestfailed',lambda r:requests.append(r.url))\n    try:\n        page.goto(copied.as_uri()+'?backend=webgl');page.wait_for_function('window.__bomber?.ready',timeout=90000)\n        check(page.title()==IDENTITY['title'],'Copied artifact identifies itself away from dev files')\n        check(page.evaluate('My3D2dge.World3D.backend')=='WebGL 2','Copied artifact starts complete native renderer')\n        check(not page.evaluate('performance.getEntriesByType(\"resource\").some(r=>!r.name.startsWith(\"file:\")&&!r.name.startsWith(\"data:\")&&!r.name.startsWith(\"blob:\"))'),'Portable artifact requires no CDN/network requests')\n        no_errors(page,errors,requests)\n    finally:context.close()\n\n\ndef webkit(p):\n    browser=p.webkit.launch(headless=True)\n    try:\n        context,page,errors,requests=open_game(browser)\n        try:\n            launch(page);advance(page,.4);page.screenshot(path=str(OUT/'webkit-cockpit.png'))\n            check(page.evaluate('My3D2dge.World3D.backend')=='WebGL 2','WebKit uses native WebGL2 route')\n            no_errors(page,errors,requests)\n        finally:context.close()\n    finally:browser.close()\n\n\ndef firefox(p):\n    browser=p.firefox.launch(headless=True)\n    try:\n        context=browser.new_context();page=context.new_page()\n        try:\n            page.goto(ARTIFACT.as_uri());page.wait_for_function('window.__bomber?.error||window.__bomber?.ready',timeout=90000)\n            ready=page.evaluate('__bomber.ready')\n            if not ready:\n                check(page.locator('#support').is_visible(),'Unsupported renderer provides visible explanation')\n                check('WEBGL 2' in page.locator('#support').inner_text(),'Unsupported renderer explains capability needed')\n                RESULT['limitations'].append('Installed Firefox has no usable native WebGL2; useful unsupported-renderer screen verified.')\n            else:check(page.evaluate('My3D2dge.World3D.backend')=='WebGL 2','Firefox available renderer works')\n        finally:context.close()\n    finally:browser.close()\n\nwith sync_playwright() as p:\n    browser=p.chromium.launch(headless=True,args=['--enable-unsafe-swiftshader'])\n    try:\n        for name,fn in [('menus/preferences/credits',menus),('pause/dev/editor/free camera',pause_dev),('attract/input consumption',attract),('mixed couch co-op',mixed_coop),('two pads/glyphs',two_pads),('touch/multitouch',touch),('copied artifact portability',portable)]:run(name,lambda fn=fn:fn(browser))\n    finally:browser.close()\n    run('WebKit native renderer',lambda:webkit(p))\n    run('Firefox unsupported renderer',lambda:firefox(p))\n(ROOT/'tests/browser-result.json').write_text(json.dumps(RESULT,indent=2))\nprint(f\"Browser verification: {RESULT['assertions']} assertions, {len(RESULT['cases'])} scenarios, {len(RESULT['failures'])} failures\")\nraise SystemExit(bool(RESULT['failures']))\n| Source research, original adaptation | `docs/research.md`; preserved instructions, developer history, directly viewed source screenshots; no original recordings reused | Complete. Exact source audio timbres remain unknown. |\n| Random title among 50 riffs | `identity.json`: B-17 Cross Channel Chaos, random draw 42 of 50 | Complete; prescribed development/artifact slug established. |\n| Native engine foundation | `E.Game`, `E.Shell`, native inputs/settings/audio/Humanoid, native World3D pen/shapes/cameras; pinned dependencies bundled by `tools/build.mjs` | Implemented. WebGL proof has two independent cameras and zero errors. Optional software WebGPU attempt has recorded implementation errors; do not describe it as passing. |\n| One complete operation | Copper Tide: Rookfield, Channel, Greyhaven transport, optional battery/refinery/tanks/works, landing and debrief | Nine honest command-driven full sorties pass. Duration 590–646 seconds. |\n| Flight and resource coupling | Native z-up coordinates at 16 units/metre; bank/pitch/throttle, payload-dependent speed/fuel, stall, course handover, engine consequences | Deterministic edge checks and all nine sortie combinations pass. |\n| Planning and navigation | Interactive route/target map, direct/dogleg choice, three viable payloads and three skill presets, displayed return forecast | Implemented. Local Player2 identity now survives map refreshes; dogleg's 1.8× coastal interval has a passing comparison regression. Final UI check required. |\n| Four directional stations | Distinct nose/starboard/tail/port transforms and real bounded world-space gun directions; finite ammunition, lead assistance and swept shot collision | All four mount fixtures hit their respective spatial targets, wrong-bearing test misses, empty gun stops, score stays unique. |\n| Bombing | Doors, 1/2/4-bomb salvo, finite payload, shared ballistic prediction including wind, authored target health, direct hit/miss/last-bomb states | Exact prediction/impact integration and duplicate-release tests pass; full sorties strike the military transport. Damaged sight now quantizes the coarse mark and removes fine target boxes. |\n| Damage and emergency fallback | Hull, engine power/burn, mount jam, damaged sight, finite fire bottle, held payload jettison, warning/fire progression | Edge checks pass for consequences, alternate gun, repair, emergency deduplication and terminal uncontrolled fire. |\n| Replay and terminal outcomes | Success, safe abort, destroyed hull, ground impact, fuel exhaustion, deadline and manual stop lead to debrief; repair/rearm/replay | Edge checks pass, including reset heading/resources and repeated warnings. |\n| Original native visual content | Custom four-engine bomber, fighters, cockpit/windows/guns, doors/gear/props, ship/cranes/refinery/battery/runway, coastline/clouds/flak/impact smoke | Present in `view.js` and custom `E.SHAPES`. Final screenshots assess TV/split/mobile readability. |\n| Animation | Fixed-state math poses for bank, control surfaces, propellers, recoil, doors, falling bombs, smoke/fire, gear; native radio portrait expressions | Implemented in native drawing/rig path. No external raster/audio assets required. |\n| Coded audio | Three original native score motifs, four engines, wind, gun mechanisms, bay mechanism, bomb/flak/impact/landing, role-dependent babble | 32 OfflineAudioContext checks pass. Music initializes at 0.1 and survives replay. Initial/persisted voice level now uses native voiceVolume/applyVolume. No human listening claim. |\n| Controller, keyboard, mouse | Standard pad bindings, device-following glyphs, PS default/Xbox option, keyboard station shortcuts, mouse aim, menu hover focus, disconnect policy | Implemented. Pilot aim now forwards to look; native free-camera motion is wired. Final standard-pad/disconnect/browser input checks pending. |\n| Touch | Invisible left/right thumb regions, assisted throttle/course hold, threat/bombs/home context actions, explicit bomb release, held FIRE BURST, pause emergency hold | All requested action paths now exist. Final multitouch/context check and jettison release/cancel check required. |\n| Local co-op | Two native row viewports, keyboard+pad or two pads; independent station ownership/handover and departure-to-AI | Renderer proof plus deterministic ownership tests pass. Simultaneous device/pause ownership needs final browser checks. |\n| AI Hub | First verbatim released session client, shared-world 1–2 declaration, authoritative fixed clock independent of drawing, server mode, input validation, compact live packets/reliable correction, departure/end/report adapter | Implemented in `online.js`/`app.js`. Actual downloaded harness scenarios and warning scans are separate required final evidence. |\n| Attract | Ten-second title idle starts isolated invulnerable/infinite demo, visible label, input exits, no real save mutation | Actual extracted `demoBot` completed every mission phase and reset to a new seed. Browser ten-second entry, consumed exits for each device, and state isolation remain final gates. |\n| Practice and dev | Gunnery/bombing/damaged-return starts; pause-access tools, invulnerability/resources, all spawns/damage/repair, jumps, pause/step, free camera, visualization, state export, same-seed replay; eight live tuning sliders/default reset | Simulation tools/practices/export pass. UI interactions, free-camera motion and slider reset need final browser evidence. |\n| Mission authoring | Waypoint/target coordinates, live application, volume preview, definition JSON export/import and validation | Round trip and invalid-data rejection pass. Current editor focuses waypoints/associated targets; debug visualization still needs encounter trigger planes, fighter hit volumes and attack-path preview beyond target rings/route line. |\n| Single-file handoff | `tools/build.mjs` inlines native engine, World3D/dependencies/WASM, CSS/game/content; unmodified Hub client first after charset; notices embedded | Build route implemented. Copied-away artifact, file origin, no missing requests/console errors and final JSON parsing remain release gates. |\n| Feedback schema | One `content/credits.json` renders About/Credits and supplies exit interview; exact TASK sections/catalogue shape | Source/engine/prompt text present. Testing feedback fields must be filled from final evidence, exported beside final HTML and parsed before release. |\n\n## Attract simulation evidence\n\nThe actual `demoBot` function was extracted from `src/app.js` and executed against the real `BomberSim` at 1/120 second. Its isolated demo completed successfully at **609 simulated seconds**, traversing launch, outbound, coast, strike, return, landing and debrief. Observed events included every required showcase system: takeoff, fighter stations/guns/hits/kills, flak warning/burst/evasion, deliberate release, impact/target destruction, return route and recovery. After its result wait, it reset to seed 1943 at time zero. Invulnerability and infinite resources were confined to this transient demo state.\n\n## Transform consistency audit\n\nSimulation and presentation share east/south/z-up units; `BEARINGS` provides the four actual world headings. Gun cameras attach at different physical positions and use the same yaw/pitch aim convention as shots. The view additionally transforms attachment position through bomber pitch/bank and rolls its camera. Ballistic prediction and bombs use identical fixed-step integration; full-sim impact checks establish the authoritative sight solution. The visual sights must avoid implying aim can teleport the bomb origin. Fine drift correction requires flight/route adjustment and timing the shared prediction.\n\n## Integration findings communicated\n\n1. Pilot input updated `aim`, while the camera initially read untouched `look`; corrected centrally by forwarding pilot aim to look.\n2. Damaged sight initially changed only the label; corrected with a quantized coarse mark and removal of fine boxes.\n3. Voice settings initially set a native bus gain without setting `voiceVolume`; corrected property/default application keeps independent radio volume stable.\n4. Free-camera controls existed in the view but were not called by application input; now wired.\n5. Touch had no gun-firing gesture or held-jettison path; now has FIRE BURST and the emergency menu. Pointer release outside the held-jettison button must cancel its timer; correction/check remains necessary.\n6. Local co-op map commits defaulted to Player1 after Player2 took command; initiating player identity now survives map preview refreshes.\n7. Dogleg initially changed travel alone; its coastal barrage interval is now 1.8× longer before the target approach, with a passing actual-warning-count test.\n8. Occupied-seat exchange initially failed to transfer command when the displaced player became pilot; corrected and regression-tested immediately, without requiring that player to request pilot again.\n9. Same-station requests initially reset aim and repeatedly emitted radio messages; now harmless no-ops, with a regression covering repeated requests.\n10. Trigger/path/hit-volume visualization currently exceeds what `debugVolumes` actually draws; extend its existing native pen path to match the promised testing tool.\n\nDo not count a known environment's absent physical hardware as an implementation failure. Do not turn an unverified gate into a passing claim. Final integration evidence should update this checkpoint and `docs/testing.md` together.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_62","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc 'cat docs/public-playthrough.json && ls -lt tests/browser-evidence | head -8'","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_62","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc 'cat docs/public-playthrough.json && ls -lt tests/browser-evidence | head -8'","aggregated_output":"{\n  \"checks\": 8,\n  \"failures\": [\n    \"Public input sortie did not destroy primary and recover\"\n  ],\n  \"result\": {\n    \"reason\": \"destroyed\",\n    \"outcome\": \"PRIMARY DESTROYED\",\n    \"win\": false,\n    \"score\": 2975,\n    \"stats\": {\n      \"primary\": true,\n      \"returned\": false,\n      \"kills\": 4,\n      \"bombs\": 2,\n      \"hits\": 1,\n      \"accuracy\": 50,\n      \"damagePenalty\": 400,\n      \"wastedPenalty\": 75,\n      \"returnBonus\": 0,\n      \"fuel\": 62,\n      \"duration\": 362\n    },\n    \"cheated\": false,\n    \"practice\": null\n  },\n  \"encounters\": [\n    \"nose\",\n    \"port\",\n    \"starboard\",\n    \"tail\"\n  ],\n  \"inputObservedBearings\": [\n    \"nose\",\n    \"tail\",\n    \"port\",\n    \"starboard\"\n  ],\n  \"fired\": 182,\n  \"cheated\": false,\n  \"browserErrors\": []\n}total 1972\n-rw-r--r-- 1 micha micha 250776 Nov  6 05:03 webkit-cockpit.png\ndrwxr-xr-x 2 micha micha   4096 Nov  6 05:03 portable\n-rw-r--r-- 1 micha micha 304631 Nov  6 05:02 phone-flight.png\n-rw-r--r-- 1 micha micha 498968 Nov  6 05:01 briefing-tv.png\n-rw-r--r-- 1 micha micha 953492 Nov  6 05:01 title-tv.png\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_63","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '1,135p' tests/sim-test.mjs && python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfrom pathlib import Path\np=Path('tests/browser-result.json')\nif p.exists():\n a=json.loads(p.read_text());print(json.dumps({k:a[k]for k in ['assertions','failures','limitations']},indent=2))\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_63","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '1,135p' tests/sim-test.mjs && python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfrom pathlib import Path\np=Path('tests/browser-result.json')\nif p.exists():\n a=json.loads(p.read_text());print(json.dumps({k:a[k]for k in ['assertions','failures','limitations']},indent=2))\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"import {BomberSim, angle, localVector, segmentHit, predictBomb, bombIntegrate} from '../src/sim.js';\nimport {U, BEARINGS, LOADOUTS, DIFFICULTIES, MISSION, validateMission} from '../content/mission.js';\nimport {fileURLToPath} from 'node:url';\n\nconst DT = 1 / 120;\nconst dist = (a, b) => Math.hypot(a.x - b.x, a.y - b.y);\nconst copy = x => JSON.parse(JSON.stringify(x));\n\nfunction advance(sim, seconds, control) {\n  for (let i = 0; i < Math.ceil(seconds / DT) && !sim.state.result; i++) {\n    if (control) control(sim, i);\n    sim.step(DT);\n  }\n}\n\nfunction airborne(options = {}) {\n  const sim = new BomberSim(options), s = sim.state, a = s.aircraft;\n  Object.assign(a, {x: 85000, y: 0, z: 900 * U, speed: 75 * U, yaw: 0, pitch: 0, bank: 0, throttle: 0.8, airborne: true, hold: false, holdMode: 'course', gear: 0});\n  s.t = 50; s.phase = 'outbound';\n  sim.definition.encounters = [];\n  return sim;\n}\n\nfunction lineUp(sim, target, offset = 0) {\n  const s = sim.state, a = s.aircraft;\n  const p = predictBomb(a, sim.wind());\n  a.x += target.x - p.x + offset; a.y += target.y - p.y;\n  s.phase = 'strike'; s.targets.find(t => t.id === 'battery').alive = false;\n  sim.command(1, {type: 'station', station: 'bombs'});\n  s.doorsOpen = true; a.doors = 1;\n  sim.updatePrediction();\n}\n\n/** An observer bot submits real commands. It never edits sortie state/resources. */\nexport function playSortie(options = {}) {\n  const sim = new BomberSim({seed: 1942, ...options}), seenTypes = new Set(), phases = new Set(), encounters = new Set();\n  let lastObserved = 0, releaseSent = false, evasiveUntil = 0, evasionSide = 1, restoredCourse = false, frame = 0;\n  const beats = [];\n  while (!sim.state.result && sim.state.t < 721 && frame++ < 120 * 723) {\n    const s = sim.state, a = s.aircraft, player = s.players[0];\n    for (const event of s.events) if (event.id > lastObserved) {\n      lastObserved = Math.max(lastObserved, event.id); seenTypes.add(event.type);\n      if (event.type === 'fighter-spawn') encounters.add(event.bearing);\n      if (event.type === 'flak-warning' && !releaseSent && a.x < 302000) { evasiveUntil = s.t + sim.balance.flakWindow + 0.12; evasionSide *= -1; restoredCourse = false; }\n    }\n    if (!phases.has(s.phase)) { phases.add(s.phase); beats.push({phase: s.phase, t: Number(s.t.toFixed(2)), hull: Number(a.hull.toFixed(1))}); }\n    if (a.fire && a.extinguishers) sim.command(1, {type: 'extinguish', actionId: `bottle-${Math.floor(s.t)}`});\n    if (s.primary && s.route.target !== 'home') sim.command(1, {type: 'route', target: 'home'});\n    if (s.phase !== 'landing' && s.t < evasiveUntil && !releaseSent) {\n      if (player.station !== 'pilot') sim.command(1, {type: 'station', station: 'pilot'});\n      sim.command(1, {type: 'controls', bank: evasionSide, pitch: 1, throttleDelta: 1});\n    } else if (!restoredCourse && evasiveUntil && !releaseSent) {\n      sim.command(1, {type: 'controls'});\n      sim.command(1, {type: 'route', target: 'harbor'}); restoredCourse = true;\n    } else if (!s.primary && a.x > 300000 && s.bombsLeft) {\n      if (player.station !== 'bombs') sim.command(1, {type: 'station', station: 'bombs'});\n      const target = s.targets.find(t => t.primary && t.alive);\n      if (target && a.doors > 0.85 && dist(s.prediction, target) < target.r * 0.55 && !releaseSent) {\n        releaseSent = sim.command(1, {type: 'release', salvo: 2, actionId: 'primary-salvo'});\n      }\n    } else if (s.phase !== 'landing') {\n      const enemy = s.enemies.find(e => e.alive && e.phase !== 'disengage');\n      if (enemy) {\n        if (player.station !== enemy.bearing) sim.command(1, {type: 'station', station: enemy.bearing});\n        const lead = dist(enemy, a) / (850 * U), x = enemy.x + (enemy.vx || 0) * lead - a.x, y = enemy.y + (enemy.vy || 0) * lead - a.y;\n        sim.command(1, {type: 'aim', yaw: angle(Math.atan2(y, x) - a.yaw - BEARINGS[enemy.bearing]), pitch: Math.atan2(enemy.z + (enemy.vz || 0) * lead - a.z, Math.hypot(x, y))});\n        sim.command(1, {type: 'controls', fire: true});\n      } else sim.command(1, {type: 'controls'});\n    }\n    sim.step(DT);\n  }\n  phases.add(sim.state.phase);\n  return {sim, seenTypes, phases, encounters, beats, frames: frame, releaseSent};\n}\n\nexport function runSimTests({full = true} = {}) {\n  let count = 0;\n  const failures = [], details = [];\n  let group = '';\n  const check = (condition, name, extra = '') => { count++; if (!condition) failures.push(`${group}: ${name}${extra ? ` (${extra})` : ''}`); };\n  const test = (name, fn) => { group = name; try { fn(); } catch (error) { count++; failures.push(`${name}: unexpected ${error.stack || error}`); } };\n\n  test('geometry and RNG', () => {\n    const east = localVector(0, 1, 2, 3), south = localVector(Math.PI / 2, 1, 0);\n    check(east.x === 1 && east.y === 2 && east.z === 3 && Math.abs(south.y - 1) < 1e-9, 'one z-up forward/right transform');\n    check(segmentHit({x: 0, y: 0, z: 0}, {x: 10000, y: 0, z: 0}, {x: 5000, y: 0, z: 0}, 10), 'fast swept shot hits between endpoints');\n    check(!segmentHit({x: 0, y: 0, z: 0}, {x: 10000, y: 0, z: 0}, {x: 5000, y: 100, z: 0}, 10), 'near swept shot misses');\n    const a = new BomberSim({seed: 413}), b = new BomberSim({seed: 413});\n    advance(a, 5); advance(b, 5); check(JSON.stringify(a.snapshot()) === JSON.stringify(b.snapshot()), 'seeded simulation is deterministic');\n  });\n\n  test('flight and resources', () => {\n    const sim = new BomberSim(); advance(sim, 30);\n    check(sim.state.aircraft.airborne && sim.state.aircraft.z > 1000 && sim.state.phase === 'outbound', 'assisted takeoff and positive climb');\n    const low = airborne(), high = airborne(); low.state.aircraft.throttle = 0.1; high.state.aircraft.throttle = 1;\n    advance(low, 15); advance(high, 15);\n    check(high.state.aircraft.fuel < low.state.aircraft.fuel && high.state.aircraft.speed > low.state.aircraft.speed, 'power trades fuel for speed');\n    const stalled = airborne(), a = stalled.state.aircraft; a.speed = 30 * U; a.throttle = 0.1;\n    let sawStall = false;\n    advance(stalled, 15, s => { s.command(1, {type: 'controls', throttleDelta: 1}); sawStall ||= s.state.aircraft.stall; });\n    check(sawStall && !a.stall && !stalled.state.result, 'stall is warned and recoverable by increasing power');\n    const hold = airborne(); Object.assign(hold.state.aircraft, {yaw: 0.4, holdYaw: 0.4, holdAlt: 900 * U, holdMode: 'course'});\n    hold.command(1, {type: 'station', station: 'nose'}); const before = copy(hold.state.aircraft); advance(hold, 10);\n    check(hold.state.aircraft.hold && Math.abs(angle(hold.state.aircraft.yaw - before.yaw)) < 0.1 && Math.abs(hold.state.aircraft.z - before.z) < 500, 'leaving flight yields stable course hold');\n    hold.command(1, {type: 'station', station: 'pilot'}); hold.command(1, {type: 'controls', bank: 1}); hold.step(DT);\n    check(!hold.state.aircraft.hold, 'direct pilot input cancels hold');\n    const healthy = airborne(), damaged = airborne(); damaged.applySystem('engine'); advance(healthy, 12); advance(damaged, 12);\n    check(damaged.state.aircraft.speed < healthy.state.aircraft.speed && damaged.state.aircraft.fuel < healthy.state.aircraft.fuel, 'damaged engine lowers power and raises burn');\n    const light = new BomberSim({loadout: 'longrange'}), heavy = new BomberSim({loadout: 'heavy'}); advance(light, 30); advance(heavy, 30);\n    check(heavy.state.bombsLeft > light.state.bombsLeft && heavy.state.aircraft.maxFuel < light.state.aircraft.maxFuel && heavy.state.aircraft.speed < light.state.aircraft.speed, 'payload presets have actual weight and fuel tradeoffs');\n  });\n\n  test('ownership and commands', () => {\n    const sim = airborne({players: [1, 2]}), s = sim.state;\n    check(!sim.command(2, {type: 'route', target: 'home'}), 'noncommander cannot commit routes');\n    check(!sim.command(1, {type: 'station', station: 'nose'}), 'occupied station requires handover');\n    check(sim.command(1, {type: 'station', station: 'nose', handover: true}) && sim.owner(2).station === 'pilot', 'explicit handover exchanges seats');\n    check(s.owners.pilot === 2 && s.owners.nose === 1, 'handover maintains unique station owners');\n    check(s.commandOwner === 2 && sim.command(2, {type: 'route', target: 'harbor'}) && !sim.command(1, {type: 'route', target: 'home'}), 'displaced player receiving pilot immediately receives flight command');\n    sim.command(2, {type: 'station', station: 'pilot'});\n    check(s.commandOwner === 2, 'taking pilot transfers command');\n    sim.command(2, {type: 'station', station: 'bombs'});\n    check(s.commandOwner === 2 && sim.command(2, {type: 'route', target: 'harbor'}), 'commander retains route rights while looking at another station');\n    check(sim.command(2, {type: 'controls', seq: 3, fire: true}) && !sim.command(2, {type: 'controls', seq: 3, fire: true}), 'continuous packet sequence deduplicates');\n    sim.depart(2);\n    check(s.owners.bombs === 'AI' && s.commandOwner === 1 && !sim.controls[2], 'departure restores AI, command and cleared held controls');\n    check(!sim.command(2, {type: 'release'}), 'departed sender cannot command');\n    check(!sim.command(1, {type: 'aim', yaw: NaN, pitch: 0}), 'invalid aim rejected');\n    sim.command(1, {type: 'aim', yaw: 200, pitch: -200});\n    check(sim.owner(1).aim.yaw <= 0.83 && sim.owner(1).aim.pitch >= -0.48, 'remote aim clamps to mount arc');\n    const repeated = airborne(); repeated.command(1, {type: 'station', station: 'bombs'}); repeated.command(1, {type: 'aim', yaw: 0.2, pitch: 0.1});\n    const historyLength = repeated.state.history.length;\n    for (let i = 0; i < 100; i++) repeated.command(1, {type: 'station', station: 'bombs'});\n    check(repeated.state.history.length === historyLength && repeated.owner(1).aim.yaw === 0.2, 'same station request preserves aim and cannot flood radio or transition events');\n  });\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
