{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_94","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"cat > docs/issues.md <<'EOF'\n# Closed implementation issue ledger\n\n37 distinct implementation issues were found by automated checks, focused code audits and screenshot review during construction. All listed items were corrected before handoff. Three are classified critical because they prevented startup, removed the central 3D picture, or prevented the promised two-view co-op mode. This count includes incomplete integration discovered by acceptance review; it is not a count of defects remaining in the release.\n\n| # | Issue found | Evidence / correction | Severity |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| 1 | Flak burst volume exceeded available evasive displacement | Simulation geometry audit and evasion regression; narrower real volume, longer warning | Major |\n| 2 | Once-only warning cache survived replay | Reset regression clears warning cache | Major |\n| 3 | Urgent radio interruption left stale chatter queued | Audio lifecycle audit; clear interrupted queue | Minor |\n| 4 | Cockpit instrument centers cropped at viewport edge | Native screenshot review; repositioned gauges | Minor |\n| 5 | Outlined cloud clusters cluttered sky silhouettes | Native screenshot review; unoutlined low-poly native meshes | Minor |\n| 6 | False engine-fire animation at initial state | Native renderer state audit; fire requires truthy fire state | Minor |\n| 7 | Gun camera pitch disagreed with authoritative round direction | Camera/ballistic audit; matching aim convention | Major |\n| 8 | UI selector helper arrow declaration failed parsing | First package build rejected it; corrected declaration | Critical |\n| 9 | Settings Back callback called itself recursively | Native Shell audit; use native back stack | Major |\n| 10 | Map opened from pause was cleared by stale pause stack | Browser/audit; clear paused stack before live navigation | Major |\n| 11 | Ordinary settings exposed developer tuning, including Hub | Native settings audit; filtered preferences and Hub write guard | Major |\n| 12 | Rebuilt HUD could lose pointer clicks before release | Input audit; immediate pointer actions | Major |\n| 13 | Native crew portraits used center as top-left and cropped | Screenshot/API review; correct portrait coordinates | Minor |\n| 14 | Player 2 could not own native menu focus | Pad-stub/browser check; scoped native menu input owner | Major |\n| 15 | Pilot aiming did not update camera look | Shared state audit; update look from authoritative pilot aim | Minor |\n| 16 | Sight damage left the exact fine reference visible | Acceptance audit; coarse quantized sight, no fine boxes | Major |\n| 17 | Voice gain was overwritten by native volume application | Audio/settings audit; use native voiceVolume | Minor |\n| 18 | Free-camera motion existed but was not wired to inputs | Dev tools audit/browser movement regression | Minor |\n| 19 | Touch gunnery had no fire action | Touch action audit; held contextual burst | Major |\n| 20 | Touch had no deliberate payload-jettison path | Emergency screen and held action added | Major |\n| 21 | Player 2 map commits used Player 1 identity | Co-op authority audit; preserve initiating player through previews | Major |\n| 22 | Dogleg risk description had no actual barrage difference | Route acceptance comparison; longer coastal battery interval | Minor |\n| 23 | Occupied-seat exchange did not transfer command to displaced pilot | Simulation/co-op regression; atomic command transfer | Major |\n| 24 | Reclaiming same station reset aim and flooded radio | Attract/state audit; idempotent same-station request | Minor |\n| 25 | Pointer release outside jettison button could leave hold active | Hold cancellation audit; capture pointer, cancel on back/release | Major |\n| 26 | Guest gunfire lacked sound when high-rate events were trimmed | Audio/network audit; monotonic shot-counter fallback, no double sound | Minor |\n| 27 | Debug tools omitted attack paths, collision and encounter gates | Acceptance audit; native path/volume/trigger visualization | Minor |\n| 28 | Native scene entry reset the co-op split after setup | Browser/native lifecycle check; apply split in play enter | Critical |\n| 29 | Navigation hold overwrote deliberate throttle changes | Flight/input audit; manual power overrides automatic setting | Major |\n| 30 | Debrief could precede physical runway touchdown | Full-input recovery review; authored approach ends stopped on runway | Major |\n| 31 | Returning from mission editor lost injected developer toolbar | Browser menu-back regression; rebuild tools after native back | Minor |\n| 32 | Touch menu release clicked new Close button and resumed immediately | Real touch-event trace; consume opening click in capture phase | Major |\n| 33 | Native START duplicated the touch menu control | Phone screenshot; declare custom menu to native touch system | Minor |\n| 34 | Practice selection leaked into a later normal sortie | Public practice/replay audit; clear practice when normal briefing opens | Major |\n| 35 | Native shell fixed button text at 13 px despite TV scale | TV screenshot; inherit game-specific accessible button sizing | Minor |\n| 36 | Cleanup briefly renamed a call argument to an undefined identifier | Targeted source review caught before release; restore call, enable undeclared-variable lint | Critical |\n| 37 | Three import crashed before unsupported-renderer catch in Firefox | Firefox early-error trace; standard GPU IDL constants let native capability check explain failure | Minor |\n\nExcluded from the implementation total: test server relative-path error, running npm in the root rather than dev folder, a driver retaining its own bank command, an input bot that ignored flak, tests pressing during the deliberate 0.22-second transition debounce, ambiguous Back locators, and a linter command flag mistake. These were test/command fixtures and were fixed separately. Software WebGPU device loss and lack of physical hardware/listeners are documented environment limits, not game defects.\nEOF\ncat >> PROGRESS.md <<'EOF'\n\n## Release regression checkpoint\n- Public native-input sortie passes again after physical recovery change: 8/8, success619s,32%fuel,86%hull,4kills,2bombs,16keyboard evasions; actual DOM/keyboard/mouse only and native game.advance.\n- Full simulation now141/141 including all9 physical runway endpoint assertions.\n- Audio now37/37 with guest gun-shot counter fallback; quiet audio wrapper38checks including test bundle build.\n- Own sources formatted with Biome; clean checks with undeclared-variable detection. Tooling CSS overrides intentionally exempt important/specificity style advice. Ruff fixes/format applied to root Python drivers.\n- Touch click-through captured in a real pointer trace; global capture consumes only the opening pointer sequence. Editor Back rebuilds tools. Normal briefing clears stale practice. Held touch fire clears by pointer identity. These changes are in the current artifact.\n- Firefox original failure was a Three module initializer reading absent GPUShaderStage before app boot catch. Build now supplies only standard missing GPU enum constants; navigator.gpu stays absent; app native WebGL capability guard can show useful unsupported screen. No engine source or Hub connect protocol changed.\n- Full browser suite currently running via quiet verifier; all test processes owned and bounded.\n- Closed issue ledger docs/issues.md:37 implementation issues,3critical; excludes test-fixture mistakes and environment/hardware limitations.\nEOF\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
