{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_96","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\nx=json.load(open('tests/browser-result.json'));print(json.dumps({'assertions':x['assertions'],'cases':x['cases'],'failures':x['failures'],'limitations':x['limitations']},indent=2))\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"{\n  \"assertions\": 132,\n  \"cases\": [\n    {\n      \"name\": \"menus/preferences/credits\",\n      \"pass\": true\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"pause/dev/editor/free camera\",\n      \"pass\": true\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"attract/input consumption\",\n      \"pass\": true\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"mixed couch co-op\",\n      \"pass\": true\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"two pads/glyphs\",\n      \"pass\": true\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"touch/multitouch\",\n      \"pass\": true\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"copied artifact portability\",\n      \"pass\": true\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"WebKit native renderer\",\n      \"pass\": true\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"Firefox unsupported renderer\",\n      \"pass\": true\n    }\n  ],\n  \"failures\": [],\n  \"limitations\": [\n    \"Installed Firefox has no usable native WebGL2; useful unsupported-renderer screen verified.\"\n  ]\n}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_97","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\np='content/credits.json';x=json.load(open(p))\ns=x['sourceInformation']\ns['tech']='my-3D2dge 0.89.1 (8ecc2f6) + native World3D; Three.js 0.182.0; Rapier 0.19.3; JavaScript/Web Audio; Bun 1.3.14 single-file bundle'\ns['testing']='Headless deterministic simulation, actual native keyboard/mouse whole sortie, standard-pad stubs, Chromium touch emulation, Chromium/WebKit file-origin rendering, OfflineAudioContext, five AI Hub harness scenarios including latency/loss and playerless server. No physical controller, touch device or listener.'\ns['online']='1–2 local couch co-op (keyboard+pad or two pads); AI Hub Session Protocol v1 shared-world, client 1.4.0. Standalone internet room hosting: none.'\ns['research']='Read preserved Blue Sky Rangers original instructions and developer history; inspected Intv Funhouse source screenshots. Original audio recordings/timbres: unknown; new music, SFX and gibberish are original.'\nx['testingFeedback']=['37 distinct implementation issues were corrected during automated checks, code audits and screenshot review; the closed ledger is docs/issues.md. Test-driver errors and environment limits are excluded.','3 critical startup, core-rendering or two-view co-op blockers were corrected. No known release-blocking issue remains.','The complete public keyboard/mouse sortie, nine loadout/difficulty full sorties and actual multi-client Hub harness were most useful because they exercised coupled systems and cleanup.','An immediate screenshot during the native menu opening animation showed a transient empty panel; a settled screenshot was needed to assess the actual briefing.']\nx['engineFeedback']=['Native World3D pen, shapes, independent cameras and fixed-step E.Game made a coherent procedural aircraft and split views possible.','The split-view camera overlay is skipped by the renderer, and Three imports WebGPU constants before a native WebGL fallback can run; both required explicit integration work.','Coupled bomber flight, resources, station authority, bombing ballistics, damage and complete sortie orchestration.','Portable bundling and first-person geometry across two independent native viewports while preserving input/menu ownership.','No upstream engine source changes. Added game systems, per-viewport native pen foreground, input/Shell adaptations, portable bundling and standard missing GPU constants for import compatibility.','Make per-viewport first-person overlays and their camera frame a documented public rendering path.']\nx['promptFeedback']=['The complete sortie loop and exact handoff schema gave the build a clear destination.','The source jettisons fuel while PLAN deliberately specifies payload jettison; this adaptation follows PLAN.','Preserving one authoritative aircraft and station/input ownership across solo, couch co-op, file origin and AI Hub.','Separate acceptance gates from optional polish and specify one expected evidence format.']\nopen(p,'w').write(json.dumps(x,indent=2,ensure_ascii=False)+'\\\\n')\nPY\nbiome format --write content/credits.json biome.json\nrg -n 'writeFileSync|sourceInformation' tools/build.mjs\nsed -n '52,92p' tools/build.mjs\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
